it, that's 9,170? Wait, 131 \u00d7 7 is 917, so adding two zeros gives 91,700.\n\nNow add them all up:\n\n262 (from 2)\n+5,240 (from 40)\n+91,700 (from 700)\n= 262 + 5,240 = 5,502; then 5,502 + 91,700 = 97,202.\n\nOkay, so that's the same result as before. So that's good. So the product is 97,202.\n\nBut just to be thorough, maybe I can check using another method. Let's try using the distributive property again but in a different way.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 742 \u00d7 131 can be thought of as 742 \u00d7 (100 + 30 + 1), which is the same as before. But maybe I can check the multiplication by breaking down 742 into 700 + 40 + 2.\n\nSo, 742 = 700 + 40 + 2. Therefore:\n\n131 \u00d7 742 = 131 \u00d7 700 + 131 \u00d7 40 + 131 \u00d7 2\n\nCompute each term:\n\n131 \u00d7 700: 131 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 100. 131 \u00d7 7: 917. So 917 \u00d7 100 = 91,700.\n\n131 \u00d7 40: 131 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 10. 131 \u00d7 4 = 524. So 524 \u00d7 10 = 5,240.\n\n131 \u00d7 2 = 262.\n\nAdding them up: 91,700 + 5,240 + 262.\n\n91,700 + 5,240: Let's do 91,700 + 5,000 = 96,700. Then +240 = 96,940.\n\nThen 96,940 + 262: 96,940 + 200 = 97,140. Then +62 = 97,202.\n\nSame result again. So that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication step-by-step:\n\nMultiply 131 by 742.\n\nFirst, multiply 131 by 2: 262.\n\nThen multiply 131 by 40 (which is 4 in the tens place): 131 \u00d7 4 = 524, then add a zero: 5,240.\n\nThen multiply 131 by 700 (which is 7 in the hundreds place): 131 \u00d7 7 = 917, then add two zeros: 91,700.\n\nNow add 262 + 5,240 + 91,700.\n\n262 + 5,240: 5,240 + 200 = 5,440; 5,440 + 62 = 5,502.\n\nThen 5,502 + 91,700: 91,700 + 5,000 = 96,700; 96,700 + 502 = 97,202.\n\nSame answer. So seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, perhaps another check.\n\nAlternatively, use the difference of squares or other algebraic identities, but that might be more complicated. Alternatively, check if 131 \u00d7 742 is close to 130 \u00d7 742 + 1 \u00d7 742.\n\n130 \u00d7 742: 13 \u00d7 742 \u00d7 10. 13 \u00d7 742. Let's compute 10 \u00d7 742 = 7,420; 3 \u00d7 742 = 2,226. So 7,420 + 2,226 = 9,646. Then \u00d710 = 96,460. Then add 1 \u00d7742 = 742. So 96,460 + 742 = 97,202. Same result.\n\nSo all methods lead to 97,202. Therefore, I think that's the correct answer.\n\nBut just to be absolutely sure, maybe do the multiplication step-by-step manually.\n\nLet's write it out:\n\n      131\n    \u00d7 742\n    --------\n\nFirst, multiply 131 by 2 (units place):\n\n131 \u00d7 2 = 262. Write down 262.\n\nNext, multiply 131 by 4 (tens place), but since it's the tens place, we add a zero:\n\n131 \u00d7 4 = 524. Add a zero: 5,240. Write down 5,240.\n\nNext, multiply 131 by 7 (hundreds place), add two zeros:\n\n131 \u00d7 7 = 917. Add two zeros: 91,700. Write down 91,700.\n\nNow add the three results:\n\n262\n\n+5,240\n\n+91,700\n\nLet's add 262 + 5,240 first. 262 + 5,000 = 5,262. Then +240 = 5,502.\n\nThen add 5,502 + 91,700. 5,502 + 90,000 = 95,502. Then +1,700 = 97,202.\n\nYep, same answer. So I think that's solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check using another decomposition. For example, 131 is 130 + 1. So:\n\n130 \u00d7 742 + 1 \u00d7 742.\n\n130 \u00d7 742: 100 \u00d7 742 = 74,200; 30 \u00d7 742 = 22,260. So 74,200 + 22,260 = 96,460.\n\nThen 1 \u00d7 742 = 742. So 96,460 + 742 = 97,202. Same result.\n\nAlright, so all methods converge to 97,202. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 131 and 742 is 97,202.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 131 and 742 is \\boxed{97202}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 131 and 742, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 131 into 100 + 30 + 1.\n2. Multiply each part by 742 and sum the results:\n   - \\(100 \\times 742 = 74200\\)\n   - \\(30 \\times 742 = 22260\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 742 = 742\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n74200 + 22260 + 742\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 74200 and 22260:\n\\[\n74200 + 22260 = 96460\n\\]\n\nThen add 742 to the result:\n\\[\n96460 + 742 = 97202\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 131 by 2: \\(131 \\times 2 = 262\\)\n- Multiply 131 by 40 (tens place): \\(131 \\times 4 = 524\\), add a zero: \\(5240\\)\n- Multiply 131 by 700 (hundreds place): \\(131 \\times 7 = 917\\), add two zeros: \\(91700\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n262 + 5240 + 91700 = 97202\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 131 and 742 is \\(\\boxed{97202}\\).",
