----\nStart adding from the right:\n\n777 + 611 = 1388 (as before)\n1388 + 611. Let's add 1388 + 600 = 1988, then 1988 + 11 = 2000. Hmm, that seems correct. But let me verify using another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let's see:\n\n117 can be broken down into 100 + 10 + 7. So, 611 \u00d7 117 = 611 \u00d7 (100 + 10 + 7) = 611\u00d7100 + 611\u00d710 + 611\u00d77.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n611\u00d7100 = 61,100\n\n611\u00d710 = 6,110\n\n611\u00d77 = 4,277\n\nNow, add them all together:\n\n61,100 + 6,110 = 67,210\n\n67,210 + 4,277. Let's compute that:\n\n67,210 + 4,000 = 71,210\n\n71,210 + 277 = 71,487\n\nWait, so according to this method, the product is 71,487. But when I did the standard multiplication, I got 2,000. That's a big discrepancy. Which one is correct?\n\nHmm, clearly, there's a mistake in one of the methods. Let me check the standard multiplication again.\n\nOriginal multiplication setup:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0611\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0117\n--------\n\nFirst partial product: 611 \u00d7 7 = 777 (units place)\nSecond partial product: 611 \u00d7 1 = 611 (tens place)\nThird partial product: 611 \u00d7 1 = 611 (hundreds place)\n\nAdding them:\n\n777 (units)\n611 (tens)\n611 (hundreds)\n--------\nLet me write them vertically properly:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0777\n\u00a0\u00a0611\n\u00a0\u00a0611\n-------\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n777 + 611 = 1388 (as before)\n1388 + 611. Let's do this addition again:\n\n1388 + 611:\n\n1388 + 600 = 1988\n\n1988 + 11 = 2000\n\nBut according to the distributive method, the answer is 71,487. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check 611 \u00d7 7 again.\n\n611 \u00d7 7:\n\n7 \u00d7 1 = 7\n\n7 \u00d7 10 = 70\n\n7 \u00d7 100 = 700\n\nSo 700 + 70 + 7 = 777. That's correct.\n\n611 \u00d7 1 = 611. Correct.\n\n611 \u00d7 1 = 611. Correct.\n\nSo adding 777 + 611 + 611:\n\n777 + 611 = 1388\n\n1388 + 611 = 2000. Wait,