to an incorrect total. After correcting that, both methods give the same result.\n\nTherefore, the product of 611 and 117 is 71,487.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 611 and 117 is \\boxed{71487}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 611 and 117, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 117 into 100, 10, and 7.\n2. Multiply 611 by each part:\n   - \\(611 \\times 100 = 61100\\)\n   - \\(611 \\times 10 = 6110\\)\n   - \\(611 \\times 7 = 4277\\)\n3. Add the results together:\n   - \\(61100 + 6110 = 67210\\)\n   - \\(67210 + 4277 = 71487\\)\n\nThus, the product of 611 and 117 is \\(\\boxed{71487}\\).",
