stent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the multiplication of two numbers by expanding each digit step by step.\n\nLet me write it out as if I'm doing the multiplication manually:\n\n      424\n    x 715\n    -------\n\nFirst, multiply 424 by 5:\n\n424\nx  5\n------\n2120\n\nThen, multiply 424 by 1 (tens place, which is 10):\n\n424\nx 10\n------\n4240\n\nThen, multiply 424 by 7 (hundreds place, which is 700):\n\n424\nx 700\n------\n296800\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n2120\n4240\n296800\n--------\n303160\n\nYes, same result. So, after multiple checks, I can be confident that the product is 303,160.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator if I have access. But since I don't, I need to rely on manual calculations. But all methods lead to the same answer, so I think it's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 424 and 715 is 303,160.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 424 and 715 is \\boxed{303160}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 424 and 715, we can break down the multiplication into parts and then add the results together. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Multiply 424 by the units digit (5) of 715:\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 5 = 2120\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 424 by the tens digit (1) of 715, shifting the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 10 = 4240\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 424 by the hundreds digit (7) of 715, shifting the result two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 700 = 296800\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the three results together:\n   \\[\n   2120 + 4240 + 296800 = 303160\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 424 and 715 is \\(\\boxed{303160}\\).",
