So when adding, you have to align them as:\n\n      2956\n     17120\n    209000\n    --------\n\nBut when adding, the digits are:\n\n- The units place: 6 (from 2956) + 0 (from 17120) + 0 (from 209000) = 6\n\n- The tens place: 5 (from 2956) + 2 (from 17120) + 0 (from 209000) = 7\n\n- The hundreds place: 9 (from 2956) + 1 (from 17120) + 0 (from 209000) = 10. So write 0, carry 1.\n\n- The thousands place: 2 (from 2956) + 7 (from 17120) + 0 (from 209000) + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n- The ten thousands place: 1 (from 2956) + 0 (from 17120) + 0 (from 209000) + 1 (carry) = 2.\n\n- The hundred thousands place: 0 (from 2956) + 1 (from 17120) + 0 (from 209000) + 1 (carry) = 2.\n\nWait, no. Wait, when adding, the partial products are:\n\nFirst partial product: 2956 (digits: 2, 9, 5, 6)\n\nSecond partial product: 17120 (digits: 1, 7, 1, 2, 0)\n\nThird partial product: 209000 (digits: 2, 0, 9, 0, 0, 0)\n\nBut when adding, we need to align them by their least significant digit. So:\n\n      2956\n     17120\n    209000\n    --------\n\nSo:\n\n- Units place: 6 + 0 + 0 = 6\n\n- Tens place: 5 + 2 + 0 = 7\n\n- Hundreds place: 9 + 1 + 0 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n- Thousands place: 2 + 7 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n- Ten thousands place: 1 + 0 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 2.\n\n- Hundred thousands place: 0 + 1 (carry) = 1.\n\nSo the total is 120,706. But that contradicts the direct calculation. So clearly, there's a mistake here. Wait, but how?\n\nWait, maybe the alignment is wrong. Wait, when you shift the partial products, the first partial product (2956) is shifted left by 0 digits, so it's 2956. The second partial product (17120) is shifted left by 1 digit, so it's 17120. The third partial product (209000) is shifted left by 2 digits, so it's 209000. So when adding, they should be:\n\n      2956\n     17120\n    209000\n    --------\n\nBut when adding, the digits are:\n\n- Units: 6 + 0 + 0 = 6\n\n- Tens: 5 + 2 + 0 = 7\n\n- Hundreds: 9 + 1 + 0 = 10 (0 with carry 1)\