output:  ['\n\nTo find the product of 348 and 861, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 348 by 1 (units place):\n   \\[\n   348 \\times 1 = 348\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 348 by 6 (tens place):\n   \\[\n   348 \\times 6 = 2088\n   \\]\n   Shifted one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   208800\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 348 by 8 (hundreds place):\n   \\[\n   348 \\times 8 = 2784\n   \\]\n   Shifted two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   2784000\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results together:\n   \\[\n   348 + 208800 + 2784000\n   \\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n- First, add 348 and 208800:\n  \\[\n  348 + 208800 = 209148\n  \\]\n- Then, add the result to 2784000:\n  \\[\n  209148 + 2784000 = 299628\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 348 and 861 is \\(\\boxed{299628}\\).', '\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 348 and 861. Hmm, let\'s see. I remember that multiplying two three-digit numbers can be a bit tricky, but maybe there\'s a way to break it down step by step. Let me start by recalling the standard multiplication algorithm. \n\nFirst, I\'ll write 348 multiplied by 861. Let me set it up like this:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0348\n×\xa0\xa0861\n--------\n\nStarting with the rightmost digit of the second number, which is 1. I need to multiply 348 by 1 and then shift it one position to the left because it\'s the units place. That gives me 348.\n\nNext, the middle digit is 6. I need to multiply 348 by 6 and shift it two positions to the left. Let me calculate that: 348 × 6. Breaking it down, 300 × 6 = 1800, 40 × 6 = 240, and 8 × 6 = 48. Adding those together: 1800 + 240 = 2040, then 2040 + 48 = 2088. So, that\'s 2088, shifted two places left, which would be 208800.\n\nThen, the leftmost digit is 8. Multiply 348 by 8 and shift it three positions to the left. Calculating 348 × 8: 300 × 8 = 2400, 40 × 8 = 320, 8 × 8 = 64. Adding those: 2400 + 320 = 2720, then 2720 + 64 = 2784. Shift that three places left, which is 2784000.\n\nNow, I need to add all those results together: 348 + 208800 + 2784000. Let me add them step by step. First, add 348 and 208800. \n\n348 + 208800. Let\'s see, 208800 + 300 = 209100, then +48 = 209148. Then add 2784000 to that. \n\n209148 + 2784000. Hmm, 209148 + 2000000 = 2209148, then +784000 = 2209148 + 784000. Let\'s break that down: 2209148 + 700000 = 2909148, then +84000 = 2909148 + 84000 = 2993148. \n\nWait, let me check that again. Maybe I made a mistake in the addition. Let\'s do it more carefully.\n\nFirst step: 348 + 208800. Let\'s write it as:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0348\n+208800\n--------\n209148\n\nYes, that\'s correct. Then adding 2784000 to 209148. Let\'s align them properly:\n\n\u202f\xa0209148\n+2784000\n----------\n2993148\n\nYes, that seems right. So the total is 2,993,148. \n\nBut wait, let me verify using another method to make sure I didn\'t make a mistake. Maybe using the distributive property. \n\n348 × 861 can be broken down into (300 + 40 + 8) × (800 + 60 + 1). Let\'s compute each part:\n\nFirst, 300 × 800 = 240,000\n\n300 × 60 = 18,000\n\n300 × 1 = 300\n\n40 × 800 = 32,000\n\n40 × 60 = 2,400\n\n40 × 1 = 40\n\n8 × 800 = 6,400\n\n8 × 60 = 480\n\n8 × 1 = 8\n\nNow, add all these together:\n\n240,000 + 18,000 + 300 + 32,000 + 2,400 + 40 + 6,400 + 480 + 8\n\nLet\'s add them step by step:\n\nStart with 240,000 + 18,000 = 258,000\n\n258,000 + 300 = 258,300\n\n258,300 + 32,000 = 290,300\n\n290,300 + 2,400 = 292,700\n\n292,700 + 40 = 292,740\n\n292,740 + 6,400 = 299,140\n\n299,140 + 480 = 299,620\n\n299,620 + 8 = 299,628\n\nWait, that\'s 299,628. But earlier, I got 2,993,148. There\'s a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nHmm, so using the standard multiplication method, I got 2,993,148, but breaking it down into the distributive property gave me 299,628. That\'s way off. So clearly, I made a mistake in one of the methods. Let me check the second method again.\n\nWait, when I broke down 348 into 300 + 40 + 8 and 861 into 800 + 60 + 1, then multiplied each component. Let me verify each multiplication