 hundreds place, we need to multiply by 600. So, 313 × 6 = 1,878, and then add two zeros to make it 187,800.\n\nNow, add all those three results together: 1,252 + 24,960 + 187,800. Let me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 1,252 and 24,960. Let's see:\n\n1,252 + 24,960. Let's break it down:\n\n1,252 + 24,000 = 25,252\n\nThen, 25,252 + 960 = 26,212\n\nSo, 1,252 + 24,960 = 26,212\n\nNow, add that to 187,800:\n\n26,212 + 187,800. Let's break it down:\n\n26,212 + 180,000 = 206,212\n\nThen, 206,212 + 7,800 = 214,012\n\nSo, adding all three parts together gives 214,012.\n\nWait, let me verify that again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Let's do the multiplication another way to cross-check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let's break down 684 into 600 + 80 + 4. Then multiply each part by 313 and add them up.\n\nFirst, 313 × 600. That's 313 × 6 × 100. 313 × 6 is 1,878, so 1,878 × 100 = 187,800. That's the same as before.\n\nNext, 313 × 80. That's 313 × 8 × 10. 313 × 8 is 2,496, so 2,496 × 10 = 24,960. Also the same as before.\n\nThen, 313 × 4 = 1,252. So adding those three results: 187,800 + 24,960 + 1,252. Which again gives 214,012. Okay, that matches. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method. Let's try multiplying 313 by 684 using the standard algorithm step by step again.\n\nMultiplying 313 by 684:\n\nStart with the units digit: 4\n\n313\n×\xa0\xa04\n------\n1,252\n\nThen the tens digit: 8\n\n313\n×\xa0\xa08\n------\n2,496\nShift one position left:\n24,960\n\nThen the hundreds digit: 6\n\n313\n×\xa0\xa06\n------\n1,878\nShift two positions left:\n187,800\n\nNow add them up:\n\n1,252\n+24,960\n------\n26,212\n\n26,212\n+187,800\n------\n214,012\n\nYes, same result. So that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator here, I need to rely on my manual calculations. Let me try another way. Maybe breaking down 313 into 300 + 13.\n\nSo, 313 = 3