ted one position left)\n+536400\u00a0\u00a0(596 \u00d7 9, shifted two positions left)\n-------\n\u00a0\u00a0555472\n\nYes, that's the same result. So, the correct product is 555,472. Therefore, my first calculation was incorrect due to a miscalculation in shifting the digits. The second method using distributive property also gave the same result, so that's reassuring.\n\nTherefore, the product of 596 and 932 is 555,472.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 596 and 932 is \\boxed{555472}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 596 and 932, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 596 by the units digit (2) of 932:\n   \\[\n   596 \\times 2 = 1192\n   \\]\n   This result is shifted one place to the left (due to the tens place in 932).\n\n2. Multiply 596 by the tens digit (3) of 932:\n   \\[\n   596 \\times 3 = 1788\n   \\]\n   This result is shifted one place to the left (due to the hundreds place in 932).\n\n3. Multiply 596 by the hundreds digit (9) of 932:\n   \\[\n   596 \\times 9 = 5364\n   \\]\n   This result is shifted two places to the left (due to the thousands place in 932).\n\n4. Add the shifted results together:\n   \\[\n   1192 + 17880 + 536400\n   \\]\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:\n- First, add 1192 and 17880:\n  \\[\n  1192 + 17880 = 19072\n  \\]\n- Then, add the result to 536400:\n  \\[\n  19072 + 536400 = 555472\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 596 and 932 is \\(\\boxed{555472}\\).",
