at:\n\n479\n+2874\n------\nLet's add the units: 9 + 4 = 13, carry over 1.\nTens: 7 + 7 = 14, plus the carried 1 is 15, carry over 1.\nHundreds: 4 + 8 = 12, plus the carried 1 is 13, carry over 1.\nThousands: 0 + 2 = 2, plus the carried 1 is 3.\n\nSo that gives 3353. Wait, is that right? Let me check again.\n\nWait, 479 + 2874. Let's break it down:\n\n479 + 2000 = 2479\n\n2479 + 800 = 3279\n\n3279 + 70 = 3349\n\n3349 + 4 = 3353. Yes, that's correct. So the total product is 3353.\n\nBut let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property. \n\nI can write 601 as 600 + 1. So, 479 \u00d7 601 = 479 \u00d7 (600 + 1) = 479 \u00d7 600 + 479 \u00d7 1.\n\nCalculating 479 \u00d7 600. Well, 479 \u00d7 6 = 2874, so 479 \u00d7 600 = 2874 \u00d7 10 = 28740.\n\nThen, 479 \u00d7 1 is 479. Adding those together: 28740 + 479.\n\nLet's compute that. 28740 + 400 = 29140, then +79 = 29219. Wait, that's different from the previous result of 3353. Hmm, that can't be. There must be a mistake here.\n\nWait, hold on. If I use the distributive property, 479 \u00d7 601 = 479 \u00d7 (600 + 1) = 479\u00d7600 + 479\u00d71. So 479\u00d7600 is 28740, and 479\u00d71 is 479. So 28740 + 479. Let's compute that again.\n\n28740 + 479:\n\nStart with the thousands: 20000 + 0 = 20000\n\nThen 8000 + 400 = 8400\n\n700 + 70 = 770\n\n40 + 9 = 49\n\nWait, maybe breaking it down:\n\n28740 + 479\n\n= 28740 + 400 + 70 + 9\n\n= (28740 + 400) + (70 + 9)\n\n= 29140 + 79\n\n= 29219\n\nBut earlier, when I did the standard multiplication, I got 3353. These two results are different. That means I made a mistake somewhere. Let me check both methods again.\n\nFirst method (standard multiplication):\n\n479 \u00d7 601\n\nBreakdown:\n\nMultiply 479 by 1: 479\n\nMultiply 479 by 0: 0\n\nMultiply 479 by 6: 2874\n\nThen add them:\n\n479\n\n+0\n\n+2874\n\n= 3353\n\nBut when I use distributive property, I get 29219. These can't both be correct. So where is the error?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up t