So first, 487 × 7. Let's do that. 400 × 7 = 2800, 80 × 7 = 560, 7 × 7 = 49. Adding those: 2800 + 560 = 3360, then 3360 + 49 = 3409. So, 487 × 7 = 3409. Then, multiply by 10 to get 70: 3409 × 10 = 34090. So, 487 × 70 = 34090. That seems right.\n\nNow, the hundreds place part: 487 × 100. That's straightforward. Multiplying by 100 adds two zeros at the end. So, 487 × 100 = 48700. Let me check that: 487 × 10 = 4870, so ×100 is 48700. Yep, that's correct.\n\nNow, I need to add all three results together: 3896 (from the units place) + 34090 (from the tens place) + 48700 (from the hundreds place). Let's do this step by step.\n\nFirst, add 3896 and 34090. Let's break it down:\n\n3896 + 34090. Let's add 3896 + 34000 first, which is 3896 + 34000 = 37896. Then add the remaining 90: 37896 + 90 = 37986. So, 3896 + 34090 = 37986.\n\nNext, add 48700 to that result. So, 37986 + 48700. Let's break it down:\n\n37986 + 40000 = 77986  \n77986 + 8700 = 77986 + 8000 = 85986; 85986 + 700 = 86686  \nSo, 37986 + 48700 = 86686.\n\nWait, let me verify that addition again to be sure. Alternatively, 37986 + 48700. Let's add the thousands: 30000 + 40000 = 70000  \nThen the hundreds: 7000 + 8000 = 15000  \nTens: 900 + 700 = 1600  \nOnes: 80 + 0 = 80  \nWait, maybe that's not the right way. Let me think.\n\nAlternatively, 37986 + 48700. Let's add 37986 + 40000 = 77986. Then add 8700: 77986 + 8700. 77986 + 8000 = 85986, then +700 = 86686. Yes, that's correct. So total is 86686.\n\nTherefore, the product of 487 and 178 is 86,686. Let me check if that makes sense. Let me verify using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step. Let's try that.\n\nMultiplying 487 by 178:\n\nFirst, write 487 × 178. Let's do it vertically.\n\nBut since I can't actually write it out here, I'll describe the steps.\n\nMultiply 487 by 8 (units place):\n\n487  \n×   8  \n------  \n3896 (since 487 × 8 = 3896)\n\nThen, multiply 487 by 70 (tens place). Since 70 is 7 × 10, we take the result from the first step (3896) and shift it one position to the left (multiply by 10), so 3896 × 10 = 38960. But wait, actually, in the standard multiplication, when you multiply by the tens digit, you have to shift left by one place. Wait, maybe I confused the steps.\n\nWait, no. Let me recall. When you multiply by the tens digit (70), you take the original number (487) and multiply by 7 (the tens digit), then shift the result one place to the left (because it's the tens place). So, 487 × 7 = 3409, then shift left by one: 34090. Similarly, multiplying by the hundreds digit (100) would be 487 × 1 = 487, shift left by two places: 48700.\n\nTherefore, adding 3896 + 34090 + 48700 = 86686. So that's the same result as before. So that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator. But since I don't have a calculator here, let me try another way. Let's use the distributive property.\n\n178 can be written as 100 + 70 + 8. So, 487 × 178 = 487 × (100 + 70 + 8) = 487×100 + 487×70 + 487×8. Which is exactly what I did before. So, 487×100=48700, 487×70=34090, 487×8=3896. Adding them gives 48700 + 34090 = 82790, then 82790 + 3896 = 86686. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another multiplication method. Let's try adding the numbers step by step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 487 × 178 = 487 × (180 - 2). Let's see:\n\n487 × 180 - 487 × 2.\n\nFirst, compute 487 × 180. Let's break that down:\n\n487 × 100 = 48700  \n487 × 80 = 38960  \nSo, 48700 + 38960 = 87660. Then subtract 487 × 2 = 974. So, 87660 - 974 = 86686. Same result. Wow, that's a good check.\n\nSo, 487 × 178 = 86686. Therefore, the answer should be 86,686. Let me just verify once more with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\nMultiply 487 by 178:\n\nFirst, multiply 487 by 8:\n\n487  \n×   8  \n------  \n3896  \n\nThen, multiply 487 by 70 (shift one position left):\n\n487  \n×  70  \n------  \n34090  \n\nThen, multiply 487 by 100 (shift two positions left):\n\n487  \n× 100  \n------  \n48700  \n\nNow, add them up:\n\n3896  \n+34090  \n+48700  \n--------  \n3896 + 34090 = 37986  \n37986 + 48700 = 86686  \n\nYes, same result. So, all methods lead to 86,686. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 487 and 178 is 86,686.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 487 and 178 is \\boxed{86686}.\n"] 10%|▉         | 49/500 [50:21<7:54:24, 63.11s/it] 
