32 = 200652\n\nWait, that's different. Wait, so now I get 200652, but before I got 62652. That's a problem. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, in the first method, I broke down 727 into 700 + 20 + 7, which is correct. Then 276*700 is 193200, 276*20 is 5520, 276*7 is 1932. Then adding those gives 193200 + 5520 + 1932.\n\nBut in the second method, I broke down 727 into 700 + 20 + 7 as well, but maybe I miscalculated the multiplication.\n\nWait, let's check 276*700 again. 276*7 is 1932, so 1932*100 is 193200. That's correct.\n\n276*20: 276*2=552, 552*10=5520. Correct.\n\n276*7: 1932. Correct.\n\nSo adding 193200 + 5520 + 1932.\n\nLet me compute 193200 + 5520 first.\n\n193200 + 5520:\n\n193200 + 5000 = 198200\n\n198200 + 520 = 198720\n\nThen add 1932: 198720 + 1932\n\n198720 + 1000 = 199720\n\n199720 + 932 = 200,652\n\nWait, 199720 + 932:\n\n199720 + 900 = 199,620\n\n199,620 + 32 = 199,652\n\nWait, so 199720 + 1932 = 199,652\n\nBut that contradicts the previous total of 62,652. So clearly, there's a mistake here. Wait, but how?\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, in the first method, I had 1932 + 5520 + 55200 = 62,652. But in the second method, I have 193200 + 5520 + 1932 = 200,652. These are two different results. That can't be. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the first method. Let me check the first method again.\n\nFirst method:\n\n276 * 727 = 276*(700 + 20 + 7) = 276*700 + 276*20 + 276*7\n\n276*700 = 193,200\n\n276*20 = 5,520\n\n276*7 = 1,932\n\nAdding them together: 193,200 + 5,520 = 198,720; 198,720 + 1,932 = 200,652\n\nWait, so in the first method, I added 1932 + 5520 + 55200, but that's incorrect. Wait, no. Wait, in the first method, I had:\n\nFirst, multiply 276 by 7: 1932\n\nThen multiply 276 by 20: 5520\n\nThen multiply 276 by 7: 1932\n\nWait, but 727 is 7*100 + 2*10 + 7*1, so the three terms are 700, 20, and 7. Therefore, the three products are 276*700, 276*20, and 276*7. So adding those three products gives the total. So 193,200