me factors and then multiply them. Although that might take longer, but let's see.\n\nFirst, factor 239. Hmm, 239 is a prime number? Let me check. Let's see if it's divisible by any primes up to its square root. The square root of 239 is approximately 15.45. So primes up to 15: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13.\n\n239 divided by 2 is 119.5, not integer. 239 divided by 3 is 79.666..., not integer. 5? 239/5 = 47.8, nope. 7? 239/7 \u2248 34.14, nope. 11? 239/11 \u2248 21.72, nope. 13? 239/13 \u2248 18.38, nope. So 239 is prime.\n\nNow factor 176. 176 divided by 2 is 88. 88 divided by 2 is 44. 44 divided by 2 is 22. 22 divided by 2 is 11. So 176 = 2^4 x 11.\n\nSo the product is 239 x 2^4 x 11. Let's compute that. 2^4 is 16. So 16 x 11 = 176. Then 239 x 176 = 239 x 176. Wait, that's circular. Maybe another way.\n\nAlternatively, 239 x 176 = 239 x (180 - 4) = 239 x 180 - 239 x 4.\n\nCompute 239 x 180 first. 239 x 100 = 23,900. 239 x 80 = 19,120. So 23,900 + 19,120 = 43,020.\n\nThen subtract 239 x 4. 239 x 4 = 956.\n\nSo 43,020 - 956 = 42,064. Wait, that's different from the previous result. Hmm, so now I have two different answers: 52,274 and 42,064. That means I must have made a mistake somewhere.\n\nWait, let's check the second method again. 239 x 176 = 239 x (180 - 4) = 239 x 180 - 239 x 4.\n\n239 x 180: Let's compute that again. 239 x 100 = 23,900. 239 x 80: 239 x 8 = 1,912. Then 1,912 x 10 = 19,120. So 23,900 + 19,120 = 43,020. That's correct.\n\n239 x 4: 200 x 4 = 800, 39 x 4 = 156. So 800 + 156 = 956. Correct.\n\nThen 43,020 - 956: Let's subtract. 43,020 - 900 = 42,120. Then subtract 56 more: 42,120 - 56 = 42,064. So that's 42,064.\n\nBut earlier, using the standard multiplication, I got 52,274. These two results are conflicting. So there must be an error in one of the methods.\n\nLet me check the standard multiplication again step by step.\n\nMultiplying 239 by 176:\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n      239\n    x 176\n    --------\n\nStart with the rightmost digit of 176, which is 6