uct of 239 and 176 is \\boxed{42064}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 239 and 176, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 239 by the rightmost digit (6):\n   \\[\n   239 \\times 6 = 1434\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 239 by the next digit (7), shifting one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   239 \\times 7 = 1673 \\quad \\text{Shifted left by one:} \\quad 16730\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 239 by the next digit (1), shifting two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   239 \\times 1 = 239 \\quad \\text{Shifted left by two:} \\quad 23900\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   1434 + 16730 + 23900\n   \\]\n\n5. Break down the addition step-by-step:\n   - First, add 1434 and 16730:\n     \\[\n     1434 + 16730 = 18164\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to 23900:\n     \\[\n     18164 + 23900 = 42064\n     \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Express 176 as 170 + 6:\n  \\[\n  239 \\times 176 = 239 \\times (170 + 6) = 239 \\times 170 + 239 \\times 6\n  \\]\n- Calculate each part:\n  \\[\n  239 \\times 170 = 40630 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 239 \\times 6 = 1434\n  \\]\n- Add the results:\n  \\[\n  40630 + 1434 = 42064\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 239 and 176 is \\(\\boxed{42064}\\).",
