 place)\n\nThen, you shift each partial product according to their place value:\n\n- 2012 (ones place) stays as is.\n- 1509 (tens place) is shifted one place left, becoming 15090.\n- 4024 (hundreds place) is shifted two places left, becoming 402400.\n\nThen, you add all three partial products:\n\n2012\n+15090\n+402400\n--------\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 2012 and 15090:\n\n2012 + 15090 = 17,102\n\nThen, add 402,400 to 17,102:\n\n17,102 + 402,400 = 4,195,102\n\nSo the total is 4,195,102. But earlier, when I did the alternative method, I got 419,502. So why the discrepancy?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the alternative method. Let me check again.\n\nAlternative method:\n\nBreak down 834 into 800 + 30 + 4.\n\nCompute 503 \u00d7 800 = 402,400\n\nCompute 503 \u00d7 30 = 15,090\n\nCompute 503 \u00d7 4 = 2,012\n\nNow, add them together:\n\n402,400 + 15,090 = 417,490\n\n417,490 + 2,012 = 419,502\n\nWait, so here, adding 402,400 + 15,090 + 2,012 gives 419,502. But according to the standard multiplication algorithm, it's 4,195,102. So which is correct?\n\nWait, this is a problem. There's a conflict here. Let me check with actual multiplication.\n\nLet me compute 503 \u00d7 834 using another method, perhaps using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, note that 834 = 800 + 30 + 4. So:\n\n503 \u00d7 834 = 503 \u00d7 (800 + 30 + 4) = 503\u00d7800 + 503\u00d730 + 503\u00d74\n\nCompute each term:\n\n503 \u00d7 800:\n\n503 \u00d7 8 = 4,024\n\nThen, since it's 800, which is 8 \u00d7 100, shift two places left: 4,024 \u00d7 100 = 402,400\n\n503 \u00d7 30:\n\n503 \u00d7 3 = 1,509\n\nShift one place left: 1,509 \u00d7 10 = 15,090\n\n503 \u00d7 4 = 2,012\n\nNow, add them together:\n\n402,400 + 15,090 = 417,490\n\n417,490 + 2,012 = 419,502\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication algorithm, it's 4,195,102. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 503 \u00d7 834 directly using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nLet me write