71 = 351,351. But when I did the standard multiplication, I got 12,285. That's a huge difference. So, clearly, I made a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let me check the standard multiplication again. Let's do it step by step.\n\nMultiplying 819 by 429:\n\nFirst, write 819 \u00d7 429.\n\nStart with the units digit: 9.\n\n819 \u00d7 9 = 7371. Write that down, shifted one position left: 73710.\n\nNext, the tens digit: 2.\n\n819 \u00d7 2 = 1638. Shifted two positions left: 163800.\n\nNext, the hundreds digit: 4.\n\n819 \u00d7 4 = 3276. Shifted three positions left: 3276000.\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, no. Wait, when you shift left, each subsequent partial product is shifted left by one more position. So, the first partial product (units place) is 7371, which is three digits. Then the next (tens place) is 1638, which is also three digits. Then the hundreds place is 3276, which is three digits. But when adding them, we need to align them by their least significant digit.\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the alignment. Let me write them properly:\n\nFirst partial product: 7371 (units place)\n\nSecond partial product: 16380 (tens place, shifted left by one, so 16380)\n\nThird partial product: 327600 (hundreds place, shifted left by two, so 327600)\n\nWait, but 819 \u00d7 429 is 819 \u00d7 (400 + 20 + 9) = 327600 + 16380 + 7371. But when adding 327600 + 16380 + 7371, we get 351,351. But when I did the standard multiplication, I got 12,285. That's a problem. So, clearly, there's a mistake here.\n\nWait, but 819 \u00d7 429. Let me compute it directly. Let's do it the standard way again.\n\nMultiply 819 by 429:\n\nFirst, write 819 \u00d7 429.\n\nStart with the rightmost digit: 9.\n\n819 \u00d7 9 = 7371. Write that down as the units place: 7371.\n\nNext digit: 2.\n\n819 \u00d7 2 = 1638. Write that shifted one position left: 16380.\n\nNext digit: 4.\n\n819 \u00d7 4 = 3276. Write that shifted two positions left: 327600.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n7371\n\n+16380\n\n+327600\n\nLet's ad