ccording to the standard multiplication, it's 787,684. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check again.\n\nFirst step: 764 \u00d7 1 = 764\n\nSecond step: 764 \u00d7 3 = 2,292, shifted left by one: 22,920\n\nThird step: 764 \u00d7 1 = 764, shifted left by two: 764,000\n\nNow, adding:\n\n764,000\n\n+\u00a0\u00a022,920\n\n= 786,920\n\n786,920\n\n+\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0764\n\n= 787,684\n\nYes, that's correct. So why is the distributive method giving a different answer? Wait, maybe I made a mistake in the distributive method. Wait, 764\u00d7131=764\u00d7(100+30+1)=76,400 +22,920 +764=100,084. But 764\u00d7131 is 764 multiplied by 131. Let me compute 764\u00d7131 manually.\n\nLet me compute 764 \u00d7 131:\n\nFirst, compute 764 \u00d7 100 = 76,400\n\nThen, compute 764 \u00d7 30 = 22,920\n\nThen, compute 764 \u00d7 1 = 764\n\nNow, add them together:\n\n76,400 + 22,920 = 99,320\n\n99,320 + 764 = 100,084\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, it's 787,684. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check with another method. Let's compute 764 \u00d7 131 using the multiplication algorithm step-by-step.\n\nStart with the units digit of 131, which is 1. Multiply 764 by 1: 764.\n\nNext, the tens digit is 3. Multiply 764 by 3: 2,292. Since this is the tens place, we shift one position to the left: 22,920.\n\nNext, the hundreds digit is 1. Multiply 764 by 1: 764. Since this is the hundreds place, we shift two positions to the left: 764,000.\n\nNow, add these three numbers:\n\n764,000\n\n+\u00a0\u00a022,920\n\n= 786,920\n\n786,920\n\n+\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0764\n\n= 787,684\n\nYes, that's correct. So the standard multiplication is correct. Therefore, the distributive method must be wrong. But how?\n\nWait, 764\u00d7131=764\u00d7(100+30+1)=76,400 +22,920 +764=100,084. But 764\u00d7131=787,684. So there's a mistake here. Wait, 