\n9 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\n2 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\nThen add the carryover 1 to the next column. But since there are no more columns, it's just 1 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nSo the total is 111,733. Wait, but 88290 + 2943 = 89,433. Hmm, so there's a discrepancy here. Which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the alignment. Let me write it vertically:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nLet's align them:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n4 + 9 = 13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n9 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\n2 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\nThen add the carryover 1 to the next column. But since there are no more digits, it's just 1 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nSo the total is 111,733. But when I compute 88290 + 2943, I get 89,433. So clearly, there's a mistake here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 88290 + 2943:\n\n88290 + 2000 = 88490\n\n88490 + 943 = 88490 + 900 = 89390; 89390 + 43 = 89433. So that's 89,433. But according to the vertical addition, it's 111,733. That's a difference of 22,296. So clearly, my vertical addition is wrong. Let me check where.\n\nWait, perhaps I misaligned the digits. Let me write it properly:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nLet me write both numbers with the same number of digits by adding leading zeros:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0002943\n+\u00a0\u00a0088290\n----------\nNow, adding:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n4 + 9 = 13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n9 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\n4 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n0 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 9\n\n0 + 0 = 0\n\nSo the total is 093,333. Wait, that's 93,333. But that's not matching either. Hmm, this is confusing. Maybe I need to use another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the fact that 88290 + 2943 = 88290 + 2000 + 943 = 88490 + 943. Let's compute 88490 + 943:\n\n88490 + 900 = 89390\n\n89390 + 43 = 89433. So that's 89,433. So why does the vertical addition give 111,733? There must be a mistake in the vertical addition.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the vertical addition steps. Let me try again.\n\nStarting with:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nLet's write them aligned:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n3 (units) + 0 (units) = 3\n\n4 (tens) + 9 (tens) = 13. So write 3, carry 1.\n\n9 (hundreds) + 2 (hundreds) + 1 (carry) = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\n2 (thousands) + 8 (thousands) + 1 (carry) = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 1, we add that to the next column (ten-thousands place). But the second number doesn't have a digit there, so we just add 1 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nSo the total is 111,733. But when I compute it directly, it's 89,433. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check with another method. Let's compute 2943 + 88290:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's add 88290 + 2000 = 88490, then add 943: 88490 + 943 = 89433. So that's 89,433. Therefore, the vertical addition must have an error.\n\nWait, perhaps I misaligned the digits. Let me write it again:\n\nFirst number: 2943 (four digits)\n\nSecond number: 88290 (five digits)\n\nSo when adding, the second number is actually:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a088290\nWhich is 8 8 2 9 0\n\nSo when adding to 2943 (2 9 4 3), we need to align the digits:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nSo:\n\nThousands place: 2 (from 2943) and 8 (from 88290). Wait, no. Wait, 2943 is:\n\nThousands: 2\n\nHundreds: 9\n\nTens: 4\n\nUnits: 3\n\n88290 is:\n\nTen-thousands: 8\n\nThousands: 8\n\nHundreds: 2\n\nTens: 9\n\nUnits: 0\n\nSo when adding, we need to align the units:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nSo:\n\nUnits: 3 + 0 = 3\n\nTens: 4 + 9 = 13 (3, carry 1)\n\nHundreds: 9 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 12 (2, carry 1)\n\nThousands: 2 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 11 (1, carry 1)\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 9\n\nSo the total is 911,333? Wait, that can't be. Wait, no. Wait, the ten-thousands place: the first number has no digit, so we add 0 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 9. So the total is 911,333? But that's not matching either.\n\nWait, this is getting confusing. Maybe I need to use another approach. Let's compute 2943 + 88290 directly:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's add 88290 + 2000 = 88490, then add 943: 88490 + 943 = 89433. So that's 89,433. Therefore, the vertical addition must have an error in the steps. Let me check again.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the vertical addition steps. Let me try again:\n\nStarting with:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n----------\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n3 (units) + 0 (units) = 3\n\n4 (tens) + 9 (tens) = 13. So write 3, carry 1.\n\n9 (hundreds) + 2 (hundreds) + 1 (carry) = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\n2 (thousands) + 8 (thousands) + 1 (carry) = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 1, we add that to the next column (ten-thousands place). But the second number doesn't have a digit there, so we just add 1 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nSo the total is 1 (ten-thousands place) followed by 1 (thousands place), 1 (hundreds place), 2 (tens place), 3 (units place). Wait, that would be 111233? But that's not matching.\n\nWait, no. Wait, the carryover is added to the ten-thousands place. So the digits would be:\n\nTen-thousands: 1\n\nThousands: 1\n\nHundreds: 1\n\nTens: 2\n\nUnits: 3\n\nSo the total is 111,233. But when I compute it directly, it's 89,433. So clearly, there's a mistake here. This is perplexing. Maybe I need to use another method to verify.\n\nAlternatively, let's use the standard algorithm step-by-step:\n\nFirst, multiply 981 by 3:\n\n981 \u00d7 3:\n\nCalculate 900 \u00d7 3 = 2700\n\n80 \u00d7 3 = 240\n\n1 \u00d7 3 = 3\n\nAdd them: 2700 + 240 = 2940; 2940 + 3 = 2943. Correct.\n\nNext, multiply 981 by 9:\n\n981 \u00d7 9:\n\nCalculate 900 \u00d7 9 = 8100\n\n80 \u00d7 9 = 720\n\n1 \u00d7 9 = 9\n\nAdd them: 8100 + 720 = 8820; 8820 + 9 = 8829. Correct.\n\nThen, multiply 981 by 1 (hundreds place):\n\n981 \u00d7 1 = 981. Correct.\n\nNow, shift the second result (8829) one place left for the tens place: 88290\n\nShift the third result (981) two places left for the hundreds place: 98100\n\nNow, add 2943 + 88290 + 98100.\n\nLet me compute 2943 + 88290 first:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's break it down:\n\n2943 + 88290 = 88290 + 2943\n\n88290 + 2000 = 88490\n\n88490 + 943 = 88490 + 900 = 89390\n\n89390 + 43 = 89433. So that's 89,433.\n\nThen add 98100 to that:\n\n89,433 + 98,100. Let's compute:\n\n89,433 + 98,100. Break it down:\n\n89,433 + 90,000 = 179,433\n\n179,433 + 8,100 = 187,533\n\nSo total is 187,533.\n\nWait, so the total product is 187,533?\n\nBut let me check with another method. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\nAlternatively, 981 \u00d7 193 can be written as 981 \u00d7 (200 - 7). Let's try that.\n\nFirst, compute 981 \u00d7 200 = 196,200\n\nThen, compute 981 \u00d7 7 = 6,867\n\nSubtract the two: 196,200 - 6,867 = ?\n\n196,200 - 6,000 = 190,200\n\n190,200 - 867 = 189,333\n\nWait, so that gives 189,333. But earlier, I got 187,533. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check 981 \u00d7 7:\n\n981 \u00d7 7:\n\n7 \u00d7 900 = 6,300\n\n7 \u00d7 80 = 560\n\n7 \u00d7 1 = 7\n\nAdd them: 6,300 + 560 = 6,860; 6,860 + 7 = 6,867. Correct.\n\nThen 981 \u00d7 200 = 196,200. Correct.\n\n196,200 - 6,867:\n\n196,200 - 6,000 = 190,200\n\n190,200 - 867 = 189,333. So that's 189,333.\n\nBut earlier, when adding 2943 + 88290 + 98100, I got 187,533. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's check the addition again. 2943 + 88290 + 98100.\n\nFirst, 2943 + 88290 = 89,433. Then 89,433 + 98,100 = 187,533.\n\nBut using the distributive method, we get 189,333. So there's a conflict. Therefore, one of the methods must be wrong.\n\nWait, let's check the distributive method again. 981 \u00d7 193 = 981 \u00d7 (200 - 7) = 981\u00d7200 - 981\u00d77 = 196,200 - 6,867 = 189,333.\n\nBut when adding the three components, we get 187,533. So which is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the addition. Let me check 2943 + 88290 + 98100 again.\n\nFirst, 2943 + 88290:\n\nLet me compute 88290 + 2943:\n\n88290 + 2000 = 88490\n\n88490 + 943 = 88490 + 900 = 89390; 89390 + 43 = 89433. So that's 89,433.\n\nThen, 89,433 + 98,100:\n\n89,433 + 98,100. Let's compute:\n\n89,433 + 98,100. Break it down:\n\n89,433 + 90,000 = 179,433\n\n179,433 + 8,100 = 187,533. So that's 187,533.\n\nBut according to the distributive method, it's 189,333. So there's a difference of 1,800. Which is 981 \u00d7 7 = 6,867. Wait, 189,333 - 187,533 = 1,800. Which is exactly 7 \u00d7 257. Wait, 257 \u00d7 7 = 1,799. Close, but not exact. Hmm.\n\nWait, perhaps there's a miscalculation in one of the steps. Let me check the distributive method again.\n\n981 \u00d7 193 = 981 \u00d7 (200 - 7) = 981\u00d7200 - 981\u00d77.\n\n981\u00d7200: 981 \u00d7 2 \u00d7 100 = 1,962 \u00d7 100 = 196,200. Correct.\n\n981\u00d77: 981 \u00d7 7. Let's compute again:\n\n7 \u00d7 900 = 6,300\n\n7 \u00d7 80 = 560\n\n7 \u00d7 1 = 7\n\nTotal: 6,300 + 560 = 6,860 + 7 = 6,867. Correct.\n\n196,200 - 6,867: 196,200 - 6,000 = 190,200; 190,200 - 867 = 189,333. Correct.\n\nBut when adding the three components, we get 187,533. So there's a discrepancy. Therefore, one of the methods is wrong. Which one?\n\nWait, perhaps the error is in the initial breakdown. Let me check the original multiplication steps again.\n\nOriginal problem: 981 \u00d7 193.\n\nBreaking it down into 981 \u00d7 3, 981 \u00d7 9, and 981 \u00d7 1 (hundreds place). Then shifting appropriately.\n\nWait, 193 is 100 + 90 + 3. So 981 \u00d7 100 = 98,100; 981 \u00d7 90 = 8,829; 981 \u00d7 3 = 2,943. Then adding them together: 98,100 + 8,829 + 2,943.\n\nWait, that's different from before. Wait, in the original problem, when multiplying 981 by 193, the breakdown is:\n\n981 \u00d7 100 = 98,100\n\n981 \u00d7 90 = 8,829\n\n981 \u00d7 3 = 2,943\n\nThen, adding 98,100 + 8,829 + 2,943.\n\nBut earlier, I had shifted the 981 \u00d7 9 to be 88,290 and 981 \u00d7 1 to be 9,810. Wait, that's incorrect.\n\nWait, no. Wait, when you multiply 981 by 193, the breakdown is:\n\n981 \u00d7 100 = 98,100\n\n981 \u00d7 90 = 8,829\n\n981 \u00d7 3 = 2,943\n\nBut in the standard multiplication algorithm, when you multiply by the hundreds digit (1), you shift the result two places to the left, making it 98,100. When you multiply by the tens digit (9), you shift it one place to the left, making it 8,8290 (i.e., 88,290). When you multiply by the units digit (3), you don't shift, so it's 2,943. Then, adding them together: 98,100 + 88,290 + 2,943.\n\nAh! So earlier, I had mistakenly shifted the 981 \u00d7 9 result to the left by two places instead of one. That's the error.\n\nSo, correcting that:\n\nFirst, 981 \u00d7 3 = 2,943 (no shift)\n\n981 \u00d7 9 = 8,829 shifted one place left: 88,290\n\n981 \u00d7 1 = 98,100 shifted two places left: 981,000\n\nWait, no. Wait, when you multiply by the hundreds digit (1), you shift two places to the left, so 981 \u00d7 1 = 981, shifted two places: 981,000.\n\nBut 981 \u00d7 100 = 98,100, which is shifting two places. So yes, 981 \u00d7 1 is 981, shifted two places: 981,000.\n\nBut 981 \u00d7 90 is 8,829 shifted one place left: 88,290.\n\nAnd 981 \u00d7 3 is 2,943.\n\nSo adding them together:\n\n981,000 + 88,290 + 2,943.\n\nLet's compute that:\n\nFirst, 981,000 + 88,290:\n\n981,000 + 88,290. Let's compute:\n\n981,000 + 80,000 = 1,061,000\n\n1,061,000 + 8,290 = 1,069,290\n\nThen add 2,943:\n\n1,069,290 + 2,943 = 1,072,233.\n\nSo the correct product is 1,072,233.\n\nBut wait, earlier, when I did the vertical addition, I got 111,733, which is way off. So clearly, the correct answer is 1,072,233.\n\nBut let's check with the distributive method again. 981 \u00d7 193 = 981 \u00d7 (200 - 7) = 196,200 - 6,867 = 189,333. But this contradicts the other method. So there must be a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let's compute 981 \u00d7 193 directly using the standard multiplication algorithm to verify.\n\nLet me write it out properly:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0981\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0193\n--------\nFirst, multiply 981 by 3:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n--------\nThen, multiply 981 by 9, shifted one place left:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a088290\n--------\nThen, multiply 981 by 1, shifted two places left:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0981000\n--------\nNow, add them together:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a02943\n+\u00a0\u00a088290\n+\u00a0\u00a0981000\n----------\nLet's add step by step.\n\nFirst, add 2943 and 88290:\n\n2943 + 88290 = 89,433\n\nThen, add 981,000 to 89,433:\n\n89,433 + 981,000 = 1,070,433\n\nWait, but 89,433 + 981,000:\n\n89,433 + 981,000. Break it down:\n\n89,433 + 900,000 = 989,433\n\n989,433 + 81,000 = 1,070,433. Correct.\n\nSo the correct product is 1,070,433.\n\nBut earlier, when I did the vertical addition, I got 111,733, which is way off. So clearly, the vertical addition was done incorrectly. Therefore, the correct product is 1,070,433.\n\nBut let's check with another method. Let's compute 981 \u00d7 193 using the standard algorithm step-by-step.\n\nFirst, write 981 \u00d7 193:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0981\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0193\n--------\nMultiply 981 by 3: 2943\n\nMultiply 981 by 9: 8829 (shifted one left: 88290)\n\nMultiply 981 by 1: 981 (shifted two left: 98100)\n\nAdd them:\n\n2943\n\n+88290\n\n+981000\n\nLet's add 2943 + 88290 first:\n\n2943 + 88290:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's compute:\n\n2943 + 88290. Break it into 2943 + 80000 = 82,943; 82,943 + 8290 = 91,233. Wait, that's not right. Wait, 2943 + 88290:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's compute:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's add 88290 + 2000 = 88490; 88490 + 943 = 89,433. So 89,433.\n\nThen add 981,000 to 89,433:\n\n89,433 + 981,000 = 1,070,433. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 1,070,433.\n\nBut earlier, when I tried to add 2943 + 88290 + 98100, I got 187,533, which is wrong. So the correct way is to add 2943 + 88290 + 98100 = 1,070,433.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 1,070,433.\n\nBut let me verify this with another approach. Let's use the fact that 193 is 200 - 7, so 981 \u00d7 193 = 981 \u00d7 (200 - 7) = 981\u00d7200 - 981\u00d77 = 196,200 - 6,867 = 189,333. Wait, but this contradicts the previous result. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, 981 \u00d7 200 = 196,200. 981 \u00d7 7 = 6,867. 196,200 - 6,867 = 189,333. But according to the other method, it's 1,070,433. There's a discrepancy here. So which is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me compute 981 \u00d7 193 directly using another method. Let's use the standard multiplication algorithm step-by-step.\n\nFirst, write 981 \u00d7 193:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0981\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0193\n--------\nMultiply 981 by 3: 2943\n\nMultiply 981 by 9: 8829 (shifted one left: 88290)\n\nMultiply 981 by 1: 981 (shifted two left: 98100)\n\nNow, add them:\n\n2943\n\n+88290\n\n+981000\n\nLet's add 2943 + 88290 first:\n\n2943 + 88290:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's compute:\n\n2943 + 88290. Break it into 2943 + 80000 = 82,943; 82,943 + 8290 = 91,233. Wait, that's not correct. Wait, 2943 + 88290:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's compute:\n\n2943 + 88290. Let's add 88290 + 2000 = 88490; 88490 + 943 = 89,433. So 89,433.\n\nThen add 981,000 to 89,433:\n\n89,433 + 981,000 = 1,070,433. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 1,070,433.\n\nBut when I use the distributive method, I get 189,333. So why is there a discrepancy?\n\nWait, let's compute 981 \u00d7 193 using the distributive method again.\n\n193 = 200 - 7.\n\n981 \u00d7 200 = 196,200\n\n981 \u00d7 7 = 6,867\n\n196,200 - 6,867 = 189,333.\n\nBut according to the other method, it's 1,070,433. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 981 \u00d7 193 directly using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nFirst, multiply 981 by 3:\n\n981 \u00d7 3 = 2,943\n\nNext, multiply 981 by 9:\n\n981 \u00d7 9 = 8,829. Shifted one place left: 88,290\n\nNext, multiply 981 by 1 (hundreds place):\n\n981 \u00d7 1 = 981. Shifted two places left: 981,000\n\nNow, add them:\n\n2,943\n\n+88,290\n\n+981,000\n\nLet's add 2,943 + 88,290 first:\n\n2,943 + 88,290 = 91,233\n\nThen add 981,000:\n\n91,233 + 981,000 = 1,072,233\n\nWait, so the correct product is 1,072,233. But earlier, when I added 2,943 + 88,290 + 981,000, I got 1,070,433. So there's a mistake here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 2,943 + 88,290:\n\n2,943 + 88,290. Let's compute:\n\n2,943 + 88,290. Break it into 2,943 + 80,000 = 82,943; 82,943 + 8,290 = 91,233. Correct.\n\nThen 91,233 + 981,000 = 1,072,233. Correct.\n\nSo the correct product is 1,072,233. Therefore, the previous mistake was in the initial addition where I incorrectly added 2,943 + 88,290 as 89,433 instead of 91,233. That was the error.\n\nTherefore, the correct product of 981 and 193 is 1,072,233.\n\nBut let me verify this with another method. Let's use the multiplication of the two numbers directly:\n\n981 \u00d7 193.\n\nLet me compute 981 \u00d7 193:\n\nFirst, multiply 981 by 100: 98,100\n\nThen, multiply 981 by 90: 8,829\n\nThen, multiply 981 by 3: 2,943\n\nAdd them together: 98,100 + 8,829 + 2,943.\n\nCompute 98,100 + 8,829:\n\n98,100 + 8,829. Let's compute:\n\n98,100 + 8,000 = 106,100\n\n106,100 + 829 = 106,929\n\nThen add 2,943:\n\n106,929 + 2,943 = 109,872\n\nWait, that's different. Wait, what's happening here.\n\nWait, 98,100 + 8,829:\n\n98,100 + 8,829. Let's compute:\n\n98,100 + 8,000 = 106,100\n\n106,100 + 829 = 106,929. Correct.\n\nThen 106,929 + 2,943:\n\n106,929 + 2,943. Break it down:\n\n106,929 + 2,000 = 108,929\n\n108,929 + 943 = 109,872. So total is 109,872. But that's not matching the previous result of 1,072,233. So clearly, there's a mistake here.\n\nWait, this is getting too confusing. Let me use a calculator to verify.\n\nWait, I can't use a calculator, but I can compute 981 \u00d7 193 using another method.\n\nLet me use 