So, starting from the rightmost digit (units place), which is 5, the partial product is shifted left by 1. Then the next digit (tens place, 0) is shifted left by 2, and the hundreds place (9) is shifted left by 3.\n\nSo, writing them out:\n\nFirst partial product (units place 5): 738 \u00d7 5 = 3690. Shift left by 1: 36900.\n\nSecond partial product (tens place 0): 738 \u00d7 0 = 0. Shift left by 2: 0000.\n\nThird partial product (hundreds place 9): 738 \u00d7 9 = 6642. Shift left by 3: 6642000.\n\nNow, adding these three partial products:\n\n36900\n+\u00a0\u00a00000\n+6642000\n= 6678900\n\nWait, so that's 6,678,900. But when I did the distributive method, I got 70,110. That's way off. So clearly, there's a mistake here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with another method. Let's compute 738 \u00d7 905 directly.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm correctly. Let me try again.\n\nMultiplying 738 by 905:\n\nFirst, write 738 \u00d7 5:\n\n5 \u00d7 8 = 40, write down 0, carry over 4.\n\n5 \u00d7 3 = 15 + 4 = 19, write down 9, carry over 1.\n\n5 \u00d7 7 = 35 + 1 = 36, write down 36.\n\nSo, 3690. That's correct.\n\nNext, multiply 738 by 0 (tens place):\n\n0 \u00d7 8 = 0, write down 0.\n\n0 \u00d7 3 = 0, write down 0.\n\n0 \u00d7 7 = 0, write down 0.\n\nSo, 0000. Correct.\n\nNext, multiply 738 by 9 (hundreds place):\n\n9 \u00d7 8 = 72, write down 2, carry over 7.\n\n9 \u00d7 3 = 27 + 7 = 34, write down 4, carry over 3.\n\n9 \u00d7 7 = 63 + 3 = 66, write down 66.\n\nSo, 6642. Correct.\n\nNow, adding the three partial products:\n\n36900 (from 5)\n+\u00a0\u00a00000 (from 0)\n+6642000 (from 9)\n= 6678900\n\nWait, so that's 6,678,900. But when I did the distributive method, I got 70,110. That's a big difference. So, which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with a calculator. Let me compute 738 \u00d7 905.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 738 \u00d7 905 using another approach. Let's see.\n\nFirst, note that 905 is 900 + 5. So,