881720. So the total product should be 881720.\n\nWait, let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\n940 \u00d7 738 can be broken down into (900 + 40) \u00d7 (700 + 30 + 8). Let's compute each part:\n\nFirst, 900 \u00d7 700 = 630000\n\nThen, 900 \u00d7 30 = 27000\n\nNext, 900 \u00d7 8 = 7200\n\nThen, 40 \u00d7 700 = 28000\n\n40 \u00d7 30 = 1200\n\n40 \u00d7 8 = 320\n\nNow, add all these together:\n\n630000 + 27000 = 657000\n\n657000 + 7200 = 664200\n\n664200 + 28000 = 692200\n\n692200 + 1200 = 693400\n\n693400 + 320 = 693720\n\nWait, that's 693720. But earlier, I got 881720. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nHmm, so clearly, I made a mistake in one of the methods. Let me check both again.\n\nFirst method:\n\n940 \u00d7 8 = 7520\n\n940 \u00d7 3 = 2820 (shifted left by one, so 28200)\n\n940 \u00d7 9 = 8460 (shifted left by two, so 846000)\n\nAdding them: 7520 + 28200 = 35720; 35720 + 846000 = 881720.\n\nSecond method:\n\nBreaking into (900 + 40) \u00d7 (700 + 30 + 8) gives:\n\n900\u00d7700=630000\n\n900\u00d730=27000\n\n900\u00d78=7200\n\n40\u00d7700=28000\n\n40\u00d730=1200\n\n40\u00d78=320\n\nAdding all: 630000 + 27000 = 657000; 657000 + 7200 = 664200; 664200 + 28000 = 692200; 692200 + 1200 = 693400; 693400 + 320 = 693720.\n\nSo two different results. Which is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the second method. Let me check each multiplication again.\n\nFirst, 900 \u00d7 700: 900*700. 9*7=63, then two zeros: 63000. So 630000. Correct.\n\n900 \u00d7 30: 900*3=2700, then one zero: 27000. Correct.\n\n900 \u00d7 8: 900*8=7200. Correct.\n\n40 \u00d7 700: 40*700. 4*7=28, two zeros: 28000. Correct.\n\n40 \u00d7 30: 40*3=120, one zero: 1200. Correct.\n\n40 \u00d7 8: 40*8=320. Correct.\n\nSo adding them up step by step:\n\n630000 + 27000 = 657000. Correct.\n\n657000 + 7200 = 664200. Correct.\n\n664200 + 28000 = 692200. Correct.\n\n692200 + 1200 = 693400. Correct.\n\n693400 + 320 = 693720. Correct.\n\nSo the second method gives 693720, but the first method gives 881720. These are different. Therefore, one of the methods is wrong. Let me check the first method again.\n\nFirst method:\n\n940 \u00d7 8: 940*8. Let's compute 900*8=7200, 40*8=320. 7200+320=7520. Correct.\n\n940 \u00d7 3: 900*3=2700, 40*3=120. 2700+120=2820. Since it's the tens place, we add a zero, making it 28200. Correct.\n\n940 \u00d7 9: 900*9=8100, 40*9=360. 8100+360=8460. Since it's the hundreds place, add two zeros: 846000. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 7520 + 28200. Let's do 7520 + 28200. 7520 + 28200. Let's add 7000 + 28000 = 35000. Then 520 + 200 = 720. So 35000 + 720 = 35720. Then 35720 + 846000. Let's add 35720 + 846000. 35720 + 800000 = 835720. Then add 46000: 835720 + 46000 = 881720. Correct.\n\nSo both methods seem correct, but they give different results. That can't be. There must be a mistake in one of the methods. Wait, but how?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the second method. Let me check the breakdown again. The original number is 940, which is 900 + 40. The multiplier is 738, which is 700 + 30 + 8. So when we distribute, we have:\n\n(900 + 40) \u00d7 (700 + 30 + 8) = 900\u00d7700 + 900\u00d730 + 900\u00d78 + 40\u00d7700 + 40\u00d730 + 40\u00d78. That's correct.\n\nBut when I add them up, I get 630000 + 27000 + 7200 + 28000 + 1200 + 320. Let's add them in a different order to check.\n\n630000 + 28000 = 658000\n\n27000 + 1200 = 28200\n\n7200 + 320 = 7520\n\nNow add those: 658000 + 28200 = 686200\n\n686200 + 7520 = 693720. Same result. So that's correct.\n\nBut the first method gave 881720. So why the discrepancy?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the first method. Let me check the partial products again.\n\nFirst partial product: 940 \u00d7 8 = 7520. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 940 \u00d7 3. Since it's the tens place, we need to shift one position left, so 2820 becomes 28200. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 940 \u00d7 9. Since it's the hund