      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 873 and 387. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two three-digit numbers can be a bit tricky, but maybe there's a way to break it down step by step. Let me start by recalling the standard multiplication algorithm. \n\nFirst, I'll write 873 multiplied by 387. Let me set it up like this:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0873\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0387\n--------\n\nStarting with the rightmost digit of the second number, which is 7. I need to multiply 873 by 7 and then multiply 873 by the next digit, which is 8, but since it's in the tens place, I have to remember to shift it one position to the left. Then, multiply 873 by 3 (the hundreds place of 387) and shift it two positions to the left. Finally, add all those results together.\n\nLet me start with the first multiplication: 873 \u00d7 7. Let's calculate that. \n\n7 \u00d7 7 is 49, write down 9 and carry over 4. Then 7 \u00d7 3 is 21, plus the carried over 4 makes 25. So that's 591. Wait, no, hold on. Wait, 7 \u00d7 7 is 49, so the first digit is 9, carry over 4. Then 7 \u00d7 3 is 21, plus 4 is 25. So the next digit is 5, carry over 2. Then 7 \u00d7 8 is 56, plus the carried over 2 is 58. So putting that together, 5891? Wait, that can't be right. Wait, 873 \u00d7 7. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 800 \u00d7 7 = 5600, 70 \u00d7 7 = 490, 3 \u00d7 7 = 21. So 5600 + 490 = 6090, plus 21 is 6111. Oh, right! I messed up the breakdown earlier. So 873 \u00d7 7 is 6111. Got that.\n\nNext, multiply 873 by 8. Let's do that. 800 \u00d7 8 = 6400, 70 \u00d7 8 = 560, 3 \u00d7 8 = 24. So 6400 + 560 = 6960, plus 24 is 6984. So 873 \u00d7 8 = 6984. But since this is in the tens place, we need to shift it one position to the left, so it becomes 69840.\n\nThen, multiply 873 by 3. 800 \u00d7 3 = 2400, 70 \u00d7 3 = 210, 3 \u00d7 3 = 9. So 2400 + 210 = 2610, plus 9 is 2619. So 873 \u00d7 3 = 2619. Since this is the hundreds place, we shift it two positions to the left, making it 261900.\n\nNow, add all three results together: 6111 + 69840 + 261900. Let's do this step by step.\n\nFirst, add 6111 and 69840. Let's see:\n\n6111 + 69840. Let's break it down:\n\n6000 + 69000 = 75000\n\n111 + 840 = 951\n\nSo total is 75000 + 951 = 75951.\n\nWait, but 6111 + 69840. Let me check with another method. 69840 + 6000 = 75840, then +111 = 75951. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow, add 75951 + 261900. Let's do that:\n\n75951 + 261900. Let's break it down:\n\n70000 + 260000 = 330000\n\n5951 + 1900 = 7851\n\nSo total is 330000 + 7851 = 337851.\n\nWait, let me verify that addition another way. 261900 + 75951. \n\n261900 + 70000 = 331900\n\n331900 + 5951 = 337851. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the total product is 337,851. Let me check if that makes sense. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to verify. Let's try using the distributive property.\n\n873 \u00d7 387 can be written as 873 \u00d7 (400 - 13). Because 387 is 400 - 13. Let's see if that helps.\n\nFirst, compute 873 \u00d7 400. That's 873 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 100 = 3492 \u00d7 100 = 349200.\n\nThen, compute 873 \u00d7 13. Let's break that down: 873 \u00d7 10 = 8730, 873 \u00d7 3 = 2619. So 8730 + 2619 = 11349.\n\nNow, subtract 873 \u00d7 13 from 873 \u00d7 400: 349200 - 11349.\n\nLet's compute that. 349200 - 10000 = 339200\n\n339200 - 1349 = 339200 - 1000 = 338200\n\n338200 - 349 = 338200 - 300 = 337900\n\n337900 - 49 = 337851\n\nYes! So that gives the same result, 337851. So that's a good check. Therefore, the product of 873 and 387 is 337,851.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another check by adding the two original numbers and then multiplying by some factor, but that might be more complicated. Alternatively, use a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, but since both methods gave me the same answer, I can be confident that 337,851 is correct.\n\nWait, just to make sure, let me try another way. Let's use the standard multiplication step-by-step.\n\nMultiplying 873 by 387:\n\nFirst, write 873 \u00d7 7 = 6111\n\nThen, 873 \u00d7 80 = 69840 (since 873 \u00d7 8 = 6984, shifted one position left)\n\nThen, 873 \u00d7 300 = 261900 (since 873 \u00d7 3 = 2619, shifted two positions left)\n\nAdding them up: 6111 + 69840 + 261900 = 337851. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the lattice method? But that might be more time-consuming. Alternatively, use the fact that 873 \u00d7 387 = 873 \u00d7 (400 - 13) which we already did. So, seems like 337,851 is the correct answer.\n\nI think that's thorough enough. I can't see any mistakes in the calculations, and both methods confirm the same result. So I'm confident that the product is 337,851.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 873 and 387 is \\boxed{337851}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 873 and 387, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. Multiply 873 by 7:\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 7 = 6111\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 873 by 8 (shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 8 = 6984 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by 1)} \\quad 69840\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 873 by 3 (shifted two positions to the left):\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 3 = 2619 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by 2)} \\quad 261900\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:\n   \\[\n   6111 + 69840 + 261900\n   \\]\n\n5. Break down the addition step-by-step:\n   - First, add 6111 and 69840:\n     \\[\n     6111 + 69840 = 75951\n     \\]\n   - Then, add 75951 and 261900:\n     \\[\n     75951 + 261900 = 337851\n     \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Express 387 as 400 - 13:\n  \\[\n  873 \\times 387 = 873 \\times (400 - 13)\n  \\]\n- Calculate each part:\n  \\[\n  873 \\times 400 = 349200 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 873 \\times 13 = 11349\n  \\]\n- Subtract the results:\n  \\[\n  349200 - 11349 = 337851\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 873 and 387 is \\(\\boxed{337851}\\).",
