600, minus 1 * 8 = 8, so 5600 - 8 = 5592. Then multiply by 100: 5592 * 100 = 559200. \n\nNext, 699 * 75. Hmm, 75 is 70 + 5. So, 699 * 70 + 699 * 5. Let's compute those. \n\n699 * 70: 699 * 7 * 10. 699 * 7: 700 * 7 = 4900, minus 1 * 7 = 7, so 4900 - 7 = 4893. Multiply by 10: 48930. \n\n699 * 5: 600 * 5 = 3000, 90 * 5 = 450, 9 * 5 = 45. So 3000 + 450 = 3450 + 45 = 3495. \n\nNow, add 48930 + 3495. Let's do that. 48930 + 3000 = 51930, then + 495 = 51930 + 495. 51930 + 400 = 52330, then +95 = 52425. \n\nSo, 699 * 75 = 52425. \n\nNow, add the two parts together: 559200 + 52425. Let's compute that. 559200 + 50000 = 609200, then +2425 = 609200 + 2425. 609200 + 2000 = 611200, then +425 = 611200 + 425 = 611625. \n\nWait, so according to this method, the product is 611625. But earlier, using the standard multiplication, I got 13980. That's a big discrepancy. So clearly, I made a mistake somewhere. Let me check both methods again.\n\nFirst, let's check the standard multiplication step by step. \n\nMultiplying 699 by 875:\n\nFirst digit (5): 699 * 5 = 3495. Correct.\n\nSecond digit (7): 699 * 7. Let's do 700*7 = 4900, minus 1*7 = 7, so 4900 - 7 = 4893. Correct.\n\nThird digit (8): 699 * 8. 700*8 = 5600, minus 1*8 = 8, so 5600 - 8 = 5592. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 3495 + 4893 + 5592.\n\n3495 + 4893: Let's compute 3495 + 4893. \n\n3495 + 4000 = 7495\n\n7495 + 800 = 8295\n\n8295 + 80 = 8375\n\n8375 + 3 = 8378. Wait, that's different from what I did before. Wait, maybe I messed up the addition steps earlier.\n\nWait, let's do 3495 + 4893 properly.\n\n3495\n\n+4893\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 + 3 = 8\n\n9 + 9 = 18, carryover 1\n\n4 + 8 + 1 (carryover) = 13, carryover 1\n\n3 + 4 + 1 (carryover) = 8\n\nSo total is 8378. Then add 5592 to 8378.\n\n8378 + 5592:\n\n8000 + 5000 = 13000\n\n378 + 592 = 970\n\nSo total is 13000 + 970 = 13970. Wait, but earlier I thought it was 13980. So that's a mistake. So the correct total is 13970. Then, 13970. But when I did the second method, I got 611625. That's way off. So clearly, there's a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let's check the second method again. 699 * 875 = 699*(800 + 75) = 699*800 + 699*75.\n\n699*800: 699*8*100. 699*8: 5592. 5592*100 = 559200. Correct.\n\n699*75: 699*(70 + 5) = 699*70 + 699*5.\n\n699*70: 699*7*10. 699*7: 4893. 4893*10 = 48930. Correct.\n\n699*5: 3495. Correct.\n\nAdding 48930 + 3495: 48930 + 3000 = 51930; 51930 + 495 = 52425. Correct.\n\nThen 559200 + 52425: 559200 + 50000 = 609200; 609200 + 2425 = 611625. Hmm, that's correct. But according to the standard multiplication, the answer is 13970. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check that again.\n\nMultiplying 699 by 875:\n\nLet's write it out vertically:\n\n      699\n\n    x 875\n\n------------\n\nFirst, multiply 699 by 5:\n\n699\n\nx  5\n\n------\n\n3495\n\nThen multiply 699 by 70 (shift one position to the left):\n\n  699\n\nx 70\n\n--------\n\n48930\n\nThen multiply 699 by 800 (shift two positions to the left):\n\n  699\n\nx 800\n\n--------\n\n559200\n\nNow add them up:\n\n  3495\n\n+48930\n\n+559200\n\nLet's add 3495 + 48930 first. 3495 + 48930. 3495 + 48930. Let's do 3495 + 48930. 3495 + 48930. 3495 + 48930. Let's add 3495 + 48930. 3495 + 48930. 3495 + 48930. Let's break it down:\n\n3495 + 48930 = 48930 + 3495. 48930 + 3000 = 51930, then +495 = 51930 + 495 = 52425. Then add 559200 to 52425. 52425 + 559200. 52425 + 559200. 52425 + 500000 = 552425, then +59200 = 552425 + 59200. 552425 + 50000 = 602425, then +9200 = 602425 + 9200 = 611625. Wait, so according to this, the total is 611625. But that contradicts the previous result. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, but 699 * 875. Let me check with another method. Maybe using the difference of squares or something. Alternatively, maybe using 875 as 75/8 or something. Wait, 875 is 75 * 11.666..., but that might not help. Alternatively, 875 is 1000 - 125. So 699 * 875 = 699*(1000 - 125) = 699*1000 - 699*125. Let's compute that.\n\n699*1000 = 699000\n\n699*125: Hmm, 125 is 100 + 25. So 699*100 = 69900, 699*25 = 17475. So 69900 + 17475 = 87375. Therefore, 699*875 = 699000 - 87375 = 699000 - 87375. Let's compute that. 699000 - 87375. \n\nSubtract 80000 from 699000: 699000 - 80000 = 619000\n\nThen subtract 7375: 619000 - 7375. 619000 - 7000 = 612000, then -375 = 612000 - 375 = 611625. So that gives 611625. So that's the same as the second method. So that's correct. Then why did the standard multiplication give me 13970? That must be wrong. Wait, but when I did the standard multiplication step by step, I thought I got 13970, but when I broke it down into 699*800 + 699*75, I got 559200 + 52425 = 611625. So clearly, the standard multiplication was done incorrectly. Let me check that again.\n\nWait, when I did the standard multiplication, I wrote:\n\nFirst digit (5): 3495\n\nSecond digit (7): 4893\n\nThird digit (8): 5592\n\nThen added them as 3495 + 4893 + 5592. But when I added 3495 + 4893, I thought it was 8378, but actually, 3495 + 4893 is 8378. Then adding 5592 to 8378: 8378 + 5592. Let's compute that again. 8378 + 5592. \n\n8378 + 5000 = 13378\n\n13378 + 592 = 13970. \n\nWait, so that's where the mistake was. When I did the standard multiplication, I thought the sum was 13970, but when I broke it down into 699*800 + 699*75, I got 611625. But according to the difference of squares method, it's 611625. So the standard multiplication must have had an error in the addition step. Let me check the addition again.\n\n3495 (from 5)\n\n+4893 (from 7)\n\n= 3495 + 4893. Let's compute this again. \n\n3495\n\n+4893\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 + 3 = 8\n\n9 + 9 = 18, carryover 1\n\n4 + 8 + 1 = 13, carryover 1\n\n3 + 4 + 1 = 8\n\nSo total is 8378. Then adding 5592:\n\n8378 + 5592. \n\n8378 + 5000 = 13378\n\n13378 + 592 = 13970. \n\nBut according to the other methods, the correct answer is 611625. So clearly, the standard multiplication was done incorrectly. Wait, but how? Let me check the original multiplication steps again.\n\nWait, 699 * 875. Let's do it another way. Maybe using the fact that 875 is 75/8. So 699 * 875 = 699 * (75/8) = (699 * 75)/8. Let's compute 699 * 75 first. \n\n699 * 75. Let's compute 699 * 75. \n\n699 * 75 = 699 * (70 + 5) = 699*70 + 699*5. \n\n699*70: 699*7*10. 699*7: 4893. 4893*10 = 48930. \n\n699*5: 3495. \n\nSo 48930 + 3495 = 52425. Then divide by 8: 52425 / 8. Let's compute that. \n\n52425 \u00f7 8. \n\n8*6000 = 48000. 52425 - 48000 = 4425. \n\n4425 \u00f7 8 = 553.125. \n\nSo total is 6000 + 553.125 = 6553.125. Wait, that's not an integer. But 699 * 875 should be an integer. So this method is wrong. Wait, why? Because 875 is 75/8, but 699 and 875 may not be compatible for division. Wait, 699 and 875: 875 divides into 699? No, 875 is larger than 699. So this approach is invalid. So that method is not applicable here. So scratch that.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication correctly. Let me try again.\n\nMultiplying 699 by 875:\n\nFirst, write 699 * 875.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n      699\n\n    x 875\n\n------------\n\nMultiply 699 by 5:\n\n699\n\nx  5\n\n------\n\n3495\n\nMultiply 699 by 70 (shift one position left):\n\n  699\n\nx 70\n\n--------\n\n48930\n\nMultiply 699 by 800 (shift two positions left):\n\n  699\n\nx 800\n\n--------\n\n559200\n\nNow, add these three results:\n\n3495\n\n+48930\n\n+559200\n\nLet's add 3495 + 48930 first. \n\n3495 + 48930:\n\n3495 + 48930 = 48930 + 3495. \n\n48930 + 3000 = 51930\n\n51930 + 495 = 52425\n\nThen add 559200 to 52425:\n\n52425 + 559200 = 611625\n\nAh! So earlier, when I thought I added 3495 + 4893 + 5592 as 13970, that was incorrect. The correct addition is 3495 + 48930 + 559200 = 611625. So the standard multiplication actually gives the correct result of 611625. So my initial mistake was in the addition step where I incorrectly summed 3495 + 4893 as 8378 and then adding 5592 to get 13970, but that was wrong. The correct sum is 611625. \n\nTherefore, the correct product of 699 and 875 is 611625. \n\nAlternatively, let me check with another method. Let's use the distributive property in a different way. \n\nNote that 875 = 1000 - 125. So 699 * 875 = 699*(1000 - 125) = 699*1000 - 699*125. \n\n699*1000 is straightforward: 699,000. \n\nNow, 699*125. Let's compute that. \n\n125 is 100 + 25. So 699*100 = 69,900. \n\n699*25: 699*25. Let's compute 699*25. \n\n25 is a quarter, so 699*25 = 699*(100/4) = (699*100)/4 = 69,900 / 4 = 17,475. \n\nTherefore, 699*125 = 69,900 + 17,475 = 87,375. \n\nTherefore, 699*875 = 699,000 - 87,375 = 611,625. \n\nSame result. So that confirms it. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the method of multiplying by adding zeros. For example, 699 * 875. Let's write 875 as 875.0 and multiply step by step, adding zeros as needed. \n\nBut that might be more complicated. Alternatively, use the fact that 699 is 700 - 1. So 699 = 700 - 1. Therefore, 699 * 875 = (700 - 1) * 875 = 700*875 - 1*875. \n\nCompute 700*875: 700*800 = 560,000; 700*75 = 52,500. So total is 560,000 + 52,500 = 612,500. \n\nThen subtract 875: 612,500 - 875 = 611,625. \n\nAgain, same result. \n\nTherefore, all methods lead to 611,625. So the correct answer is 611,625. \n\nI must have made a mistake in the initial standard multiplication when I thought the sum was 13,970 instead of 611,625. That was a critical error. So the key takeaway is to carefully perform each step in multiplication and addition, making sure not to make any arithmetic mistakes. \n\nAnother way to verify is to use a calculator. But since I don't have one here, I'll just cross-verify with another manual multiplication. \n\nLet me write out 699 * 875 using the standard algorithm step by step:\n\nFirst, write 699 and 875 aligned:\n\n      699\n\n    x 875\n\n------------\n\nMultiply 699 by 5:\n\n699\n\nx  5\n\n------\n\n3495\n\nMultiply 699 by 70 (shift one position left):\n\n  699\n\nx 70\n\n--------\n\n48930\n\nMultiply 699 by 800 (shift two positions left):\n\n  699\n\nx 800\n\n--------\n\n559200\n\nNow, add the three partial products:\n\n3495\n\n+48930\n\n+559200\n\nStart adding 3495 + 48930:\n\n3495 + 48930 = 52425\n\nThen add 52425 + 559200:\n\n52425 + 559200 = 611625\n\nYes, that's correct. So the correct product is 611,625. \n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and cross-verification, the product of 699 and 875 is 611,625.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 699 and 875 is \\boxed{611625}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 699 and 875, we can use the distributive property and step-by-step multiplication:\n\n1. **Break down 875 into 800 and 75:**\n   \\[\n   699 \\times 875 = 699 \\times (800 + 75)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**\n   - \\(699 \\times 800\\):\n     \\[\n     699 \\times 800 = 699 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 5592 \\times 100 = 559200\n     \\]\n   - \\(699 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     699 \\times 75 = 699 \\times (70 + 5) = 699 \\times 70 + 699 \\times 5\n     \\]\n     - \\(699 \\times 70\\):\n       \\[\n       699 \\times 70 = 699 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 4893 \\times 10 = 48930\n       \\]\n     - \\(699 \\times 5\\):\n       \\[\n       699 \\times 5 = 3495\n       \\]\n     - Add the results:\n       \\[\n       48930 + 3495 = 52425\n       \\]\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two parts:**\n   \\[\n   559200 + 52425 = 611625\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification using another method:**\n   - Using the difference of squares:\n     \\[\n     699 \\times 875 = 699 \\times (1000 - 125) = 699 \\times 1000 - 699 \\times 125\n     \\]\n     - \\(699 \\times 1000 = 699000\\)\n     - \\(699 \\times 125 = 87375\\)\n     - Subtract:\n       \\[\n       699000 - 87375 = 611625\n       \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 699 and 875 is \\(\\boxed{611625}\\).",
