00=224780, then +328. 224780 + 300=225080, then +28=225108. Yes, that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's a smarter way to do this multiplication. Let me try another method to cross-verify.\n\nAnother way to multiply 666 and 338 is to use the distributive property. Let's see:\n\n338 can be written as 300 + 30 + 8, which is what I did before. Alternatively, maybe 338 is 340 - 2. Let me try that.\n\nSo, 666*(340 - 2) = 666*340 - 666*2.\n\nFirst, compute 666*340. Let's break that down. 666*300=199800, 666*40=26640. So 199800 + 26640 = 226440.\n\nThen subtract 666*2=1332. So 226440 - 1332. Let's compute that.\n\n226440 - 1000 = 225440\n\n225440 - 332 = 225440 - 300 = 225140, then +68 = 225140 + 68 = 225208.\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result of 225108. Hmm, so now I have two different answers. That means I must have made a mistake somewhere. Let me check this alternative method again.\n\nWait, 666*340 - 666*2. Let's compute 666*340 first.\n\n340 is 300 + 40. So 666*300=199800, 666*40=26640. Adding those gives 199800 + 26640. Let's compute that again.\n\n199800 + 26640. 199800 + 20000 = 219800, then +6640. 219800 + 6640. 219800 + 6000 = 225800, then +640 = 226440. So that part is correct.\n\nThen subtract 666*2=1332. So 226440 - 1332. Let's do this subtraction step by step.\n\n226440 - 1000 = 225440\n\n225440 - 300 = 225140\n\n225140 - 32 = 225140 - 30 = 225110, then +8 = 225118\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, 225440 - 1332. Let's break down 1332 into 1000 + 300 + 32.\n\nSo 225440 - 1000 = 225440 - 1000 = 224440\n\n224440 - 300 = 224440 - 300 = 224140\n\n224140 - 32 = 224140 - 30 = 224110, then +8 = 224118\n\nWait, so that gives 224118. But that contradicts the previous result. Wait, so now I'm confused. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the alternative method. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal problem: 666 * 338.\n\nAlternative approach: 338 = 340 - 2, so 666*338 = 666*340 - 666*2.\n\nCompute 666*340:\n\n340 * 666. Let's compute 340*600 = 204000\n\n340*60 = 20400\n\n340*6 = 2040\n\nAdding those: 204000 + 20400 = 224400 + 2040 = 226440. So that's correct.\n\nThen subtract 666*2=1332. So 226440 - 1332.\n\nLet me compute 226440 - 1332:\n\n226440 - 1000 = 225440\n\n225440 - 300 = 225140\n\n225140 - 32 = 225140 - 30 = 225110 + 8 = 225118\n\nWait, so that gives 225118. But previously, using the standard multiplication, I got 225108. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check that again.\n\nStandard multiplication:\n\n666\n\nx338\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 666 by 8:\n\n666*8=5328\n\nThen multiply 666 by 30 (shift one position to the left):\n\n666*30=19980\n\nThen multiply 666 by 300 (shift two positions to the left):\n\n666*300=199800\n\nNow add them up:\n\n199800\n\n+ 19980\n\n= 219780\n\nThen add 5328:\n\n219780 + 5328 = 225108\n\nSo that's 225108.\n\nBut in the alternative method, I got 225118. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 666*338 using another method. Maybe using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nLet me write it out properly:\n\n      666\n\n    x 338\n\n    --------\n\nFirst, multiply 666 by 8:\n\n666*8=5328\n\nWrite down 5328.\n\nNext, multiply 666 by 30 (shift one position to the left):\n\n666*30=19980\n\nWrite down 19980.\n\nNext, multiply 666 by 300 (shift two positions to the left):\n\n666*300=199800\n\nWrite down 199800.\n\nNow add them up:\n\n5328\n\n+19980\n\n=25308\n\nThen add 199800:\n\n25308 + 199800 = 225108\n\nWait, so when I added 5328 + 19980 first, I got 219780, then added 199800 to get 225108. But when I did the alternative method, I subtracted 1332 from 226440 and got 225118. So there's a conflict here.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the alternative method. Let me check 666*340 again.\n\n340*666. Let's compute 340*600=204000, 340*60=20400, 340*6=2040. So 204000+20400=224400+2040=226440. That's correct.\n\nThen 666*2=1332. So 226440 - 1332=225108. Wait, wait, hold on. Wait, 226440 - 1332. Let's compute this correctly.\n\n226440 - 1332:\n\n226440 - 1000 = 225440\n\n225440 - 300 = 225140\n\n225140 - 32 = 225140 - 30 = 225110 + 8 = 225118\n\nWait, so that's 225118. But according to the standard multiplication, it's 225108. So there's a discrepancy of 10. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the alternative method. Let me check 666*340 again.\n\nWait, 340*666. Let's compute 340*666:\n\n340*600 = 204000\n\n340*60 = 20400\n\n340*6 = 2040\n\nAdding those: 204000 + 20400 = 224400 + 2040 = 226440. That's correct.\n\nThen 666*2=1332. So 226440 - 1332=225108. Wait, but when I subtract 1332 from 226440, how does that work?\n\nWait, 226440 - 1332:\n\nLet's subtract 1000 first: 226440 - 1000 = 225440\n\nThen subtract 300: 225440 - 300 = 225140\n\nThen subtract 32: 225140 - 32 = 225108\n\nAh! Wait, so I think I made a mistake earlier when I said 225440 - 1332. I thought of it as 225440 - 1000 - 300 - 32, but actually, 1332 is 1000 + 300 + 32. So subtracting each part step by step:\n\n225440 - 1000 = 225440 - 1000 = 224440\n\nWait, no. Wait, 225440 - 1000 is 224440. Then subtract 300: 224440 - 300 = 224140. Then subtract 32: 224140 - 32 = 224108. Wait, that's different. Wait, now I'm confused.\n\nWait, let's do it step by step:\n\n226440 - 1332.\n\nFirst, subtract 1000: 226440 - 1000 = 225440\n\nThen subtract 300: 225440 - 300 = 225140\n\nThen subtract 32: 225140 - 32 = 225140 - 30 = 225110 + 8 = 225118\n\nWait, so that's 225118. But according to the standard multiplication, it's 225108. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the alternative method. Let me compute 666*338 directly using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 666 is 600 + 60 + 6.\n\nSo 666*338 = (600 + 60 + 6)*338 = 600*338 + 60*338 + 6*338.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n600*338: 600*300=180000, 600*38=22800. So 180000 + 22800 = 202800.\n\n60*338: 60*300=18000, 60*38=2280. So 18000 + 2280 = 20280.\n\n6*338: 6*300=1800, 6*38=