 400,856\n\nWait, but according to the standard multiplication, the correct answer is 399,856. So there's a discrepancy of 399,856 vs 400,856. That's a difference of 1,000. So where is the mistake here?\n\nLooking at the components:\n\n700*500 = 350,000\n\n700*30 = 21,000\n\n700*6 = 4,200\n\n40*500 = 20,000\n\n40*30 = 1,200\n\n40*6 = 240\n\n6*500 = 3,000\n\n6*30 = 180\n\n6*6 = 36\n\nWait, 700*500 is 350,000. But 700*500 should be 350,000. That's correct. Then 700*30 is 21,000. Correct. 700*6 is 4,200. Correct. \n\n40*500 is 20,000. Correct. 40*30 is 1,200. Correct. 40*6 is 240. Correct. \n\n6*500 is 3,000. Correct. 6*30 is 180. Correct. 6*6 is 36. Correct. \n\nSo all components are correct. Then adding them up step by step:\n\n350,000 + 21,000 = 371,000\n\n371,000 + 4,200 = 375,200\n\n375,200 + 20,000 = 395,200\n\n395,200 + 1,200 = 396,400\n\n396,400 + 240 = 396,640\n\n396,640 + 3,000 = 399,640\n\n399,640 + 180 = 400,820\n\n400,820 + 36 = 400,856\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, the answer is 399,856. So there's a difference of 1,000. Where is this error coming from?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the partial products. Let me check the partial products again. \n\nFirst partial product: 746 * 6. 700*6=4200, 40*6=240, 6*6=36. So 4200+240=4440+36=4476. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 746 * 30. 746*3=2238, then add a zero: 22380. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 746 * 500. 746*5=3730, add two zeros: 373000. Correct.\n\nSo adding 4476 + 22380 + 373000. Let's compute:\n\n4476 + 22380: 4476 + 22380. Let's do 4476 + 20000 = 24476, then +2380 = 24476 + 2380. 24476 + 2000 = 26476, +380 = 26856. Then 26856 + 373000. 26856 + 373000. 26856 + 300000 = 328566, +73000 = 328566 + 73000 = 399,566. Wait, that's different. Wait, 26856 + 373000. Let's compute 373000 + 20000 = 393000, then +6856 = 393000 + 6856 = 399,856. \n\nAh! So I must have miscalculated earlier. When I added 26856 + 373000, I thought it was 399,856. But in my previous breakdown, I added 396,640 + 3,000 + 180 + 36 = 400,856. But according to this, it's 399,856. So where did I go wrong in the breakdown?\n\nWait, let's re-examine the breakdown:\n\nFirst, 700*500 = 350,000\n\n700*30 = 21,000\n\n700*6 = 4,200\n\n40*500 = 20,000\n\n40*30 = 1,200\n\n40*6 = 240\n\n6*500 = 3,000\n\n6*30 = 180\n\n6*6 = 36\n\nAdding these:\n\n350,000 + 21,000 = 371,000\n\n371,000 + 4,200 = 375,200\n\n375,200 + 20,000 = 395,200\n\n395,200 + 1,200 = 396,400\n\n396,400 + 240 = 396,640\n\n396,640 + 3,000 = 399,640\n\n399,640 + 180 = 400,820\n\n400,820 + 36 = 400,856\n\nBut according to the partial products, the correct sum is 399,856. So there's a discrepancy of 1,000. Where is this error?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check each component again:\n\n700*500 = 350,000. Correct.\n\n700*30 = 21,000. Correct.\n\n700*6 = 4,200. Correct.\n\n40*500 = 20,000. Correct.\n\n40*30 = 1,200. Correct.\n\n40*6 = 240. Correct.\n\n6*500 = 3,000. Correct.\n\n6*30 = 180. Correct.\n\n6*6 = 36. Correct.\n\nSo all components are correct. Then why is there a difference?\n\nWait, perhaps I added them in the wrong order. Let me add them again:\n\n350,000 (700*500)\n\n+21,000 (700*30)\n\n= 371,000\n\n+4,200 (700*6)\n\n= 375,200\n\n+20,000 (40*500)\n\n= 395,200\n\n+1,200 (40*30)\n\n= 396,400\n\n+240 (40*6)\n\n= 396,640\n\n+3,000 (6*500)\n\n= 399,640\n\n+180 (6*30)\n\n= 399,820\n\n+36 (6*6)\n\n= 399,856\n\nAh! There we go. I must have added 396,640 + 3,000 as 399,640, but actually, 396,640 + 3,000 is 399,640. Then 399,640 + 180 = 399,820. Then 399,820 + 36 = 399,856. \n\nSo my previous mistake was in the last step where I added 396,640 + 3,000. I incorrectly wrote it as 399,640 instead of 399,640 + 3,000 = 399,640. Wait, no. Wait, 396,640 + 3,000 is 399,640. Then adding 180 gives 399,820, then +36 gives 399,856. \n\nSo the correct total is 399,856, which matches the standard multiplication result. So my initial breakdown had a miscalculation in the last step. \n\nTherefore, both methods give the same result: 399,856. \n\nSo the correct product of 746 and 536 is 399,856. \n\nLet me verify this with another method to be absolutely sure. Maybe using the difference of squares or another algebraic identity. \n\nAlternatively, note that 746 = 700 + 46 and 536 = 500 + 36. Then, using the formula (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd. \n\nSo, (700 + 46)(500 + 36) = 700*500 + 700*36 + 46*500 + 46*36. \n\nCompute each term:\n\n700*500 = 350,000\n\n700*36 = 25,200\n\n46*500 = 23,000\n\n46*36 = 1,656\n\nAdding them up:\n\n350,000 + 25,200 = 375,200\n\n375,200 + 23,000 = 398,200\n\n398,200 + 1,656 = 399,856\n\nSame result. So that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 746 and 536 is 399,856. \n\nI think that's solid. Initially, I made a mistake in the breakdown method by miscalculating the last step, but after correcting that, both methods agree. The standard multiplication also confirms it. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 746 and 536 is \\boxed{399856}.\n"] 43%|████▎     | 217/500 [3:25:38<4:48:46, 61.22s/it]
