 algorithm and verify the result using different methods.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   356 \\\\\n\\times 952 \\\\\n\\hline\n   712 \\quad \\text{(356 \\times 2)} \\\\\n 1780 \\quad \\text{(356 \\times 5, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n 32040 \\quad \\text{(356 \\times 9, shifted two positions to the left)} \\\\\n\\hline\n 338912 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding the partial products:\n- \\(712 + 1780 = 2492\\)\n- \\(2492 + 32040 = 338912\\)\n\nNext, verifying using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n356 \\times 952 = 356 \\times (900 + 50 + 2) = 356 \\times 900 + 356 \\times 50 + 356 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n- \\(356 \\times 900 = 320400\\)\n- \\(356 \\times 50 = 17800\\)\n- \\(356 \\times 2 = 712\\)\n\nAdding these results:\n- \\(320400 + 17800 = 338200\\)\n- \\(338200 + 712 = 338912\\)\n\nAnother verification using the difference of squares method:\n\\[\n356 \\times 952 = 356 \\times (1000 - 48) = 356000 - 356 \\times 48\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(356 \\times 48\\):\n- \\(356 \\times 48 = 300 \\times 48 + 50 \\times 48 + 6 \\times 48 = 14400 + 2400 + 288 = 17088\\)\n\nSubtracting:\n\\[\n356000 - 17088 = 338912\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 356 and 952 is \\(\\boxed{338912}\\).",
