2,740\n\n482,740 + 242 = 482,982\n\nSo the total product is 482,982.\n\nWait, let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 606 by 797:\n\nFirst, multiply 606 by 7:\n\n606 × 7 = 4242\n\nThen, multiply 606 by 90 (since the tens place is 9, which is 9 × 10):\n\n606 × 90 = 606 × 9 × 10 = 5454 × 10 = 54,540\n\nThen, multiply 606 by 700 (since the hundreds place is 7, which is 7 × 100):\n\n606 × 700 = 606 × 7 × 100 = 4242 × 100 = 424,200\n\nNow, add all three results:\n\n424,200 (from 700)\n+\xa0\xa054,540 (from 90)\n+\xa0\xa0\xa0424,2 (from 7)\n--------\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 424,200 + 54,540:\n\n424,200 + 50,000 = 474,200\n\n474,200 + 4,540 = 478,740\n\nThen add 424,2:\n\n478,740 + 424,2 = 903,  wait, 478,740 + 424,200 = 902,940? Wait, no:\n\nWait, 478,740 + 424,200:\n\n478,740 + 400,000 = 878,740\n\n878,740 + 24,200 = 902,940\n\nThen add the remaining 2: 902,940 + 2 = 902,942\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. Wait, so now I get 902,942? But earlier I had 482,982. That's a discrepancy. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, hold on. Let me check again.\n\nWait, in the first method, I had:\n\nFirst partial product: 4242 (606×7)\n\nSecond: 54540 (606×9 shifted left by 1)\n\nThird: 424200 (606×7 shifted left by 2)\n\nAdding them:\n\n424200 + 54540 + 4242\n\nBut 424200 + 54540 is 478,740, then +4242 is 478,740 + 4,242 = 482,982.\n\nBut in the second method, multiplying 606×700=424,200, 606×90=54,540, 606×7=4,242. Then adding 424,200 +54,540 +4,242= 424,200+54,540=478,740 +4,242=482,982. So same result. Wait, but in the second method, when I added 424,200 +54,540 +4,242, I thought 424,200 +54,540 is 478,740, then +4,242 is 482,982. So both methods give 482,982. So why did I think there was a discrepancy? Maybe miscalculation in the second method when I thought 478,740 +424,200. Wait, no, in the second method, the three partial products are 424,200 (700), 54,540 (90), and 4,242 (7). So adding them:\n\n424,200 + 54,540 = 478,740\n\n478,740 + 4,242 = 482,982. So that's correct.\n\nEarlier, when I tried to add 478,740 +424,200, I thought that was 902,940, but that's wrong. Because 478,740 +424,200 is 478,740 +400,000=878,740 +24,200=902,940. But that's not the case here. The three partial products are 424,200; 54,540; and 4,242. So adding them as 424,200 +54,540 +4,242=482,982. So both methods confirm that the product is 482,982.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 482,982.\n\nBut let me verify using another method, perhaps the distributive property.\n\nAlternatively, 606 × 797 can be written as 606 × (800 - 3) = 606 × 800 - 606 × 3.\n\nCalculating 606 × 800:\n\n606 × 8 × 100 = (600 × 8) + (6 × 8) × 100 = 4800 + 48 × 100 = 4800 + 4800 = 9600 × 100 = 960,000.\n\nThen, 606 × 3 = 1,818.\n\nTherefore, 960,000 - 1,818 = 958,182.\n\nWait, that's different from 482,982. Hmm, so now there's a discrepancy. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me check both calculations.\n\nFirst method: 606 × 797 = 482,982.\n\nSecond method: 606 × (800 - 3) = 606 × 800 - 606 × 3 = 960,000 - 1,818 = 958,182.\n\nThese two results are different. That means I made a mistake somewhere. Let's check both.\n\nFirst, let's check 606 × 797.\n\nAlternative approach: Let's use the standard multiplication.\n\nMultiply 606 by 797.\n\nFirst, write 606 × 797:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0606\n×\xa0\xa0797\n--------\n\nMultiply 606 by 7: 4242\n\nMultiply 606 by 9: 5454, shifted left by 1: 54540\n\nMultiply 606 by 7: 4242, shifted left by 2: 424200\n\nAdd them up:\n\n424200\n\n+\xa0\xa054540\n\n+\xa0\xa0\xa04242\n\nLet's add 424200 + 54540 first.\n\n424200 + 54540:\n\n424200 + 50000 = 474200\n\n474200 + 4540 = 478,740\n\nThen add 4242:\n\n478,740 + 4,242 = 482,982.\n\nSo that's correct.\n\nNow, the other method: 606 × 797 = 606 × (800 - 3) = 606 × 800 - 606 × 3.\n\n606 × 800:\n\n606 × 8 = 4848\n\n4848 × 100 = 484,800\n\n606 × 3 = 1,818\n\nSo 484,800 - 1,818 = 482,982.\n\nAh! Wait, I see where I messed up earlier. When I calculated 606 × 800, I did 606 × 8 × 100 = (600 × 8) + (6 × 8) × 100 = 4800 + 48 × 100 = 4800 + 4800 = 9600 × 100 = 960,000. Wait, that's wrong. Wait, 606 × 8 is 4848, not 4800. So that's the mistake.\n\nSo 606 × 800 = 606 × 8 × 100 = 4848 × 100 = 484,800. Then subtract 606 × 3 = 1,818. So 484,800 - 1,818 = 482,982. Which matches the first method. So my initial mistake was in the second method when I miscalculated 606 × 800 as 484,800 versus 960,000. That was incorrect. So both methods give the same result, 482,982. Therefore, the correct answer is 482,982.\n\nAlternatively, let's check using another method, like the difference of squares or something else. But that might be more complicated. Alternatively, use a calculator to verify.\n\nBut since I don't have a calculator here, let's check with another multiplication step.\n\nAlternatively, multiply 606 × 797:\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0606\n×\xa0\xa0797\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 606 by 7:\n\n606\n×\xa0\xa07\n------\n4242\n\nThen, multiply 606 by 90 (since the tens place is 9, which is 9 × 10):\n\n606\n×\xa0\xa090\n------\n54540\n\nThen, multiply 606 by 700 (since the hundreds place is 7, which is 7 × 100):\n\n606\n×\xa0\xa0700\n------\n424200\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n424200\n\n+\xa0\xa054540\n\n+\xa0\xa0\xa04242\n\nLet's add 424200 and 54540 first:\n\n424200 + 54540:\n\n424200 + 50000 = 474200\n\n474200 + 4540 = 478,740\n\nThen add 4242:\n\n478,740 + 4,242 = 482,982\n\nYes, same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 606 and 797 is 482,982.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 606 and 797 is \\boxed{482982}.\n"] 48%|████▊     | 238/500 [3:48:30<4:16:02, 58.64s/it]
