hat 259 is 260 - 1. So, 744 \u00d7 260 - 744 \u00d7 1.\n\nCompute 744 \u00d7 260. Let's break that down:\n\n744 \u00d7 200 = 148,800\n\n744 \u00d7 60 = 44,640\n\nSo, 148,800 + 44,640 = 193,440\n\nThen subtract 744 \u00d7 1 = 744\n\n193,440 - 744 = 192,696. Same result. Perfect.\n\nSo, all methods lead to 192,696. Therefore, the product of 744 and 259 is 192,696.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 744 and 259 is \\boxed{192696}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 744 and 259, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 744 by the rightmost digit (9):\n   \\[\n   744 \\times 9 = 6696\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 744 by the next digit (5), shifting one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   744 \\times 5 = 3720 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position left becomes 37200)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 744 by the next digit (2), shifting another position to the left:\n   \\[\n   744 \\times 2 = 1488 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions left becomes 148800)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of these multiplications:\n   \\[\n   6696 + 37200 + 148800 = 192696\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n- Break down 259 into 200, 50, and 9:\n  \\[\n  744 \\times 200 = 148800\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  744 \\times 50 = 37200\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  744 \\times 9 = 6696\n  \\]\n- Add these results together:\n  \\[\n  148800 + 37200 + 6696 = 192696\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 744 and 259 is \\(\\boxed{192696}\\).",
