u00d78 = 240\n\n3\u00d7100 = 300\n\n3\u00d78 = 24\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n20,000 + 1,600 = 21,600\n\n21,600 + 3,000 = 24,600\n\n24,600 + 240 = 24,840\n\n24,840 + 300 = 25,140\n\n25,140 + 24 = 25,164\n\nSame result! Okay, that's reassuring. So both methods give 25,164. Let me try another check. Maybe using a calculator-like step-by-step multiplication.\n\nMultiplying 233 by 108:\n\nStart with 233 \u00d7 8. As before, 233 \u00d7 8:\n\n200 \u00d7 8 = 1,600\n\n30 \u00d7 8 = 240\n\n3 \u00d7 8 = 24\n\nAdding those: 1,600 + 240 = 1,840; 1,840 + 24 = 1,864. So that's correct.\n\nThen 233 \u00d7 100 is 23,300. Adding 1,864 to 23,300:\n\n23,300 + 1,864. Let's add 23,300 + 1,000 = 24,300; then add 864: 24,300 + 800 = 25,100; 25,100 + 64 = 25,164. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 108 is 100 + 8, so 233*108 = 233*(100 + 8) = 233*100 + 233*8 = 23,300 + 1,864 = 25,164. All methods converge to the same number.\n\nJust to be thorough, maybe do the multiplication vertically:\n\n   233\n\u00d7 108\n-------\n  233 \u00d7 8 = 1,864\n  233 \u00d7 0 = 0\n233 \u00d7 100 = 23,300\n-------\nAdding them up: 1,864 + 0 + 23,300 = 25,164\n\nYep, same result. So I think that's solid. Therefore, the product of 233 and 108 is 25,164.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 233 and 108 is \\boxed{25164}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 233 and 108, we can break down the multiplication into parts and use the distributive property:\n\n1. Calculate \\(233 \\times 100\\):\n   \\[\n   233 \\times 100 = 23300\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(233 \\times 8\\):\n   \\[\n   233 \\times 8 = (200 \\times 8) + (30 \\times 8) + (3 \\times 8) = 1600 + 240 + 24 = 1864\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results from the two calculations:\n   \\[\n   23300 + 1864 = 25164\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by expanding the multiplication:\n\\[\n233 \\times 108 = (200 + 30 + 3) \\times (100 + 8)\n\\]\nExpanding and summing the terms:\n\\[\n200 \\times 100 + 200 \\times 8 + 30 \\times 