 the numbers into their hundreds, tens, and ones components and then multiplying each part separately, then adding all the products together in their respective place values gives the correct result.\n\nTherefore, the correct product of 171 and 271 is 46,341.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 171 and 271 is \\boxed{46341}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 171 and 271, we can break down the numbers into their components and multiply each part separately, then add the results together.\n\nFirst, we express 171 and 271 in terms of their hundreds, tens, and ones components:\n- 171 can be written as \\(100 + 70 + 1\\)\n- 271 can be written as \\(200 + 70 + 1\\)\n\nNext, we multiply each component of 171 by each component of 271:\n- \\(100 \\times 200 = 20000\\)\n- \\(100 \\times 70 = 7000\\)\n- \\(100 \\times 1 = 100\\)\n- \\(70 \\times 200 = 14000\\)\n- \\(70 \\times 70 = 4900\\)\n- \\(70 \\times 1 = 70\\)\n- \\(1 \\times 200 = 200\\)\n- \\(1 \\times 70 = 70\\)\n- \\(1 \\times 1 = 1\\)\n\nNow, we sum these products:\n- Hundreds place: \\(20000 + 7000 + 100 = 27100\\)\n- Tens place: \\(14000 + 4900 + 70 = 18970\\)\n- Ones place: \\(100 + 70 + 1 = 171\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n- \\(27100 + 18970 = 46070\\)\n- \\(46070 + 171 = 46341\\)\n\nThus, the product of 171 and 271 is \\(\\boxed{46341}\\).",
