e the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 122 by the units digit of 126 (6):\n   \\[\n   122 \\times 6 = 732\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 122 by the tens digit of 126 (2), shifting the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   122 \\times 2 = 244 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one position: 2440)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 122 by the hundreds digit of 126 (1), shifting the result two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   122 \\times 1 = 122 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two positions: 12200)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   732 + 2440 + 12200\n   \\]\n\n5. Calculate the sum step-by-step:\n   \\[\n   732 + 2440 = 3172\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3172 + 12200 = 15372\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this result using prime factorization:\n- Prime factors of 122: \\(2 \\times 61\\)\n- Prime factors of 126: \\(2 \\times 3^2 \\times 7\\)\n\nMultiplying these together:\n\\[\n(2 \\times 61) \\times (2 \\times 3^2 \\times 7) = 2^2 \\times 3^2 \\times 61 \\times 7\n\\]\n\nCalculating the constants:\n\\[\n2^2 = 4, \\quad 4 \\times 3^2 = 4 \\times 9 = 36, \\quad 36 \\times 7 = 252\n\\]\n\nMultiplying by 61:\n\\[\n252 \\times 61 = 252 \\times (60 + 1) = 252 \\times 60 + 252 \\times 1 = 15120 + 252 = 15372\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 122 and 126 is \\(\\boxed{15372}\\).",
