any places. Wait, when you multiply by the hundreds digit (9), you need to shift the result two places left. So 376*9=3384, then shift two places: 338400. That's correct. Then, adding 22560 (from tens place) and 338400 (from hundreds place):\n\n22560 + 338400 = 360,960. Then adding the units place 2256 gives 360,960 + 2,256 = 363,216. Wait, but in the standard multiplication, I added 22560 + 225600 + 338400 = 586,560. But according to the distributive method, it's 363,216. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, perhaps in the standard multiplication, I added the three parts incorrectly. Let me check:\n\nFirst part: 22560 (units)\n\nSecond part: 225600 (tens)\n\nThird part: 338400 (hundreds)\n\nAdding them:\n\n22560 + 225600 = 248,160\n\n248,160 + 338,400 = 586,560\n\nBut according to the distributive method, the correct answer is 363,216. Therefore, there's a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check the standard multiplication again.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the standard multiplication by miscalculating the products. Let me verify each multiplication:\n\nFirst, 376 * 6:\n\n376 * 6:\n\n300*6 = 1800\n\n70*6 = 420\n\n6*6 = 36\n\n1800 + 420 = 2220\n\n2220 + 36 = 2256. Correct.\n\nThen, 376 * 60:\n\n376 * 60:\n\n376 * 6 = 2256\n\nThen, shift one place left: 22560. Correct.\n\nThen, 376 * 900:\n\n376 * 900:\n\n376 * 9 = 3384\n\nShift two places left: 338400. Correct.\n\nSo the products are correct. Then, adding them:\n\n22560 + 225600 = 248,160\n\n248,160 + 338,400 = 586,560\n\nBut according to the distributive method, the correct answer is 363,216. Therefore, there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the distributive method. Let me check:\n\n376 * 966 = 376*(900 + 60 + 6) = 376*900 + 376*60 + 376*6.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n376*900:\n\n376 * 900 = 376 * 9 * 100 = 3384 * 100 = 338,400. Correct.\n\n376*60:\n\n376 * 60 = 376 * 6 * 10 = 2256 * 10 = 22,560. Correct.\n\n376*6:\n\n376 * 6 = 2,256. Correct.\n\nAdding t