00 minus 500 is 126,000. Then subtract 6 more: 126,000 - 6 = 125,994. So that seems correct. \n\nNow, checking the second method: 506*9 = 4,554. 506*40 = 2,0240. 506*200 = 101,200. Adding them: 4,554 + 2,0240. Let's do this again. 4,554 + 2,0240. Let's add 4,554 + 2,000 = 6,554. Then add 240: 6,554 + 240. 6,554 + 200 = 6,754; 6,754 + 40 = 6,794. Then add 101,200: 6,794 + 101,200. 6,794 + 100,000 = 106,794; then add 1,200: 106,794 + 1,200 = 107,994. So that's the same as before. \n\nHmm, so both methods give different results. That can't be. There must be an error in one of the methods. Let me check the multiplication steps again.\n\nFirst method: 250*506. 250*500 = 125,000. 250*6 = 1,500. 125,000 + 1,500 = 126,500. Then subtract 506: 126,500 - 506. Let's do this subtraction carefully. 126,500 minus 500 is 126,000. Then subtract 6: 126,000 - 6 = 125,994. That seems correct. \n\nSecond method: 506*9. 506*9: 500*9=4,500; 6*9=54. 4,500 + 54 = 4,554. Correct. \n\n506*40: 506*4=2,024; times 10 is 2,0240. Correct. \n\n506*200: 506*2=1,012; times 100 is 101,200. Correct. \n\nAdding them: 4,554 + 2,0240. Let's do this again. 4,554 + 2,0240. Let's add 4,554 + 2,000 = 6,554. Then add 240: 6,554 + 240. 6,554 + 200 = 6,754; 6,754 + 40 = 6,794. Then add 101,200: 6,794 + 101,200. 6,794 + 100,000 = 106,794; 106,794 + 1,200 = 107,994. \n\nWait, so both methods give different results. That can't be. There must be a miscalculation in one of the steps. Let me check the second method again. \n\nWait, 506*40 is 506*4*10. 506*4: 500*4=2,000; 6*4=24. So 2,000 +24=2,024. Then times 10 is 2,0240. That's correct. \n\n506*200: 506*2=1,012. 1,012*100=101,200. Correct. \n\nSo adding 4,554 + 2,0240. Let's do this in another way. 4,554 + 2,0240. Let's add 4,554 + 2,000 = 6,554. Then add 240: 6,554 + 240. 6,554 + 200 = 6,754; 6,754 + 40 = 6,794. Then add 101,200: 6,794 + 101,200. 6,794 + 100,000 = 106,794; 106,794 + 1,200 = 107,994. \n\nBut according to the first method, the answer is 125,994. So t