368\n\nSo the total is 314368. But earlier, when I thought I added 2608 + 11268 + 314368, I thought that was 328244. Wait, but that's not correct. Wait, 2608 + 11268 is 13876, then 13876 + 314368 is 328244. But that contradicts the other method. So which is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check the partial products again.\n\nFirst partial product: 433 x 6. 400*6=2400, 30*6=180, 3*6=18. 2400+180=2580+18=2608. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 433 x 20. 433 x 2=866, 866 x10=8660. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 433 x 700. 433 x7=3031, 3031 x100=303100. Correct.\n\nSo adding them: 2608 + 8660 + 303100. Let's compute 2608 + 8660 first. 2608 + 8660. Let's do 2608 + 8000 = 10608, then +660 = 11268. Then 11268 + 303100. 11268 + 303100. Let's compute 11268 + 300000 = 311268, then +3100 = 314368. So that's correct. So why did I think it was 328244 before? Because I added 2608 + 11268 + 314368 as if they were separate numbers, but actually, the second partial product is 11268, which is 11,268, not 112,68. Wait, no. Wait, 11268 is 11,268. So when I add 2608 (2,608) + 11,268 + 314,368, that's 2,608 + 11,268 = 13,876; 13,876 + 314,368 = 328,244. Wait, but that's conflicting with the other method. So which is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me check with another method. Let's use the standard algorithm again, but more carefully.\n\nMultiplying 433 by 726:\n\nFirst, write 433 x 6. 433 x 6 = 2608.\n\nThen, write 433 x 20. Since 20 is in the tens place, we shift one position left: 8660.\n\nThen, write 433 x 700. Since 700 is in the hundreds place, shift two positions left: 303100.\n\nNow, adding these three numbers:\n\n2608\n\n 8660\n\n+303100\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 2608 and 8660:\n\n2608 + 8660. Let's compute:\n\n2608 + 8000 = 10608\n\n10608 + 660 = 11268\n\nThen add 303100:\n\n11268 + 303100. Let's compute:\n\n11268 + 300000 = 311268\n\n311268 + 3100 = 314368\n\nSo the total is 314368. But when 