ing to the other method, it's 314,368. There's a discrepancy here. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is a problem. Let me check 433 x 726 using another method. Let's use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 433 by 726:\n\nFirst, write 433 x 6. 433 x 6 = 2,608.\n\nNext, write 433 x 20. Since 20 is in the tens place, shift one position left: 8,660.\n\nThen, write 433 x 700. Since 700 is in the hundreds place, shift two positions left: 303,100.\n\nNow, adding these three numbers:\n\n2,608\n\n 8,660\n\n+303,100\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 2,608 and 8,660:\n\n2,608 + 8,660. Let's compute:\n\n2,608 + 8,000 = 10,608\n\n10,608 + 660 = 11,268\n\nThen add 11,268 + 303,100:\n\n11,268 + 303,100. Let's compute:\n\n11,268 + 300,000 = 311,268\n\n311,268 + 3,100 = 314,368\n\nSo that's 314,368. Therefore, the correct product is 314,368. But when I computed 400x726 + 30x726 + 3x726, I got 313,558. So why is there a discrepancy?\n\nWait, let's compute 400x726, 30x726, and 3x726 separately:\n\n400 x 726 = 400 x 700 + 400 x 26 = 280,000 + 10,400 = 290,400\n\nWait, no. Wait, 400 x 726 = 400 x (700 + 26) = 400 x 700 + 400 x 26 = 280,000 + 10,400 = 290,400\n\n30 x 726 = 30 x 700 + 30 x 26 = 21,000 + 780 = 21,780\n\n3 x 726 = 2,178\n\nAdding them together: 290,400 + 21,780 = 312,180; 312,180 + 2,178 = 314,358. Wait, that's 314,358. But earlier, using the breakdown, we had 314,368. There's a difference of 10. What's going on here?\n\nWait, let's compute 400x726 again. 400 x 726. 726 x 400. 726 x 4 = 2,904. Then add two zeros: 29,0400. Wait, no. 726 x 400 = 726 x 4 x 100 = 2,904 x 100 = 290,400. Correct.\n\n30x726: 30 x 700 = 21,000; 30 x 26 = 780; total 21,780. Correct.\n\n3x726: 2,178. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 290,400 + 21,780 = 312,180; 312,180 + 2,178 = 314,358. But according to the other method, it's 314,368. So there's a difference of 10. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 433 x 726 using the standard multiplication algorithm again, step by step.\n\nFirst, multiply 433 by 6: 2,608.\n\nThen, multiply 433 by 20: 8,660.\n\nThen, multiply 433 by 700: 303,100.\n\nAdding them: 2,608 + 8,660 = 11,268; 11,268 + 303,100 = 314,368.\n\nBut when I compute 400x726 + 30x726 + 3x726, I get 314,358. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 433 x 726 directly using the standard multiplication steps.\n\n      433\n    x 726\n    -------\n\nStart with the rightmost digit: 6.\n\n433 x 6 = 2,608. Write down 2,608.\n\nNext digit: 2. Since it's the tens place, shift one position left and multiply: 433 x 20 = 8,660. Write down 8,660.\n\nNext digit: 7. Multiply: 433 x 700 = 303,100. Write down 303,100.\n\nNow, add the three partial products:\n\n2,608\n\n 8,660\n\n+303,100\n\nLet's add 2,608 + 8,660 first. 2,608 + 8,660 = 11,268.\n\nThen add 11,268 + 303,100 = 314,368.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 314,368. So why does the other method give 314,358? Because when I computed 400x726 + 30x726 + 3x726, I must have made a mistake.\n\nWait, let's compute 400x726 again. 400 x 726. 726 x 4 = 2,904. 2,904 x 100 = 290,400. Correct.\n\n30x726: 30 x 700 = 21,000; 30 x 26 = 780. 21,000 + 780 = 21,780. Correct.\n\n3x726: 2,178. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 290,400 + 21,780 = 312,180. Then 312,180 + 2,178 = 314,358. But according to the other method, it's 314,368. So there's a discrepancy of 10. Where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's compute 433 x 726 using another method. Let's use the fact that 726 = 700 + 20 + 6, so:\n\n433 x 700 = 303,100\n\n433 x 20 = 8,660\n\n433 x 6 = 2,608\n\nAdding them: 303,100 + 8,660 = 311,760; 311,760 + 2,608 = 314,368. So that's correct.\n\nBut when I compute 400x726 + 30x726 + 3x726, I get 314,358. So why is there a difference?\n\nWait, let's compute 400x726 + 30x726 + 3x726:\n\n400x726 = 290,400\n\n30x726 = 21,780\n\n3x726 = 2,178\n\nTotal: 290,400 + 21,780 = 312,180; 312,180 + 2,178 = 314,358.\n\nBut according to the other method, it's 314,368. So there's a difference of 10. Which one is 