sands is 3000, 13 hundreds is 1300, 1 ten is 10, 16 ones is 16. Adding those together: 3000 + 1300 = 4300, 4300 + 10 = 4310, 4310 + 16 = 4326. Okay, that's correct.\n\nThen, adding 5562 to 4326:\n\n4326 + 5562.\n\nThousands: 4 + 5 = 9\n\nHundreds: 3 + 5 = 8\n\nTens: 2 + 6 = 8\n\nOnes: 6 + 2 = 8\n\nSo, 9 thousands, 8 hundreds, 8 tens, 8 ones. Which is 9888. That seems right.\n\nWait, but let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property or another multiplication technique.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the lattice method. But that might be more complicated. Alternatively, check using a calculator if I have access. But since I don't, let me try another way.\n\nAlternatively, maybe break down 618 into 600 + 18. Then multiply each by 961 and add the results.\n\nSo, 618 \u00d7 961 = (600 + 18) \u00d7 961 = 600\u00d7961 + 18\u00d7961.\n\nCalculate 600\u00d7961. 600\u00d7961 = 6\u00d7100\u00d7961 = 6\u00d796100. Let's compute 6\u00d796100. 96100 \u00d7 6: 90000\u00d76=540000, 6000\u00d76=36000, 100\u00d76=600. So, 540000 + 36000 = 576000, plus 600 is 576600. So, 600\u00d7961 = 576600.\n\nNow, 18\u00d7961. Let's compute that. 10\u00d7961 = 9610, 8\u00d7961. 8\u00d7900=7200, 8\u00d761=488. So, 7200 + 488 = 7688. Then, 9610 + 7688. 9610 + 7000 = 16610, 16610 + 688 = 17298. So, 18\u00d7961 = 17298.\n\nNow, add 576600 + 17298. Let's do that:\n\n576600 + 17298.\n\nStart with 576600 + 10000 = 676600\n\nThen, 676600 + 7000 = 746600\n\nThen, 746600 + 298 = 746600 + 200 = 746800, then subtract 2: 746800 - 2 = 746798.\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result of 9888. Wait, that can't be. Wait, hold on, this is a problem. If I use two different methods, I get two different results, which means I must have made a mistake somewhere.\n\nWait, first method gave me 9888, second method gave me 746798. That's a huge discrepancy. So, clearly, I messed up somewhere. Let me check both calculations again.\n\nFirst method:\n\n618 \u00d7 961.\n\nFirst line: 618 \u00d7 1 = 618\n\nSecond line: 618 \u00d7 6 = 3708\n\nThird line: 618 \u00d7 9 = 5562\n\nAdding them: 618 + 3708 = 4326; 4326 + 5562 = 9888.\n\nSecond method:\n\nBreaking 618 into 600 + 18.\n\n600 \u00d7 961 = 576600\n\n18 \u00d7 961 = 17298\n\n576600 + 17298 = 746798.\n\nWait, so which one is correct? Let's check with another method. Let's use the standard multiplication again, but more carefully.\n\nAlternative approach:\n\nMultiply 618 by 961.\n\nStart with the units digit of 961, which is 1. Multiply 618 by 1: 618.\n\nBring down the next digit, which is 6. Multiply 618 by 6: 618 \u00d7 6. Let's compute that again. 600 \u00d7 6 = 3600, 18 \u00d7 6 = 108. 3600 + 108 = 3708. So, that's correct.\n\nBring down the next digit, which is 9. Multiply 618 by 9: 600 \u00d7 9 = 5400, 18 \u00d7 9 = 162. 5400 + 162 = 5562. Correct.\n\nSo, adding 618 + 3708 + 5562. Let's do this again:\n\n618 + 3708:\n\n618 + 3708. Let's add 618 + 3700 first, which is 4318, then add 8: 4318 + 8 = 4326. Then 4326 + 5562:\n\n4326 + 5562. Let's add 4326 + 5000 = 9326, then add 562: 9326 + 562 = 9888. So, that's correct. So why does the second method give 746798?\n\nWait, in the second method, when I broke down 618 into 600 + 18, then multiplied each by 961 and added. Let's check each step again.\n\nFirst, 600 \u00d7 961. 600 \u00d7 961. 600 is 6 \u00d7 100. So, 6 \u00d7 961 = 5766. Then, 5766 \u00d7 100 = 576600. That's correct.\n\nThen, 18 \u00d7 961. Let's compute 18 \u00d7 961. 10 \u00d7 961 = 9610, 8 \u00d7 961. 8 \u00d7 900 = 7200, 8 \u00d7 61 = 488. So, 7200 + 488 = 7688. Then, 9610 + 7688. 9610 + 7000 = 16610, 16610 + 688 = 17298. So, 18 \u00d7 961 = 17298. Then, 576600 + 17298. Let's compute that again.\n\n576600 + 17298:\n\n576600 + 10000 = 676600\n\n676600 + 7000 = 746600\n\n746600 + 298 = 746600 + 200 = 746800\n\n746800 - 2 = 746798.\n\nWait, but according to the first method, the correct answer is 9888. So, there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I m