carry) = 11, carry over 1. Then 8 + 3 + 1 = 12, carry over 1. Then 2 + 6 + 1 = 9. So the sum is 92106. Hmm, that seems right.\n\nBut let me cross-verify using another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the distributive property or another multiplication technique.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step again, but more carefully.\n\nLet me write it out again:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0903\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0732\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 903 by 2 (units place):\n\n903 \u00d7 2 = 1806\n\nNext, multiply 903 by 3 (tens place), shifted one position to the left:\n\n903 \u00d7 3 = 2709, shifted left by 1: 27090\n\nThen, multiply 903 by 7 (hundreds place), shifted two positions to the left:\n\n903 \u00d7 7 = 6321, shifted left by 2: 63210\n\nNow, adding them up:\n\n1806\n+27090\n-------\n28896\n\n28896\n+63210\n-------\n92106\n\nYes, same result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another method. For example, breaking down 732 into 700 + 30 + 2.\n\nSo, 903 \u00d7 700 = 903 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 100 = 6321 \u00d7 100 = 632100\n\nThen, 903 \u00d7 30 = 903 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 10 = 2709 \u00d7 10 = 27090\n\nThen, 903 \u00d7 2 = 1806\n\nAdding those together: 632100 + 27090 = 659190; then 659190 + 1806 = 660, 996? Wait, wait, let me compute that again.\n\nWait, 632100 + 27090. Let's do 632100 + 20000 = 652100, then +7090 = 652100 + 7090 = 659,190. Then add 1806: 659,190 + 1,806. Let's break it down: 659,190 + 1,000 = 660,190; 660,190 + 806 = 660,996. So total is 660,996. Wait, but earlier I got 92,106. That's way different. Wait, that can't be. There must be a mistake here.\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, 903 \u00d7 700 is 903 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 100. 903 \u00d7 7: 900 \u00d77=6300, 3\u00d77=21, so 6300+21=6321. Then 6321 \u00d7100=632,100. That's correct.\n\nThen 903 \u00d730: 903 \u00d73=2709, then \u00d710=27,090. Correct.\n\nThen 903 \u00d72=1,806. Correct.\n\nSo adding 632,100 +27,090=659,190. Then 659,190 +1,806=660,996. But earlier, when I added the partial products, I got 92,106. That's conflicting. So clearly, there's a mistake here. Wait, why the discrepancy?\n\nWait, no. Wait, when I did the partial products, I added 1806 (units place) +27090 (tens place) +63210 (hundreds place). But when I broke down 732 into 700+30+2, I multiplied each by 903 and then added. But in the partial product method, the hundreds place is shifted two positions, so 63210 is actually 632100 when shifted two places? Wait, no. Wait, in the partial product method, when you shift left by two, you multiply by 100, so 903 \u00d77 is 6321, then shifted two places becomes 632100. But in the partial product addition, when you add 63210 (which is 6321 shifted two places) to 28896 (shifted one place), you get 63210 + 27090 = 88,300? Wait, no, that's not right. Wait, maybe I confused the shifting.\n\nWait, perhaps the confusion is arising from how the partial products are shifted. Let me clarify.\n\nIn the standard multiplication algorithm, when you multiply by the units digit (2), you get the first partial product (1806). Then, when you multiply by the tens digit (3), you shift the partial product one place to the left (2709 becomes 27090). Then, multiplying by the hundreds digit (7), you shift it two places to the left (6321 becomes 632100). Therefore, when adding the partial products, you have:\n\n1806 (units)\n+27090 (tens)\n+632100 (hundreds)\n\nSo adding these together:\n\n1806 + 27090 = 28896\n\n28896 + 632100 = 660,996\n\nAh! So that's where the 660,996 comes from. But earlier, when I broke down 732 into 700+30+2, I got 660,996. So that's correct. But when I first thought I added 632100 +27090 +1806, I must have miscalculated. Wait, no. Wait, 632100 +27090 is 659,190, then +1806 is 660,996. So that's correct. So the correct total is 660,996. But in my first calculation, I thought I added 1806 +27090 +63210 and got 92,106, which is wrong. So that was a mistake in adding the partial products. So the correct sum is 660,996.\n\nTherefore, the product of 903 and 732 is 660,996.\n\nWait, but let me confirm this with another method. Maybe using the standard algorithm again, but more carefully.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0903\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0732\n--------\n\u00a0\u00a01806\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0(903 \u00d7 2)\n\u00a0\u00a027090\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0(903 \u00d7 30, shifted one left)\n\u00a0\u00a0632100\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0(903 \u00d7 700, shifted two left)\n--------\n\u00a0\u00a0660996\n\nYes, that's correct. So adding 1806 +27090 +632100 gives 660,996. Therefore, the correct product is 660,996.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach, like the lattice method, but that might be more complicated. Alternatively, use a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, let me try another multiplication step.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 903 \u00d7 732 using another breakdown. For example, 903 \u00d7 700 = 632,100; 903 \u00d7 30 = 27,090; 903 \u00d7 2 = 1,806. Then add them up: 632,100 +27,090 = 659,190; 659,190 +1,806 = 660,996. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 903 is 900 +3. So 900 \u00d7732 = 658,800; 3 \u00d7732 = 2,196; then 658,800 +2,196 = 660,996. That's another way to compute it. So that also gives 660,996. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 903 and 732 is 660,996.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 903 and 732 is \\boxed{660996}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 903 and 732, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and break down the multiplication into partial products:\n\n1. Multiply 903 by the units digit (2) of 732:\n   \\[\n   903 \\times 2 = 1806\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 903 by the tens digit (3) of 732, shifted one place to the left:\n   \\[\n   903 \\times 3 = 2709 \\quad \\text{Shifted left by 1:} \\quad 27090\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 903 by the hundreds digit (7) of 732, shifted two places to the left:\n   \\[\n   903 \\times 7 = 6321 \\quad \\text{Shifted left by 2:} \\quad 632100\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   1806 + 27090 + 632100\n   \\]\n\n5. Perform the addition step-by-step:\n   - First, add 1806 and 27090:\n     \\[\n     1806 + 27090 = 28896\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to 632100:\n     \\[\n     28896 + 632100 = 660996\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 903 and 732 is \\(\\boxed{660996}\\).",
