ute 40*13=520 and 8*13=104, so 520+104=624\n\nNow add all together: 40,000 + 1,300 = 41,300; 41,300 + 19,200 = 60,500; 60,500 + 624 = 61,124. Same result again! Wow, three different methods all leading to 61,124. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, but I can check with another multiplication step.\n\nWait, let's check 148*413. Let's do it digit by digit.\n\nMultiplying 148 by 413:\n\nFirst, write 148\n\nMultiply by 3:\n\n148*3 = 444\n\nMultiply by 10 (shift one position left):\n\n148*10 = 1480\n\nMultiply by 400 (shift two positions left):\n\n148*400 = 59,200\n\nAdd them up:\n\n444\n\n1480\n\n59200\n\nAdding:\n\n444 + 1480 = 1924\n\n1924 + 59200 = 61,124\n\nSame result. So all methods converge to 61,124. Therefore, I can be confident that the product is indeed 61,124.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 148 and 413 is \\boxed{61124}.\n"] 59%|█████▉    | 297/500 [4:42:18<1:56:21, 34.39s/it]
