en +160 = 741960. Then add 916: 741960 + 916 = 742876. So same result. Okay, that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method. Let's try multiplying 916 × 811 using the standard algorithm again, but more carefully.\n\nSet it up:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0916\n×\xa0\xa0811\n--------\n\nStart with the rightmost digit of 811, which is 1. Multiply 916 by 1: 916. Write that down.\n\nNext digit: 1 (tens place). Multiply 916 by 10: 9160. Write that next to the previous partial product, shifted one position to the left (but since we're adding, we can just add it as is).\n\nNext digit: 8 (hundreds place). Multiply 916 by 800: 732800. Write that next to the previous partial products, shifted two positions to the left.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\nFirst partial product: 916\n\nSecond partial product: 9160\n\nThird partial product: 732800\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart with 916 + 9160 = 10076\n\nThen 10076 + 732800 = 742876\n\nYes, same result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, let me check with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, use the fact that 916 × 800 = 732800, as before. Then 916 × 11 = 916 + 9160 = 10076. Then 732800 + 10076 = 742876. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication step-by-step:\n\nMultiply 916 by 811:\n\nFirst, multiply 916 by 1: 916\n\nThen, multiply 916 by 10: 9160\n\nThen, multiply 916 by 800: 732800\n\nAdd them up: 916 + 9160 = 10076; 10076 + 732800 = 742876.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm with more attention to place values.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0916\n×\xa0\xa0811\n--------\n\xa0\xa0916\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0(916 × 1)\n\xa0\xa09160\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0(916 × 10)\n\xa0732800\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0(916 × 800)\n--------\n\xa0\xa0742876\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So adding those gives 742876.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the lattice method? But that might be more complicated. Alternatively, use the difference of squares or other algebraic identities, but since these numbers aren't obviously related, that might not help.\n\nAlternatively, check the multiplication using another method. Let's try multiplying 916 × 811 by expanding 811 as (800 + 10 + 1) and then compute each term:\n\n916 × 800 = 916 × 8 × 100 = 7328 × 100 = 732800\n\n916 × 10 = 9160\n\n916 × 1 = 916\n\nAdding them: 732800 + 9160 = 741960; 741960 + 916 = 742876. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm with partial products:\n\nFirst, multiply 916 by 1: 916\n\nThen, multiply 916 by 10 (shifted one position left): 9160\n\nThen, multiply 916 by 800 (shifted two positions left): 732800\n\nAdding them:\n\n916\n\n+9160\n\n+732800\n\n= 742876\n\nYes, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication step-by-step:\n\nStart with 916\n\nMultiply by 811:\n\nFirst, multiply 916 by 1: 916\n\nThen, multiply 916 by 1 (tens place): 9160\n\nThen, multiply 916 by 8 (hundreds place): 732800\n\nAdd them up: 916 + 9160 = 10076; 10076 + 732800 = 742876.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 916 × 811 = 916 × (800 + 10 + 1) = 916×800 + 916×10 + 916×1 = 732800 + 9160 + 916 = 732800 + 9160 = 741960; 741960 + 916 = 742876.\n\nAll methods lead to the same result. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 916 and 811 is 742,876.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 916 and 811 is \\boxed{742876}.\n"]
