n106200 + 30000 = 136200\n\n136200 + 1860 = 138,060\n\nWait, 106200 + 31860:\n\n106200 + 30000 = 136200\n\n136200 + 1860 = 138,060. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow, add 2655 to 138,060.\n\n138,060 + 2000 = 140,060\n\n140,060 + 655 = 140,715\n\nSo, the total is 140,715. Let me check if that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can verify using another method. Let's try the standard multiplication algorithm again to cross-check.\n\nMultiplying 531 by 265:\n\nFirst, write 531 \u00d7 265.\n\nStart with the units digit of 265, which is 5. Multiply 531 by 5:\n\n531\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a05\n------\n\u00a02655\n\nThen, multiply 531 by the tens digit, which is 6, but since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left:\n\n531\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a060\n------\n31860\n\nThen, multiply 531 by the hundreds digit, which is 2, shift two positions to the left:\n\n531\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0200\n------\n106200\n\nNow, add them up:\n\nFirst, 2655 (units place)\n+31860 (tens place)\n+106200 (hundreds place)\n------\nLet's add 2655 + 31860 first.\n\n2655 + 31860:\n\n2655 + 30000 = 32655\n\n32655 + 1860 = 34515\n\nThen add 106200 to 34515:\n\n34515 + 106200 = 140,715\n\nSame result. Okay, that seems consistent. So the product is 140,715.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, maybe I can check using another method. Let's try using the difference of squares or something else. Hmm, not sure. Alternatively, maybe approximate the numbers to check.\n\n531 is approximately 500, and 265 is approximately 250. 500 \u00d7 250 = 125,000. The actual answer is 140,715, which is higher, so that makes sense. The difference is 140,715 - 125,000 = 15,715. So, the exact calculation seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another multiplication technique. Let's try multiplying 531 by 265 using the lattice method. Hmm, that might be a bit involved, but let's try.\n\nFirst, write 531 \u00d7 265. The lattice method involves creating a grid with the multiplicands and multiplicdands, but since I can't draw here, I'll try t