der of operations. Let me go back to the standard multiplication step-by-step.\n\nOriginal problem: 664 \u00d7 988.\n\nSet it up as:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0664\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0988\n--------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (8):\n\nFirst, multiply 664 by 8: 664 \u00d7 8 = 5,328. Write down 5,328.\n\nNext, multiply 664 by the next digit (8 in the tens place), but since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left. So, 5,328 becomes 53,280.\n\nThen, multiply 664 by the hundreds digit (9 in the hundreds place), shift two positions to the left: 5,328 becomes 532,800.\n\nNow, add all three partial products:\n\n5,328 (ones place)\n+53,280 (tens place shifted)\n+532,800 (hundreds place shifted)\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 5,328 + 53,280:\n\n5,328 + 53,280. Let's add 5,000 + 53,000 = 58,000. Then 328 + 280 = 608. So total is 58,000 + 608 = 58,608.\n\nThen add 532,800 to 58,608:\n\n58,608 + 532,800. Let's break it down:\n\n58,608 + 500,000 = 558,608\n\n558,608 + 32,800 = 591,408.\n\nOkay, so that gives 591,408. But when I used the distributive property, I got 656,032. So there's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check the distributive method again. 664 \u00d7 988 = 664 \u00d7 (1000 - 12) = 664,000 - 7,968 = 656,032. But the standard multiplication gave 591,408. These two results are different. Therefore, one of the methods must be wrong.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in one of the methods. Let's check the distributive method first.\n\n664 \u00d7 1000 is indeed 664,000. Then 664 \u00d7 12: 664 \u00d7 10 is 6,640; 664 \u00d7 2 is 1,328. Adding those gives 6,640 + 1,328 = 7,968. Then subtracting 7,968 from 664,000: 664,000 - 7,968. Let's compute that.\n\n664,000 - 7,000 = 657,000\n\n657,000 - 968 = 656,032. So that seems correct.\n\nBut the standard multiplication gave 591,408. Let's check that again.\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the standard multiplication steps. Let me go through it again.\n\nMultiplying 664 by 988