rent results. That can't be. There must be a mistake in one of the methods. Let's check with actual multiplication.\n\nLet me compute 664 \u00d7 988 using another method, perhaps the lattice method or by expanding the numbers.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the fact that 988 is 1000 - 12, but let's verify the distributive method again.\n\nWait, 664 \u00d7 988 = 664 \u00d7 (1000 - 12) = 664,000 - 664 \u00d7 12. That's correct.\n\nBut 664 \u00d7 12: 664 \u00d7 10 is 6,640; 664 \u00d7 2 is 1,328. So 6,640 + 1,328 = 7,968. Then 664,000 - 7,968 = 656,032. So that's correct.\n\nBut the standard multiplication gave 591,408. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 664 \u00d7 988 directly.\n\nLet me do it step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 664 by 8:\n\n664 \u00d7 8:\n\n4 \u00d7 8 = 32, write 2, carry 3.\n\n6 \u00d7 8 = 48 + 3 = 51, write 1, carry 5.\n\n6 \u00d7 8 = 48 + 5 = 53, write 53. So 5328. Correct.\n\nThen, multiply 664 by 80 (tens place):\n\n664 \u00d7 8 = 5328, then shift left by one: 53280. Correct.\n\nMultiply 664 by 900 (hundreds place):\n\n664 \u00d7 9 = 5976, shift left by two: 597600. Correct.\n\nNow, adding 5328 + 53280 + 597600.\n\nFirst, 5328 + 53280:\n\n5328 + 53280. Let's add 53280 + 5000 = 58280, then +328 = 58608. Correct.\n\nThen 58608 + 597600:\n\n58608 + 597600. Let's add 500000 + 50000 = 550000, then 8608 + 97600 = 106,208. Then total is 550,000 + 106,208 = 656,208. Wait, hold on, that's different from before. Wait, no, wait:\n\nWait, 58608 + 597600. Let's do it properly:\n\n58,608 + 597,600.\n\n58,608 + 500,000 = 558,608\n\n558,608 + 97,600 = 558,608 + 90,000 = 648,608; 648,608 + 7,600 = 656,208.\n\nWait, so that's 656,208. But earlier, I thought it was 591,408. Wait, so where did I go wrong before?\n\nAh! I see. In the initial addition step, I incorrectly added 532,800 + 597,600 as 1,130,400. That's wrong. Let's do it correctly:\n\n532,800 + 597,600:\n\n532,800 + 500,000 = 1,032,800\n\n1,032,800 + 97,600 = 1,130,400. Wait, that's the same