e leftmost digit is 8, which is in the hundreds place. So, we take the previous result (5106) and multiply it by 8, then shift left by two places because there are two digits to the left of the 8 in the original number. Wait, actually, in the multiplication algorithm, each subsequent digit you multiply is shifted left by one more position. So, the first digit (6) is shifted left by 0 positions, the second digit (1) is shifted left by 1 position, and the third digit (8) is shifted left by 2 positions. Therefore, after multiplying 851 by 8, we need to shift the result two places to the left.\n\nLet me compute 851 × 8 first. Breaking it down:\n\n- 800 × 8 = 6400\n- 50 × 8 = 400\n- 1 × 8 = 8\n\nAdding those: 6400 + 400 = 6800, then 6800 + 8 = 6808. So, 851 × 8 = 6808. Now, shifting this two places to the left would be 680800.\n\nNow, adding all three results together: 5106 (from the units place) + 51060 (from the tens place) + 680800 (from the hundreds place). Let me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 5106 and 51060. Let's see:\n\n5106\n+51060\n------\n56166\n\nWait, let me check that again. 5106 + 51060. Let's align them:\n\n\xa0\xa05106\n+51060\n--------\n\xa056166\n\nYes, that's correct. So, 5106 + 51060 = 56166.\n\nNow, add 680800 to 56166. Let's do that:\n\n\xa0\xa056166\n+680800\n----------\n\xa0736,966\n\nWait, let me verify that addition. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digits:\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\nThen the remaining digits: 736,966. Hmm, let me check:\n\n56166 + 680800. Let's break it down:\n\n56166 + 60000 = 116166\n\n116166 + 8000 = 124166\n\n124166 + 800 = 124966\n\n124966 + 6 = 124972\n\nWait, that doesn't match. Hmm, maybe I made a mistake in the addition. Let me try again.\n\n56166 + 680800. Let's add the numbers:\n\n680800\n+\xa056166\n----------\nLet's add them step by step:\n\n680800 + 50,000 = 730,800\n\n730,800 + 6,000 = 736,800\n\n736,800 + 166 = 736,966\n\nYes, that's correct. So, the total is 736,966.\n\nTherefore, the product of 851 and 816 is 736,966.\n\nWait, let me cross-verify this result using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the distributive property or another multiplication technique.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the standard multiplication algorithm again but more carefully.\n\nLet me write it out again:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0851\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0×\xa0\xa0816\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0----------\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa05106\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0(851 × 6)\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0+51060\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0(851 × 1, shifted one position left)\n\xa0\xa0\xa0+680800\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0(851 × 8, shifted two positions left)\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0------------\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0736,966\n\nYes, that's the same result. Alternatively, maybe I can use another approach. Let's try breaking down 816 into 800 + 16.\n\nSo, 851 × 800 + 851 × 16.\n\nCompute 851 × 800 first. 851 × 8 = 6808, so 6808 × 100 = 680,800.\n\nThen compute 851 × 16. Let's break that down:\n\n851 × 10 = 8,510\n\n851 × 6 = 5,106\n\nAdding those together: 8,510 + 5,106 = 13,616.\n\nNow, add 680,800 + 13,616. Let's do that:\n\n680,800 + 10,000 = 690,800\n\n690,800 + 3,000 = 693,800\n\n693,800 + 616 = 694,416\n\nWait, that's different. Wait, hold on. Wait, 851 × 16 is 13,616. So, adding 680,800 + 13,616:\n\n680,800 + 13,616:\n\n680,800 + 10,000 = 690,800\n\n690,800 + 3,000 = 693,800\n\n693,800 + 600 = 694,400\n\n694,400 + 16 = 694,416\n\nWait, so that gives 694,416. But earlier, when I did the standard multiplication, I got 736,966. That's a discrepancy. Which one is correct?\n\nHmm, so there's a problem here. Which method is correct? Let me check my calculations again.\n\nFirst method:\n\n851 × 816 = 736,966\n\nSecond method:\n\n851 × 800 = 680,800\n\n851 × 16 = 13,616\n\nTotal: 680,800 + 13,616 = 694,416\n\nBut these two results are different. That means I made a mistake somewhere. Let me check both methods again.\n\nFirst method:\n\nMultiplying 851 by 6 gives 5106\n