arts:**\n   - Multiply 720 by 600.\n   - Multiply 720 by 20.\n   - Multiply 720 by 6.\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**\n   - \\( 720 \\times 600 = 432000 \\)\n   - \\( 720 \\times 20 = 14400 \\)\n   - \\( 720 \\times 6 = 4320 \\)\n\n3. **Sum the results of each part:**\n   - \\( 432000 + 14400 = 446400 \\)\n   - \\( 446400 + 4320 = 450720 \\)\n\n4. **Verification using vertical multiplication:**\n   - Write 720 and 626 in a vertical multiplication format.\n   - Multiply 720 by each digit of 626 (6, 2, 6) and shift appropriately.\n   - Sum the partial products:\n     - \\( 432000 \\)\n     - \\( 14400 \\)\n     - \\( 4320 \\)\n   - Adding these together gives \\( 432000 + 14400 + 4320 = 450720 \\).\n\n5. **Verification using lattice method:**\n   - Construct a 3x3 grid for the multiplicands 720 and 626.\n   - Multiply each row and column digit and sum the diagonals.\n   - The result matches the previous calculations.\n\nAfter verifying through multiple methods, the product of 720 and 626 is confirmed to be:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{450720}\n\\]",
