output:  ['\n\nTo find the product of 379 and 418, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 379 by the units digit (8) of 418:\n   \\[\n   379 \\times 8 = 3032\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 379 by the tens digit (1) of 418, shifted one place to the left (adding a zero):\n   \\[\n   379 \\times 10 = 3790\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 379 by the hundreds digit (4) of 418, shifted two places to the left (adding two zeros):\n   \\[\n   379 \\times 400 = 151600\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   3032 + 3790 + 151600\n   \\]\n\n5. Break down the addition step-by-step:\n   - First, add 3032 and 3790:\n     \\[\n     3032 + 3790 = 6822\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to 151600:\n     \\[\n     6822 + 151600 = 158422\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 379 and 418 is \\(\\boxed{158422}\\).', '\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 379 and 418. Hmm, let\'s see. I remember that multiplying two-digit numbers can be done by breaking them down into parts. Maybe I can use the method where you multiply each number by the tens place and then the units place separately, and then add them together. Let me try that.\n\nFirst, let\'s write down the numbers: 379 and 418. Both are three-digit numbers. Let me break them into their hundreds, tens, and units. So, 379 is 3 hundreds, 7 tens, and 9 units. Similarly, 418 is 4 hundreds, 1 ten, and 8 units.\n\nThe method I remember is called the "lattice method" or maybe the "distribute" method. Let me recall. If I have two numbers, say (a + b + c) and (d + e + f), then their product is (ad + ae + af + bd + be + bf + cd + ce + cf). Wait, that seems like a lot of terms. Maybe there\'s a simpler way.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Let\'s try that. Multiply 379 by 418. Let\'s start by multiplying 379 by 8 (the units digit of 418), then 379 by 10 (the tens digit, which is 1 multiplied by 10), and then 379 by 400 (the hundreds digit, which is 4 multiplied by 100). Then add all those results together.\n\nLet me write that out step by step.\n\nFirst, multiply 379 by 8:\n\n379\n×\xa0\xa0\xa08\n------\n3032 (since 379 × 8: 9×8=72, carryover 7; 7×8=56 +7=63, carryover 6; 3×8=24 +6=30. So 3032)\n\nNext, multiply 379 by 10:\n\n379\n×\xa0\xa010\n------\n3790 (just add a zero at the end: 379 × 10 = 3790)\n\nThen, multiply 379 by 400:\n\n379\n×\xa0400\n------\n151600 (379 × 4 = 1516, then add two zeros: 151600)\n\nNow, add all three results together:\n\n3032 (units place)\n+3790 (tens place)\n+151600 (hundreds place)\n----------\nLet\'s add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 3032 and 3790:\n\n3032 + 3790. Let\'s break it down:\n\n3000 + 3700 = 6700\n\n32 + 90 = 122\n\nSo total is 6700 + 122 = 6822\n\nThen add 151600 to 6822:\n\n151600 + 6822. Let\'s break it down:\n\n151600 + 6000 = 211600\n\n211600 + 822 = 212422\n\nWait, is that right? Let me check again.\n\nWait, 151600 + 6822:\n\n151600 + 6000 = 211600\n\n211600 + 800 = 212400\n\n212400 + 22 = 212422\n\nYes, that\'s correct. So the total product is 212,422.\n\nBut let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn\'t make a mistake. Maybe using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property in a different way. Let\'s see.\n\n379 × 418 can be written as (300 + 70 + 9) × (400 + 10 + 8). Then, expanding this:\n\n300×400 + 300×10 + 300×8 + 70×400 + 70×10 + 70×8 + 9×400 + 9×10 + 9×8\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n300×400 = 120,000\n\n300×10 = 3,000\n\n300×8 = 2,400\n\n70×400 = 28,000\n\n70×10 = 700\n\n70×8 = 560\n\n9×400 = 3,600\n\n9×10 = 90\n\n9×8 = 72\n\nNow, add all these together:\n\n120,000 + 3,000 = 123,000\n\n123,000 + 2,400 = 125,400\n\n125,400 + 28,000 = 153,400\n\n153,400 + 700 = 154,100\n\n154,100 + 560 = 154,660\n\n154,660 + 3,600 = 158,260\n\n158,260 + 90 = 158,350\n\n158,350 + 72 = 158,422\n\nWait, that\'s 158,422. But earlier, using the standard multiplication method, I got 212,422. These two results are different. That means I made a mistake somewhere. Let me check both methods again.\n\nFirst, the standard multiplication method:\n\n379 × 418.\n\nLet me do it step by step.\n\nMultiply 379 by 8:\n\n379 × 8:\n\nUnits place: 9 × 8 = 72, write down 2, carryover 7.\n\nTens place: 7 × 8 = 56 + 7 (carryover) = 63, write down 3, carryover 6.\n\nHundreds place: 3 × 8 = 24 + 6 (carryover) = 30, write down 30.\n\nSo 3032. That seems correct.\n\nThen 379 × 10:\n\n379 × 10 is 3790. Correct.\n\nThen 379 × 400:\n\n379 × 4 = 1516, then add two zeros: 151600. Correct.\n\nAdding 3032 + 3790 + 151600.\n\n3032 + 3790:\n\n3032 + 3000 = 6032\n\n6032 + 790 = 6822. Correct.\n\n6822 + 151600:\n\n6822 + 150000 = 156822\n\n156822 + 1600 = 158422. Wait, hold on. Wait, 151600 is 151,600. So adding 6822 + 151,600.\n\n6822 + 151,600:\n\n6822 + 150,000 = 218,222\n\n218,222 + 1,600 = 219,822\n\nWait, that\'s different from before. Wait, earlier I thought 6822 + 151600 was 212,422. But now, when I recalculate, it\'s 219,822. Which is correct?\n\nWait, let me check again.\n\nFirst, 3032 + 3790:\n\n3032 + 3790:\n\n3000 + 3000 = 6000\n\n32 + 790 = 822\n\nSo 6000 + 822 = 6822. Correct.\n\nThen 6822 + 151600:\n\n6822 + 151600. Let\'s break it down:\n\n151600 + 6000 = 157600\n\n157600 + 822 = 158422\n\nYes, so total is 158,422. But when I did the other method, expanding the product, I got 158,422. Wait, but earlier when I did the expansion, I thought I got 158,422, but when I first did the expansion, I thought I had 158,350. Wait, let me check that again.\n\nWait, in the expansion method:\n\n120,000 + 3,000 = 123,000\n\n123,000 + 2,400 = 125,400\n\n125,400 + 28,000 = 153,400\n\n153,400 + 700 = 154,100\n\n154,100 + 560 = 154,660\n\n154,660 + 3,600 = 158,260\n\n158,260 + 90 = 158,350\n\n158,350 + 72 = 158,422\n\nAh, okay, so in the expansion method, I must have miscalculated earlier. Let me check each step again.\n\nFirst term: 300×400 = 120,000. Correct.\n\nSecond term: 300×10 = 3,000. Correct.\n\nThird term: 300×8 = 2,400. Correct.\n\nFourth term: 70×400 = 28,000. Correct.\n\nFifth term: 70×10 = 700. Correct.\n\nSixth term: 70×8 = 560. Correct.\n\nSeventh term: 9×400 = 3,600. Correct.\n\nEighth term: 9×10 = 90. Correct.\n\nNinth term: 9×8 = 72. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n120,000 + 3,000 = 123,000\n\n123,000 + 2,400 = 125,400\n\n125,400 + 28,000 = 153,400\n\n153,400 + 700 = 154,100\n\n154,100 + 560 = 154,660\n\n154,660 + 3,600 = 158,260\n\n158,260 + 90 = 158,350\n\n158,350 + 72 = 158,422\n\nYes, that\'s correct. So both methods give 158,422. So my initial calculation was correct. Earlier, when I thought I had 158,350, I must have made a mistake in the addition steps. So the correct product is 158,422.\n\nBut wait, let me check with another method to be absolutely sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nLet\'s do 379 × 418.\n\nFirst, write it down:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0379\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0×\xa0418\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0--------\n\nStart with the units digit of 418, which is 8. Multiply 379 by 8:\n\n379\n×\xa0\xa0\xa08\n------\n3032\n\nWrite down 3032.\n\nNext, multiply 379 by the tens digit of 418, which is 1. But since it\'s the tens place, we add a zero:\n\n379\n×\xa0\xa010\n------\n3790\n\nWrite down 3790, shifted one place to the left (so it\'s 37900 now).\n\nThen, multiply 379 by the hundreds digit of 418, which is 4. Add two zeros:\n\n379\n×\xa0\xa0400\n------\n151600\n\nWrite down 151600, shifted two places to the left (so it\'s 15160000 now).\n\nNow, add the three numbers together:\n\n3032\n+3790\n------\n6822\n\n6822\n+151600\n------\n158422\n\nYes, that\'s the same result. So 158,422 is the correct product.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another check. Let\'s use the fact that 379 × 418 = (400 - 21) × 418. Let\'s expand that.\n\n400 × 418 = 167,200\n\n-21 × 418 = -8,778\n\nSo total is 167,200 - 8,778 = 158,422. That\'s the same result. So that confirms it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to verify. But since I don\'t have a calculator here, but I can check with another multiplication method.\n\nAlternatively, use the difference of squares or other algebraic identities, but that might be more complicated.\n\nAlternatively, break down 418 into 400 + 18, then multiply 379 by 400 and 379 by 18, then add them.\n\n379 × 400 = 151,600\n\n379 × 18:\n\nFirst, 379 × 10 = 3,790\n\n379 × 8 = 3,032\n\nSo 3,790 + 3,032 = 6,822\n\nThen, 151,600 + 6,822 = 158,422. Same result.\n\nOkay, so all methods lead to 158,422. Therefore, the product of 379 and 418 is 158,422.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 379 and 418 is \\boxed{158422}.\n'] 68%|██████▊   | 340/500 [5:28:50<1:46:54, 40.09s/it]
