      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 911 and 467. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two three-digit numbers can be a bit tricky, but maybe there's a way to break it down step by step. Let me start by recalling the standard multiplication algorithm. \n\nFirst, I'll write 911 multiplied by 467. Let me set it up like this:\n\n      911\n    x 467\n    --------\n\nStarting with the rightmost digit of the second number, which is 7. I need to multiply 911 by 7 and then multiply 911 by the next digit, which is 6, but since it's in the tens place, I have to remember to shift that result one position to the left. Then, multiply 911 by 4, which is the hundreds place, and shift that two positions to the left. Finally, add all those results together.\n\nLet me start with the first multiplication: 911 x 7. Let's calculate that. \n\n7 times 1 is 7, 7 times 10 is 70, 7 times 100 is 700. So adding those up: 7 + 70 + 700 = 777. Wait, is that right? Let me check again. 7*1 = 7, 7*10 = 70, 7*100 = 700. So 7 + 70 is 77, plus 700 is 777. Yeah, that seems correct.\n\nNext, multiply 911 by 6. Let's do that. 6*1 is 6, 6*10 is 60, 6*100 is 600. So adding those: 6 + 60 + 600 = 666. Wait, 6 + 60 is 66, plus 600 is 666. That checks out.\n\nThen, multiply 911 by 4. 4*1 is 4, 4*10 is 40, 4*100 is 400. Adding those: 4 + 40 + 400 = 444. Yep, that's right.\n\nNow, according to the standard multiplication algorithm, I need to shift the second result (666) one place to the left because it's in the tens place. So that becomes 6660. Then, the third result (444) is already in the hundreds place, so it stays as 444. Then, the first result (777) is in the thousands place, so it stays as 7770.\n\nNow, I need to add these three numbers together: 7770 + 4440 + 6660. Let me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 7770 and 4440. Let's see, 7770 + 4440. Breaking it down: 7000 + 4000 = 11000, 700 + 400 = 1100, 70 + 40 = 110, 7 + 0 = 7. Adding those together: 11000 + 1100 = 12100, 12100 + 110 = 12210, 12210 + 7 = 12217. So 7770 + 4440 = 12217.\n\nNext, add 6660 to that result. So 12217 + 6660. Let's break it down: 12000 + 6000 = 18000, 200 + 600 = 800, 217 + 60 = 277. Adding those: 18000 + 800 = 18800, 18800 + 277 = 19077. So 12217 + 6660 = 19077.\n\nTherefore, the total product is 19077. Let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let's see. 911 x 467 can be broken down into (900 + 11) x (400 + 60 + 7). Let's compute each part:\n\nFirst, 900 x 400 = 360000\n\nThen, 900 x 60 = 54000\n\nThen, 900 x 7 = 6300\n\nNext, 11 x 400 = 4400\n\n11 x 60 = 660\n\n11 x 7 = 77\n\nNow, add all these together:\n\n360000 + 54000 = 414000\n\n414000 + 6300 = 420300\n\n420300 + 4400 = 464300\n\n464300 + 660 = 470960\n\n470960 + 77 = 471037\n\nWait, that's 471,037. But that's different from the previous result of 19,077. Hmm, that can't be right. There must be a mistake here. Let me check my breakdown again.\n\nWait, hold on. The original problem is 911 x 467. If I break it down as (900 + 11) x (400 + 60 + 7), that's correct. But when I calculated each part, maybe I messed up the multiplication.\n\nLet me recalculate each term:\n\nFirst, 900 x 400 = 360,000. That's correct.\n\n900 x 60 = 54,000. Correct.\n\n900 x 7 = 6,300. Correct.\n\n11 x 400 = 4,400. Correct.\n\n11 x 60 = 660. Correct.\n\n11 x 7 = 77. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n360,000 + 54,000 = 414,000\n\n414,000 + 6,300 = 414,000 + 6,000 = 414,000 + 300 = 414,300\n\nWait, no. Wait, 414,000 + 6,300 is 414,000 + 6,000 = 414,000 + 300 = 414,300. Then, 414,300 + 4,400 = 414,300 + 4,000 = 418,300 + 400 = 418,700. Then, 418,700 + 660 = 419,360. Then, 419,360 + 77 = 419,437. \n\nWait, so that's 419,437. But that's still different from the first method. Hmm, so clearly, there's a mistake here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me try another approach. Let's use the standard multiplication method again, but more carefully.\n\nMultiplying 911 by 467:\n\nFirst, write 911 x 7:\n\n7 x 1 = 7\n\n7 x 10 = 70\n\n7 x 100 = 700\n\nAdding those: 7 + 70 + 700 = 777. Correct.\n\nThen, 911 x 6 (tens place):\n\n6 x 1 = 6\n\n6 x 10 = 60\n\n6 x 100 = 600\n\nAdding those: 6 + 60 + 600 = 666. Correct.\n\nThen, 911 x 4 (hundreds place):\n\n4 x 1 = 4\n\n4 x 10 = 40\n\n4 x 100 = 400\n\nAdding those: 4 + 40 + 400 = 444. Correct.\n\nNow, shift the second result (666) one place left: 6660\n\nThird result (444) stays as 444\n\nFirst result (777) stays as 7770\n\nNow, adding 7770 + 4440 + 6660:\n\n7770 + 4440 = 12210\n\n12210 + 6660 = 18870\n\nWait, hold on, that's different from before. Wait, 7770 + 4440 is 12210? Let me check:\n\n7770 + 4440:\n\n7000 + 4000 = 11000\n\n700 + 400 = 1100\n\n70 + 40 = 110\n\n7 + 0 = 7\n\nAdding those: 11000 + 1100 = 12100; 12100 + 110 = 12210; 12210 + 7 = 12217. Wait, that's what I had before. Then 12217 + 6660:\n\n12217 + 6660:\n\n12000 + 6000 = 18000\n\n200 + 600 = 800\n\n217 + 60 = 277\n\nAdding those: 18000 + 800 = 18800; 18800 + 277 = 19077. So that's correct.\n\nBut when I did the distributive method, I got 419,437. That's way off. So clearly, I made a mistake in the distributive approach. Let me check that again.\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the breakdown. Let me try again. 467 is 400 + 60 + 7. So 911 multiplied by 400, 60, and 7. Then, adding those products.\n\nSo:\n\n911 x 400 = 364,400\n\n911 x 60 = 54,660\n\n911 x 7 = 6,377\n\nNow, adding those together:\n\n364,400 + 54,660 = 419,060\n\n419,060 + 6,377 = 425,437\n\nWait, that's 425,437. Hmm, still different from 19,077. So clearly, there's a problem here. Wait, but 911 x 467 is definitely not 425,437. Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the calculator method. Let me compute 911 x 467.\n\nLet me do it step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 911 by 400: 911 x 400 = 364,400\n\nThen, multiply 911 by 60: 911 x 60 = 54,660\n\nThen, multiply 911 by 7: 911 x 