nCompute each term:\n\n270*270 = 72,900\n\n270*2 = 540\n\n4*270 = 1,080\n\n4*2 = 8\n\nAdding them up: 72,900 + 540 = 73,440; 73,440 + 1,080 = 74,520; 74,520 +8 = 74,528. \n\nSame result. So that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 274 and 272 is 74,528. \n\nI think that's solid. All methods lead to 74,528. So the answer is 74,528.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 274 and 272 is \\boxed{74528}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 274 and 272, we can use the distributive property and recognize that 274 and 272 are 1 unit away from the average of 273. \n\nFirst, we note that:\n- 274 = 273 + 1\n- 272 = 273 - 1\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n(273 + 1)(273 - 1) = 273^2 - 1^2\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(273^2\\):\n\\[\n273^2 = (270 + 3)^2 = 270^2 + 2 \\cdot 270 \\cdot 3 + 3^2 = 72900 + 1620 + 9 = 74529\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 1 from this result:\n\\[\n74529 - 1 = 74528\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using the standard multiplication method:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  274 \\\\\n\\times 272 \\\\\n\\hline\n   548 \\quad \\text{(274 \\times 2)} \\\\\n 19180 \\quad \\text{(274 \\times 70)} \\\\\n 54800 \\quad \\text{(274 \\times 200)} \\\\\n\\hline\n 74528 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n548 + 19180 + 54800 = 74528\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 274 and 272 is \\(\\boxed{74528}\\).",
