= 18,000\n\nThird part: 900*6 = 5,400\n\nAdding those: 180,000 + 18,000 = 198,000; 198,000 + 5,400 = 203,400\n\nThen the 70s:\n\n70*200 = 14,000\n\n70*20 = 1,400\n\n70*6 = 420\n\nAdding those: 14,000 + 1,400 = 15,400; 15,400 + 420 = 15,820\n\nThen the 6s:\n\n6*200 = 1,200\n\n6*20 = 120\n\n6*6 = 36\n\nAdding those: 1,200 + 120 = 1,320; 1,320 + 36 = 1,356\n\nNow add all the parts together:\n\n203,400 (from 900s) + 15,820 (from 70s) = 219,220\n\n219,220 + 1,356 (from 6s) = 220,576\n\nWait, now this is different. Hmm, so I must have messed up the addition steps earlier. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, 900*200 = 180,000\n\n900*20 = 18,000\n\n900*6 = 5,400\n\nAdding those: 180,000 + 18,000 = 198,000; 198,000 + 5,400 = 203,400\n\nThen 70*200 = 14,000\n\n70*20 = 1,400\n\n70*6 = 420\n\nAdding those: 14,000 + 1,400 = 15,400; 15,400 + 420 = 15,820\n\nThen 6*200 = 1,200\n\n6*20 = 120\n\n6*6 = 36\n\nAdding those: 1,200 + 120 = 1,320; 1,320 + 36 = 1,356\n\nNow, adding all parts:\n\n203,400 (from 900s) + 15,820 (from 70s) = 219,220\n\n219,220 + 1,356 (from 6s) = 220,576\n\nWait, so now I get 220,576. But when I did the first breakdown, I ended up with 220,156. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in the first breakdown. Let me check the first calculation again.\n\nFirst breakdown:\n\n900*200 = 180,000\n\n900*20 = 18,000\n\n900*6 = 5,400\n\n70*200 = 14,000\n\n70*20 = 1,400\n\n70*6 = 420\n\n6*200 = 1,200\n\n6*20 = 120\n\n6*6 = 36\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\n180,000 + 18,000 = 198,000\n\n198,000 + 5,400 = 203,400\n\n203,400 + 14,000 = 217,400\n\n217,400 + 1,400 = 218,800\n\n218,800 + 420 = 219,220\n\n219,220 + 1,200 = 220,420\n\n220,420 + 36 = 220,456\n\nWait, now this is different again. So now I'm confused. Each time I add the parts, I get a different total. That can't be right. There must be an error in how I'm grouping the numbers.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to use the standard multiplication algorithm properly. Let me try that.\n\nMultiplying 976 by 226.\n\nFirst, write it down:\n\n      __________\n    976\n  x226\n  _______\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit of 226, which is 6.\n\nMultiply 976 by 6:\n\n6 * 976 = 5,856\n\nWrite that down:\n\n      __________\n    976\n  x226\n  _______\n      5,856\n\nNext digit: 2 (from 226), multiply 976 by 2:\n\n2 * 976 = 1,952\n\nBut since we're in the tens place, we add a zero:\n\n1,9520\n\nSo now:\n\n      __________\n    976\n  x226\n  _______\n      19,520\n\nNext digit: 2 (from 226), multiply 976 by 2 again:\n\n2 * 976 = 1,952\n\nBut this time, it's in the hundreds place, so add two zeros:\n\n195,200\n\nNow add all the partial products:\n\n5,856\n\n+19,520\n\n+195,200\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 5,856 + 19,520:\n\n5,856 + 19,520 = 25,376\n\nThen add 195,200:\n\n25,376 + 195,200 = 220,576\n\nSo according to the standard multiplication method, the product is 220,576. That seems consistent. So why did I get different results when I broke it down into parts? Probably because I made a mistake in the addition steps. Let me check again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to verify. Let's try using the distributive property again but more carefully.\n\nFirst, 976 * 226 can be written as 976*(200 + 20 + 6) = 976*200 + 976*20 + 976*6\n\nCompute each term:\n\n976*200 = 976*2*100 = 1,952*100 = 195,200\n\n976*20 = 976*2*10 = 1,952*10 = 19,520\n\n976*6 = 5,856\n\nNow add them together:\n\n195,200 + 19,520 = 214,720\n\n214,720 + 5,856 = 220,576\n\nAh, there we go! So when I broke it down into parts, I must have added them incorrectly in the first attempt. The correct total is 220,576. So the standard multiplication method gives the same result as this breakdown. Therefore, the product of 976 and 226 is 220,576.\n\nJust to be thorough, let me try multiplying using another method, like the lattice method or another breakdown.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using 976 as (1000 - 24) and 226 as (200 + 26). Let's see:\n\n(1000 - 24) * (200 + 26) = 1000*200 + 1000*26 - 24*200 - 24*26\n\nCompute each term:\n\n1000*200 = 200,000\n\n1000*26 = 26,000\n\n24*200 = 4,800\n\n24*26 = 624\n\nNow add them:\n\n200,000 + 26,000 = 226,000\n\n226,000 - 4,800 = 221,200\n\n221,200 - 624 = 220,576\n\nSame result! So that confirms it. Therefore, the product is indeed 220,576.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using prime factors? Let's see:\n\nBut that might be more complicated. Let's try:\n\n976 and 226.\n\nFirst, factor 976:\n\n976 ÷ 2 = 488\n\n488 ÷ 2 = 244\n\n244 ÷ 2 = 122\n\n122 ÷ 2 = 61\n\nSo 976 = 2^4 * 61\n\nFactor 226:\n\n226 ÷ 2 = 113\n\n113 is a prime number.\n\nSo 226 = 2 * 113\n\nTherefore, the product is 2^4 * 61 * 2 * 113 = 2^5 * 61 * 113\n\nBut calculating that would require multiplication:\n\n2^5 = 32\n\n32 * 61 = 1,952\n\n1,952 * 113\n\nLet's compute 1,952 * 100 = 195,200\n\n1,952 * 13 = 25,376\n\n195,200 + 25,376 = 220,576\n\nAgain, same result. So regardless of the method, the product is 220,576. Therefore, I can be confident that the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 976 and 226 is \\boxed{220576}.\n"] 71%|███████   | 356/500 [5:46:55<1:29:58, 37.49s/it]
