t me add 1314 + 32850 first:\n\n1314 + 32850. Let's do this:\n\n1314 + 32850. Let's add 1314 + 30000 = 31314, then 31314 + 2850 = 34164.\n\nThen, add 34164 + 591300:\n\n34164 + 591300. Let's add 34164 + 500000 = 534164, then 534164 + 91300 = 625464.\n\nSo, total is 625,464. Hmm, but when I did the initial addition of 1314 + 3285 + 5913, I got 10,508. That was wrong because I didn't shift the partial products. So, the correct total is 625,464. Let me check this with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, use the distributive property:\n\n657 × 952 = 657 × (900 + 50 + 2) = 657×900 + 657×50 + 657×2\n\nCompute each term:\n\n657 × 900: 657 × 9 × 100. 657 × 9: 5913. So, 5913 × 100 = 591,300\n\n657 × 50: 657 × 5 × 10. 657 × 5 = 3,285. So, 3,285 × 10 = 32,850\n\n657 × 2 = 1,314\n\nNow, add them all together:\n\n591,300 + 32,850 + 1,314\n\nFirst, add 591,300 + 32,850:\n\n591,300 + 32,850. Let's compute:\n\n591,300 + 30,000 = 621,300\n\n621,300 + 2,850 = 624,150\n\nThen, add 1,314 to 624,150:\n\n624,150 + 1,314 = 625,464\n\nYes, that's the same result as before. So, the product of 657 and 952 is 625,464. Therefore, the correct answer should be 625,464. \n\nBut wait, let me verify with a calculator to be absolutely sure. Since I can't use a calculator, maybe I can check with another multiplication method.\n\nAlternatively, multiply 657 × 952:\n\nLet me write it out as:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0657\n×\xa0\xa0952\n--------\n\xa0\xa01314\xa0\xa0(657 × 2)\n\xa0\xa032850\xa0\xa0(657 × 50)\n\xa0591300\xa0\xa0\xa0(657 × 900)\n--------\n\xa0\xa0625464\n\nYes, adding those gives 625,464. So, that's correct. Therefore, the product is 625,464.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 657 and 952 is \\boxed{625464}.\n"] 72%|███████▏  | 358/500 [5:47:37<1:09:56, 29.56s/it]
