0000 + 2325 = 622325.\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, it's 8525. That's a conflict. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the standard multiplication. Let me check the standard multiplication again.\n\nWait, in standard multiplication, when you multiply by the units digit (3), you get 2325. Then, when you multiply by the tens digit (0), you get 0. Then, when you multiply by the hundreds digit (8), you get 6200. Then, when adding, you have to shift each partial product according to their place.\n\nBut in standard multiplication, the partial products are:\n\n- The first partial product (from the units digit) is in the units place.\n- The second partial product (from the tens digit) is in the tens place.\n- The third partial product (from the hundreds digit) is in the hundreds place.\n\nTherefore, adding them:\n\n2325 (units)\n+\u00a0\u00a00 (tens)\n+\u00a0\u00a06200 (hundreds)\n= 2325 + 0 + 6200 = 8525.\n\nBut according to the other method, it's 622325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, 775 \u00d7 803. Let me compute 775 \u00d7 803 using another method. Let's use the distributive property.\n\n775 \u00d7 803 = 775 \u00d7 (800 + 3) = 775 \u00d7 800 + 775 \u00d7 3 = 620000 + 2325 = 622325.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 775 \u00d7 803 using the standard multiplication:\n\n775\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0803\n--------\n\u00a0\u00a02325\u00a0\u00a0(3 \u00d7 775)\n\u00a0\u00a00\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0(0 \u00d7 775)\n\u00a0\u00a06200\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0(8 \u00d7 775)\n--------\nAdding these:\n\n2325 + 0 + 6200 = 8525.\n\nBut 622325 vs. 8525. There's a problem here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check 775 \u00d7 803 again.\n\nWait, 775 \u00d7 803. Let's compute 775 \u00d7 803 step by step.\n\nFirst, multiply 775 by 800:\n\n775 \u00d7 800. 775 \u00d7 8 = 6200, so 6200 \u00d7 100 = 620000.\n\nThen, multiply 775 by 3:\n\n775 \u00d7 3 = 2325.\n\nAdd them together: 620000 + 