2,872 + 7,000 = 9,872. Then add 180: 9,872 + 180 = 10,052.\n\nThen add 28,720 to 10,052. 10,052 + 28,720. Let's break it down:\n\n10,052 + 20,000 = 30,052\n\n30,052 + 8,720 = 38,772.\n\nBut according to the first method, the product is 297,252. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the second method. Let me check the multiplication steps again.\n\nWait, 359*800: 359*8=2,872, then times 100 is 287,200. That's correct.\n\n359*28: 359*20=7,180 and 359*8=2,872. 7,180+2,872=10,052. Correct.\n\nSo 287,200 + 10,052 = 297,252. So why does the second method give 38,772? That's way off. There must be a mistake in the second method's addition.\n\nWait, no. Wait, when you do the standard multiplication, you have to shift the digits appropriately. Let me write it out properly.\n\nMultiplying 359 by 828:\n\n          359\n        x828\n        -------\n          2872  (359*8)\n         7180   (359*20, shifted one position)\n        28720   (359*800, shifted two positions)\n        -------\n        297252\n\nWait, so when you add them:\n\n2,872 (units)\n+7,180 (tens)\n+28,720 (hundreds)\n= 2,872 + 7,180 = 10,052; 10,052 + 28,720 = 38,772. But that's not matching the first method. So which is correct?\n\nWait, this is impossible. There must be a miscalculation here. Let me check the addition again.\n\nWait, 2,872 + 7,180. Let's compute 2,872 + 7,180:\n\n2,872 + 7,000 = 9,872\n\n9,872 + 180 = 10,052. That's correct.\n\nThen 10,052 + 28,720:\n\n10,052 + 28,720. Let's compute 10,000 + 28,000 = 38,000\n\n52 + 720 = 772\n\n38,000 + 772 = 38,772. Hmm, that's correct. But according to the first method, it's 297,252. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the first method. Let me check 359*800 and 359*28 again.\n\n359*800: 359*8=2,872. 2,872*100=287,200. Correct.\n\n359*28: 359*20=7,180. 359*8=2,872. 7,180+2,872=10,052. Correct.\n\n287,200 + 10,052: 287,200 + 10,000 = 297,200. Then +52 = 297,252. C