out breaking it down:\n\n          359\n        x828\n        -------\n          2872  (359*8)\n         7180   (359*20)\n        28720   (359*800)\n        -------\n        297252\n\nYes, adding those gives 297,252. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the lattice method? But that might be more complicated. Alternatively, use calculator-like multiplication.\n\nBut since both methods of breaking down into 800 and 28, and the standard multiplication give the same result, I can be confident that 297,252 is the correct product.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 297,252.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 359 and 828 is \\boxed{297252}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 359 and 828, we can break down the multiplication into parts and then add the results. \n\nFirst, calculate \\(359 \\times 800\\):\n\\[\n359 \\times 800 = 359 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 2872 \\times 100 = 287200\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(359 \\times 28\\):\n\\[\n359 \\times 28 = 359 \\times 20 + 359 \\times 8 = 7180 + 2872 = 10052\n\\]\n\nNow, add the two results together:\n\\[\n287200 + 10052 = 297252\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  359 \\\\\n\\times 828 \\\\\n\\hline\n  2872 \\quad \\text{(359 \\times 8)} \\\\\n 7180 \\quad \\text{(359 \\times 20)} \\\\\n 28720 \\quad \\text{(359 \\times 800)} \\\\\n\\hline\n 297252 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding the partial products step-by-step:\n\\[\n2872 + 7180 = 10052\n\\]\n\\[\n10052 + 28720 = 297252\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 359 and 828 is \\(\\boxed{297252}\\).",
