r, 280,000 + 6,400 = 286,400. That's the same result. So that estimation method also gives 286,400. So that's another confirmation.\n\nWait, maybe I can check using another multiplication method. Let's do it step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 716 by 4:\n\n716\nx  4\n------\n2864\n\nThen, since it's 400, which is 4 x 100, so 2864 x 100. Moving the decimal two places right: 2864 becomes 286400. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, if I didn't break it down, maybe I could multiply 716 by 400 directly. Let's try that. 716 x 400. Let's think of 400 as 4 x 100. So again, 716 x 4 = 2864, then 2864 x 100 = 286400. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 400 is 4 x 100, so 716 x 400 = (716 x 4) x 100. Which is 2864 x 100. So again, 286400.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nMultiply 716 by 400.\n\nFirst, multiply 716 by 4:\n\n716\nx  4\n------\n2864\n\nThen, since 400 is 4 x 100, you add two zeros to the result. So 2864 becomes 286400.\n\nAlternatively, if I didn't break it down, maybe I could multiply 716 by 400 by multiplying 716 by 4 and then by 100. Which is the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property in another way. Let's see:\n\n716 x 400 = 716 x (4 x 100) = (716 x 4) x 100 = 2864 x 100 = 286400.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 400 is 100 x 4, so 716 x 100 x 4. Which is the same as (716 x 100) x 4. 716 x 100 is 71600, then 71600 x 4. Let's compute that:\n\n71600 x 4. 70000 x 4 = 280000, 1600 x 4 = 6400. So 280000 + 6400 = 286400. Same answer. So that works too.\n\nSo regardless of the method, the answer seems to be 286,400. Let me just verify once more with another approach. Maybe using a calculator if I have one, but since I don't, I'll do a manual check.\n\nLet me write out 716 x 400:\n\n716\nx 400\n--------\n286400\n\nYes, that's 286,400. So all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 716 and 400 is 286,400.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 716 and 400 is \\boxed{286400}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 716 and 400, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps. \n\nFirst, multiply 716 by 4:\n\\[\n716 \\times 4 = 2864\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply the result by 100 (since 400 is 4 multiplied by 100):\n\\[\n2864 \\times 100 = 286400\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this by recognizing that multiplying by 400 is equivalent to multiplying by 4 and then by 100. Another method is to use the distributive property:\n\\[\n716 \\times 400 = (716 \\times 4) \\times 100 = 2864 \\times 100 = 286400\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 716 and 400 is \\(\\boxed{286400}\\).",
