then 71600 x 4. Let's compute that:\n\n71600 x 4. 70000 x 4 = 280000, 1600 x 4 = 6400. So 280000 + 6400 = 286400. Same answer. So that works too.\n\nSo regardless of the method, the answer seems to be 286,400. Let me just verify once more with another approach. Maybe using a calculator if I have one, but since I don't, I'll do a manual check.\n\nLet me write out 716 x 400:\n\n716\nx 400\n--------\n286400\n\nYes, that's 286,400. So all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 716 and 400 is 286,400.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 716 and 400 is \\boxed{286400}.\n"] 82%|████████▏ | 410/500 [6:37:00<1:08:36, 45.74s/it]
