 That's correct. Then 340 x 80: 340 x 8 = 2,720, times 10 is 27,200. Correct. Then 340 x 8 = 2,720. Adding them up: 306,000 + 27,200 is 333,200. Then 333,200 + 2,720 is 335,920. Hmm, seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another method. Let's try the standard multiplication algorithm step by step. Let's write 340 x 988.\n\nFirst, multiply 340 by 8: 340 x 8 = 2,720. Then multiply 340 by 80: 340 x 80 = 27,200. Then multiply 340 by 900: 340 x 900 = 306,000. Then add them all together: 2,720 + 27,200 + 306,000. Wait, that's the same as before. So 2,720 + 27,200 is 29,920. Then 29,920 + 306,000 = 335,920. Yep, same result. So that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach. Let's see. 340 x 988. Maybe break down 988 into 1000 - 12. So, 340 x 1000 = 340,000. Then subtract 340 x 12. Let's compute 340 x 12. 340 x 10 = 3,400. 340 x 2 = 680. So 3,400 + 680 = 4,080. Therefore, 340,000 - 4,080 = 335,920. That's the same answer. Nice, so that method also gives 335,920. So that's a good confirmation.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property in another way. Let's see. 340 x 988. Let me think of 988 as (1000 - 12) as before, but maybe also as (900 + 80 + 8). Wait, that's the same as before. So, perhaps the first method is the most straightforward.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, I need to rely on my manual calculations. But both methods I tried gave me 335,920, so that gives me confidence.\n\nWait, let me just do a quick check with another method. Let's use the fact that 340 x 988 = 340 x (1000 - 12) = 340,000 - (340 x 12). As before, 340 x 12 is 4,080. So 340,000 - 4,080 = 335,920. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step. Let's write it out:\n\n     340\n   x 988\n   -------\n     2720  (340 x 8)\n   306000   (340 x 900)\n  299200    (340 x 80)\n ---------\n  335920\n\nWait, let me align the numbers properly. When 