o write 4, carry 5.\n\nWait, so the result is 5424. Wait, but when I did it before, I thought the first step was 5424. So that's correct.\n\nWait, but in my initial calculation, I thought 678 × 8 was 5424, which is correct. Then 678 × 50 is 33900, and 678 × 300 is 203400. Then adding them up gives 242724. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check with another approach. Let's compute 678 × 358.\n\nAlternatively, break down 358 into 300 + 50 + 8, which is what I did. So that's the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nLet me write it out again:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0678\n×\xa0\xa0358\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 678 by 8:\n\n8\n×\xa0\xa0678\n------\n4 (units place)\n6 (tens place, carry 6)\n5 (hundreds place, carry 5)\nSo 5424\n\nThen multiply 678 by 50. Since 50 is 5 × 10, so first multiply by 5:\n\n5\n×\xa0\xa0678\n------\n4 (units place)\n6 (tens place, carry 4)\n3 (hundreds place, carry 3)\nSo 3390\n\nThen multiply 678 by 300. 300 is 3 × 100, so multiply by 3:\n\n3\n×\xa0\xa0678\n------\n2 (units place)\n8 (tens place, carry 2)\n4 (hundreds place, carry 4)\nSo 203400\n\nNow, add 5424 + 33900 + 203400.\n\nFirst, 5424 + 33900:\n\n5424 + 33900. Let's add 5424 + 33900.\n\n5424 + 33900 = (5000 + 424) + (30000 + 3900) = 5000 + 30000 = 35000; 424 + 900 = 1324; total 35000 + 1324 = 36324. Wait, but earlier I thought it was 39324. Wait, that's a mistake here. Wait, no. Wait, 5424 + 33900. Let's compute it properly.\n\n5424 + 33900:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n4 + 0 = 4\n\n2 + 9 = 11, write 1, carry 1\n\n4 + 3 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\n5 + 3 = 8\n\nSo total is 8824? Wait, that can't be. Wait, no. Wait, 5424 + 33900.\n\nWait, 5424 is 5 thousands, 4 hundreds, 2 tens, 4 units.\n\n33900 is 3 ten thousands, 3 thousands, 9 hundreds, 0 tens, 0 units.\n\nAdding them:\n\n5 thousands + 3 ten thousands = 8 ten thousands\n\n4 hundreds + 3 hundreds = 7 hundreds\n\n2 tens + 0 tens = 2 tens\n\n4 units + 0 units = 4 units\n\nSo total is 88240? Wait, that's not right. Wait, no. Wait, 5424 is 5.424 thousand, and 33900 is 33.9 thousand. So 5.424 + 33.9 = 39.324 thousand, which is 39324. Ah, right. So 5424 + 33900 = 39324. Then adding 203400 to that.\n\n39324 + 203400. Let's compute:\n\n39324 + 203400. Break it down:\n\n39324 + 200000 = 239324\n\n239324 + 3400 = 242724\n\nYes, that's correct. So the total is 242724. So that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check using another method. Let's try multiplying 678 × 358 using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, use the fact that 678 × 358 = (600 + 78) × (300 + 50 + 8). But that's similar to the previous method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nLet me write it out again:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0678\n×\xa0\xa0358\n--------\n\nMultiply 678 by 8:\n\n8\n×\xa0\xa0678\n------\n4 (units)\n6 (tens, carry 6)\n5 (hundreds, carry 5)\nResult: 5424\n\nMultiply 678 by 50:\n\n5\n×\xa0\xa0678\n------\n4 (units)\n6 (tens, carry 4)\n3 (hundreds, carry 3)\nResult: 3390\n\nMultiply 678 by 300:\n\n3\n×\xa0\xa0678\n------\n2 (units)\n8 (tens, carry 2)\n4 (hundreds, carry 4)\nResult: 203400\n\nNow, add 5424 + 33900:\n\n5424 + 33900:\n\n5424 + 33900 = 39324\n\nThen add 39324 + 203400:\n\n39324 + 203400 = 242724\n\nYes, same result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check using a different multiplication method. For example, using the grid method.\n\nBut that might take longer. Alternatively, use approximate estimation to check if 242724 is reasonable.\n\n678 is approximately 700, and 358 is approximately 360. So 700 × 360 = 252,000. So 242,724 is close to that, which makes sense. So the exact answer is 242,724, which is less than 252,000, which seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check using another multiplication step.\n\nLet me verify 678 × 8 again:\n\n8 × 600 = 4800\n\n8 × 70 = 560\n\n8 × 8 = 64\n\nAdding those: 4800 + 560 = 5360; 5360 + 64 = 5424. Correct.\n\nThen 678 × 50:\n\n50 × 600 = 30,000\n\n50 × 70 = 3,