output:  ['\n\nTo find the product of 684 and 119, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 684 by the rightmost digit (9):\n   \\[\n   684 \\times 9 = 6156\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 684 by the next digit (1), shifting the result one place to the left:\n   \\[\n   684 \\times 1 = 684 \\quad \\text{shifted left by 1} \\quad 6840\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 684 by the next digit (1), shifting the result two places to the left:\n   \\[\n   684 \\times 1 = 684 \\quad \\text{shifted left by 2} \\quad 68400\n   \\]\n4. Add the results of these multiplications:\n   \\[\n   6156 + 6840 + 68400 = 81396\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n684 \\times 119 = 684 \\times (100 + 10 + 9) = 684 \\times 100 + 684 \\times 10 + 684 \\times 9\n\\]\n\\[\n= 68400 + 6840 + 6156 = 81396\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 684 and 119 is \\(\\boxed{81396}\\).', "\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 684 and 119. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two numbers can be done step by step, breaking it down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm here. Let me recall how that works.\n\nFirst, I'll write 684 multiplied by 119. Let me set it up like this:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0684\n×\xa0\xa0119\n--------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit of the second number, which is 9. I need to multiply 684 by 9 first. Let me calculate that:\n\n684 × 9. Let's break it down:\n- 600 × 9 = 5400\n- 80 × 9 = 720\n- 4 × 9 = 36\nAdding those together: 5400 + 720 = 6120; 6120 + 36 = 6156. So, 684 × 9 = 6156.\n\nNext, I need to multiply 684 by the next digit, which is 1. But since it's the tens place, I have to remember to shift the result one place to the left. So, 684 × 1 = 684. Now, shifting it left by one gives 6840.\n\nThen, the next digit is 1 again, but this time it's the hundreds place. So, multiply 684 by 1 and shift two places to the left. That would be 684 × 1 = 684, shifted to the left twice: 68400.\n\nNow, add all those results together: 6156 (from the 9s place) + 6840 (from the 1 in the tens place) + 68400 (from the 1 in the hundreds place).\n\nLet me add them step by step. First, 6156 + 6840. Let's see:\n\n6156 + 6840. Breaking it down:\n- 6000 + 6000 = 12000\n- 156 + 840 = 996\nSo total is 12000 + 996 = 12996.\n\nThen add 68400 to that. 12996 + 68400. Let's compute:\n\n12996 + 68400. Breaking it down:\n- 10000 + 60000 = 70000\n- 2996 + 8400 = 11396\nSo total is 70000 + 11396 = 81396.\n\nWait, let me check that again. Maybe I made a mistake in the addition. Let's do it another way.\n\n12996 + 68400. Let's add 12996 + 68400:\n\nStart with 12996 + 60000 = 72996\n\nThen add 8400: 72996 + 8400 = 81396. Yeah, that's correct.\n\nSo, the total product is 81396. Let me verify this using another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let's break down 119 into 100 + 10 + 9. So, 684 × 119 = 684 × (100 + 10 + 9) = 684×100 + 684×10 + 684×9.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n684×100 = 68400\n\n684×10 = 6840\n\n684×9 = 6156 (as before)\n\nAdding them up: 68400 + 6840 = 75240; 75240 + 6156 = 81396. Same result. Okay, that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another multiplication method. Let's try multiplying 684 by 119 using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nFirst, write 684 × 119:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0684\n×\xa0\xa0119\n--------\n\nMultiply 684 by 9: 6156\n\nMultiply 684 by 1 (tens place): 6840\n\nMultiply 684 by 1 (hundreds place): 68400\n\nAdd them up: 6156 + 6840 + 68400 = 81396. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator here, I'll just verify once more.\n\nWait, let me check 684 × 119 again. Let's do it digit by digit.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n9 (units place): 684 × 9 = 6156\n\n1 (tens place): 684 × 1 = 684, shifted one position left: 6840\n\n1 (hundreds place): 684 × 1 = 684, shifted two positions left: 68400\n\nAdding 6156 + 6840:\n\n6156 + 6840. Let's add 6000 + 6000 = 12000\n\n156 + 840 = 996\n\n12000 + 996 = 12996\n\nThen 12996 + 68400 = 81396. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach. Let's consider 119 as 120 - 1. So, 684 × 119 = 684 × (120 - 1) = 684 × 120 - 684 × 1.\n\nCalculate 684 × 120:\n\n684 × 100 = 68400\n\n684 × 20 = 13680\n\nSo, 68400 + 13680 = 82080\n\nThen subtract 684 × 1 = 684\n\n82080 - 684 = 81396. Same result. Perfect.\n\nSo, all methods lead to 81396. Therefore, the product of 684 and 119 is 81,396.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 684 and 119 is \\boxed{81396}.\n"] 86%|████████▋ | 432/500 [6:54:17<1:16:45, 67.73s/it]
