 me calculate that:\n\n763 × 20. Hmm, that's the same as 763 × 2 × 10. Let's compute 763 × 2 first:\n- 700 × 2 = 1400\n- 60 × 2 = 120\n- 3 × 2 = 6\nAdding those: 1400 + 120 = 1520, then 1520 + 6 = 1526. Then multiply by 10: 1526 × 10 = 15260. So, the second partial product is 15260.\n\nNow, the leftmost digit of 828 is 8 again, but this time it's in the hundreds place. So, we need to multiply 763 by 800 (since 8 is in the hundreds place). Let's compute that:\n\n763 × 800. That's 763 × 8 × 100. First, 763 × 8:\n- 700 × 8 = 5600\n- 60 × 8 = 480\n- 3 × 8 = 24\nAdding those: 5600 + 480 = 6080, then 6080 + 24 = 6104. Then multiply by 100: 6104 × 100 = 610400. So, the third partial product is 610400.\n\nNow, adding up all the partial products: 6104 (first) + 15260 (second) + 610400 (third). Let's do that step by step.\n\nFirst, add 6104 and 15260. Let's break it down:\n6104 + 15260. Let's add 6000 + 15260 = 21260, then add the remaining 104: 21260 + 104 = 21364.\n\nNext, add 21364 to 610400. Let's see:\n610400 + 21364. Let's break it down:\n610400 + 20000 = 810400\n810400 + 1364 = 811,764\n\nWait, let me check that again. 610400 + 21364. Let's add 610400 + 20000 = 810400. Then add 1364: 810400 + 1000 = 811400, then +364 = 811400 + 364 = 811,764. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo, the total product is 811,764. Let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let's express 828 as (800 + 20 + 8). Wait, that's the same as before. Alternatively, maybe break down 828 into 800 + 28. Let's try that.\n\n763 × 828 = 763 × (800 + 28) = 763 × 800 + 763 × 28.\n\nWe already calculated 763 × 800 = 610,400.\n\nNow, 763 × 28. Let's compute that. 28 is 20 + 8.\n\n763 × 20 = 15,260 (as before)\n763 × 8 = 6,104 (as before)\nAdding those: 15,260 + 6,104 = 21,364.\n\nThen, adding 610,400 + 21,364 = 631,764. Wait, that's different from the previous result. Wait, hold on, that can't be. Wait, no, wait, 610,400 + 21,364. Let me check that again.\n\n610,400 + 21,364. Let's add 610,400 + 20,000 = 630,400. Then add 1,364: 630,400 + 1,364 = 631,764. Wait, but earlier I got 811,764. That's a discrepancy. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me check both methods again.\n\nFirst method: 763 × 828.\n\nFirst partial product: 763 × 8 = 6,104\n\nSecond partial product: 763 × 20 = 15,260\n\nThird partial product: 763 × 800 = 610,400\n\nAdding them: 6,104 + 15,260 = 21,364; 21,364 + 610,400 = 631,764.\n\nSecond method: 763 × (800 + 28) = 763 × 800 + 763 × 28 = 610,400 + 21,364 = 631,764.\n\nWait, so both methods give 631,764. But earlier, when I did the first method, I thought I got 811,764. That was a mistake. Wait, no, let me check again.\n\nWait, in the first method, when I broke down 828 into 800 + 20 + 8, then multiplied each by 763 and added the partial products. Let me recheck that.\n\nFirst partial product: 763 × 8 = 6,104\n\nSecond partial product: 763 × 20 = 15,260\n\nThird partial product: 763 × 800 = 610,400\n\nAdding them: 6,104 + 15,260 = 21,364; 21,364 + 610,400 = 631,764. So that's correct.\n\nWait, but in my initial calculation, I thought I added 6104 + 15260 + 610400 as 6104 + 15260 = 21364, then 21364 + 610400 = 631,764. So, that's correct. So why did I think I had 811,764 before? Maybe a miscalculation. So both methods give 631,764. So that's the correct answer.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method. Maybe using the standard algorithm again, but more carefully.\n\nLet me write it out step by step:\n\n\u202f\xa0\xa0763\n×\xa0\xa0828\n--------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n8 × 763 = 6,104\n\nNext digit: 2 (tens place) × 763 = 1,526 (but shifted one position to the left, so 15,260)\n\nNext digit: 8 (hundreds place) × 763 = 61,040 (shifted two positions, so 610,400)\n\nNow, adding them up:\n\n6,104\n\n+15,260\n\n=21,364\n\n21,364\n\n+610,400\n\n=631,764\n\nYes, that's correct. So the product is 631,764.\n\nWait, but let me verify using a