o that's the same as the first method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 172 by 6:\n\n172 \u00d7 6: 100\u00d76=600, 70\u00d76=420, 2\u00d76=12. So 600+420=1,020+12=1,032. That's the first partial product.\n\nThen multiply 172 by 40. Since 40 is 4\u00d710, so 172\u00d74=688, then \u00d710=6,880. That's the second partial product.\n\nThen multiply 172 by 800. 172\u00d78=1,376, then \u00d7100=137,600. That's the third partial product.\n\nAdding them all together: 1,032 + 6,880 + 137,600. Let's add 1,032 and 6,880 first. 1,032 + 6,880. 1,000 + 6,000 = 7,000; 32 + 880 = 912. So total is 7,000 + 912 = 7,912. Then add 137,600 to 7,912. 137,600 + 7,000 = 144,600; 144,600 + 912 = 145,512. Same result again.\n\nSo all methods lead to 145,512. Therefore, I think that's the correct answer. Let me just check with a calculator to be absolutely sure. But since I don't have a calculator here, maybe I can cross-verify with another multiplication.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another decomposition. For example, 172 \u00d7 846. Let's see, 172 is 170 + 2, and 846 is 800 + 40 + 6. So:\n\n170 \u00d7 800 = 136,000\n\n170 \u00d7 40 = 6,800\n\n170 \u00d7 6 = 1,020\n\n2 \u00d7 800 = 1,600\n\n2 \u00d7 40 = 80\n\n2 \u00d7 6 = 12\n\nAdding all these:\n\n136,000 + 6,800 = 142,800\n\n142,800 + 1,020 = 143,820\n\n1,600 + 80 = 1,680\n\n1,680 + 12 = 1,692\n\n143,820 + 1,692 = 145,512. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication step-by-step:\n\nMultiply 172 by 846:\n\nFirst, multiply 172 by 6: 172\u00d76=1,032\n\nThen, multiply 172 by 40 (shift one position to the left): 172\u00d740=6,880\n\nThen, multiply 172 by 800 (shift two positions to the left): 172\u00d7800=137,600\n\nAdd them up:\n\n1,032\n\n+6,880\n\n+137,600\n\n=145,512\n\nYes, same answer. So I think that's solid. Therefore, the product of 172 and 846 is 145,512.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 172 and 846 is \\boxed{145512}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 172 and 846, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts.\n\nFirst, we decompose 172 into 170 and 2, and 846 into 800, 40, and 6. Then, we multiply each part separately and add the results together:\n\n1. Multiply 170 by each part of 846:\n   - \\(170 \\times 800 = 136,000\\)\n   - \\(170 \\times 40 = 6,800\\)\n   - \\(170 \\times 6 = 1,020\\)\n\n2. Add these results together:\n   - \\(136,000 + 6,800 = 142,800\\)\n   - \\(142,800 + 1,020 = 143,820\\)\n\n3. Multiply 2 by each part of 846:\n   - \\(2 \\times 800 = 1,600\\)\n   - \\(2 \\times 40 = 80\\)\n   - \\(2 \\times 6 = 12\\)\n\n4. Add these results together:\n   - \\(1,600 + 80 = 1,680\\)\n   - \\(1,680 + 12 = 1,692\\)\n\n5. Add the two results together:\n   - \\(143,820 + 1,692 = 145,512\\)\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 172 by 6: \\(172 \\times 6 = 1,032\\)\n2. Multiply 172 by 40: \\(172 \\times 40 = 6,880\\)\n3. Multiply 172 by 800: \\(172 \\times 800 = 137,600\\)\n\n4. Add these results together:\n   - \\(1,032 + 6,880 = 7,912\\)\n   - \\(7,912 + 137,600 = 145,512\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 172 and 846 is \\(\\boxed{145512}\\).",
