 Shifted left by two, so 228300. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n3044 + 15220:\n\n3044 + 15220. Let's add 3000 + 15200 = 18200, then 44 + 20 = 64. So 18200 + 64 = 18264. Then 18264 + 228300:\n\n18264 + 228300. Let's add 18000 + 228000 = 246000, then 264 + 300 = 564. So 246000 + 564 = 246564. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, adding 18264 and 228300:\n\n18264\n\n+228300\n\n=246564. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo, all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, the product of 761 and 324 is 246,564.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 761 and 324 is \\boxed{246564}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 761 and 324, we can break down the multiplication into parts using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 761 by the units digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   761 \\times 4 = 3044\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 761 by the tens digit (2), shifting the result one place to the left:**\n   \\[\n   761 \\times 2 = 1522 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one place: 15220)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 761 by the hundreds digit (3), shifting the result two places to the left:**\n   \\[\n   761 \\times 3 = 2283 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two places: 228300)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results of the three parts together:**\n   \\[\n   3044 + 15220 + 228300\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 3044 and 15220:\n     \\[\n     3044 + 15220 = 18264\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to 228300:\n     \\[\n     18264 + 228300 = 246564\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 761 and 324 is \\(\\boxed{246564}\\).",
