te it out more carefully.\n\nWait, 4764 + 47640:\n\nLet's add 4764 + 47640. Let's consider 4764 as 47640 - 46. So 47640 - 46 = 47594. Hmm, not sure if that helps. Alternatively, maybe add 4764 + 47640:\n\n4764\n+47640\n= 4764 + 47640. Let's add 4764 + 47640:\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\n4 + 0 = 4\n\n6 + 4 = 10, write down 0, carry over 1\n\n7 + 6 + 1 (carry) = 14, write down 4, carry over 1\n\n4 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 12, write down 2, carry over 1\n\nThen the next digit: 0 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 5\n\nSo the sum is 52404. Wait, let me check:\n\nWait, 4764 + 47640:\n\nIf I write 4764 as 04764, then adding to 47640:\n\n04764\n+47640\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 0 = 4\n\n6 + 4 = 10, carry 1\n\n7 + 6 + 1 = 14, carry 1\n\n4 + 7 + 1 = 12, carry 1\n\n0 + 4 + 1 = 5\n\nSo the sum is 52404. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo 4764 + 47640 = 52404.\n\nNow, add 3970 to 52404.\n\n52404 + 3970. Let's break it down:\n\n52404 + 3000 = 55404\n\n55404 + 970 = 55404 + 900 = 56304; 56304 + 70 = 56374\n\nSo total is 56374.\n\nWait, let me verify that addition again:\n\n52404 + 3970:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n4 + 0 = 4\n\n0 + 7 = 7\n\n4 + 9 = 13, write down 3, carry over 1\n\n2 + 3 + 1 = 6\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\nSo the sum is 56374. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 794 and 536 is 56,374.\n\nWait, but let me check if I did all steps correctly. Let me cross-verify using another method, maybe the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property. Let's see:\n\n794 \u00d7 536 can be written as 794 \u00d7 (500 + 30 + 6) = 794\u00d7500 + 794\u00d730 + 794\u00d76.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n794 \u00d7 500 = 794 \u00d7 5 \u00d7 100 = 3970 \u00d7 100 = 397,000\n\n794 \u00d7 30 = 794 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 10 = 2,382 \u00d7 10 = 23,820\n\n794 \u00d7 6 = 4,764 (as before)\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n397,000 + 23,820 = 420,820\n\n420,820 + 4,764 = 425,584\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result of 56,374. Wait, that can't be. There must be a mistake here. Wait, 397,000 + 23,820 is 420,820. Then 420,820 + 4,764 is 425,584. But earlier, when I did the step-by-step multiplication, I got 56,374. That's a discrepancy. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, 794 \u00d7 536. If I use the distributive method, breaking into 500 + 30 + 6, then:\n\n794 \u00d7 500 = 397,000\n\n794 \u00d7 30 = 23,820\n\n794 \u00d7 6 = 4,764\n\nAdding them: 397,000 + 23,820 = 420,820; 420,820 + 4,764 = 425,584.\n\nBut when I did the standard multiplication, I got 56,374. That's way off. So clearly, I made a mistake in the standard multiplication method. Let me check again.\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication, I had:\n\nFirst, 794 \u00d7 6 = 4,764\n\nThen, 794 \u00d7 3 (tens place) = 2,382, shifted left by one, so 47,640\n\nThen, 794 \u00d7 5 (hundreds place) = 3,970, shifted left by two, so 39,700\n\nThen adding 4,764 + 47,640 + 39,700.\n\nWait, but in my initial calculation, I added 4,764 (ones place) + 47,640 (tens place) + 39,700 (hundreds place). But when I added them, I got 56,374. But according to the distributive method, it's 425,584. So which is correct?\n\nWait, 794 \u00d7 536. Let me compute it using another method. Let's use the standard multiplication step-by-step.\n\nLet me write it out properly:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0794\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0536\n--------\nFirst, multiply 794 by 6:\n\n794\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a06\n------\n4,764\n\nThen, multiply 794 by 3 (tens place), which is 2,382, shifted one position left:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a04764\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a03\n------\n14,292\n\nWait, no. Wait, when you multiply by the tens digit, you shift the result one position left. So 794 \u00d7 3 = 2,382. Then, since it's in the tens place, you write 2,382 shifted left by one, which is 4,764.\n\nSimilarly, multiplying 794 by 5 (hundreds place), which is 3,970, shifted two positions left: 39,700.\n\nSo adding 4,764 (ones place) + 47,640 (tens place) + 39,700 (hundreds place):\n\n4,764 + 47,640 = 52,404\n\n52,404 + 39,700 = 92,10