 place):\n\n794\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a03\n------\n2,382\n\nShift this result one position to the left (since it's the tens place):\n\n4,764\n\nThen, multiply 794 by 5 (hundreds place):\n\n794\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a05\n------\n3,970\n\nShift this result two positions to the left (since it's the hundreds place):\n\n39,700\n\nNow, add all three results:\n\n4,764 (ones place)\n+47,640 (tens place)\n+39,700 (hundreds place)\n= 4,764 + 47,640 = 52,404; 52,404 + 39,700 = 92,104\n\nBut according to the distributive method, it's 425,584. There's a conflict here. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the distributive method. Let me check:\n\n794 \u00d7 536 = 794 \u00d7 (500 + 30 + 6) = 794\u00d7500 + 794\u00d730 + 794\u00d76\n\n794\u00d7500 = 397,000\n\n794\u00d730 = 23,820\n\n794\u00d76 = 4,764\n\nAdding them: 397,000 + 23,820 = 420,820; 420,820 + 4,764 = 425,584\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, it's 92,104. That's a huge difference. So clearly, one of the methods is wrong. Let me check with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 794 \u00d7 536 using the standard multiplication algorithm step-by-step.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0794\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0536\n--------\nFirst, write down 794 multiplied by 6:\n\n794\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a06\n------\n4,764\n\nNext, write down 794 multiplied by 3 (tens place), shifted one position left:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a04764\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a03\n------\n14,292\n\nWait, no. Wait, when you multiply by the tens digit (3), you shift the result one position left. So 794 \u00d7 3 = 2,382. Shift left by one: 4,764.\n\nThen, multiply 794 by 5 (hundreds place), shifted two positions left:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a039700\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a05\n------\n197,500\n\nWait, no. Wait, 794 \u00d7 5 = 3,970. Shift two positions left: 39,700.\n\nSo adding:\n\n4,764 (ones place)\n+47,640 (tens place)\n+39,700 (hundreds place)\n= 4,764 + 47,640 = 52,404; 52,404 + 39,700 = 92,104\n\nBut according to the distributive 