\n\n967 \u00d7 921 can be written as 967 \u00d7 (900 + 20 + 1). Let's compute each part:\n\nFirst, 967 \u00d7 900. 967 \u00d7 9 = 8703, so 967 \u00d7 900 = 8703 \u00d7 100 = 870,300.\n\nNext, 967 \u00d7 20. 967 \u00d7 2 = 1934, so 967 \u00d7 20 = 1934 \u00d7 10 = 19,340.\n\nThen, 967 \u00d7 1 = 967.\n\nAdding those together: 870,300 + 19,340 + 967. \n\nFirst, 870,300 + 19,340. Let's add 870,300 + 10,000 = 880,300; then 880,300 + 9,340 = 889,640. Then add 967: 889,640 + 967 = 890,607. \n\nSame result! Okay, that's reassuring. So the product of 967 and 921 is 890,607. \n\nJust to be absolutely sure, maybe I can use another approach. Let's try multiplying 967 by 921 using the standard algorithm again, but more carefully.\n\nMultiplying 967 by 921:\n\nFirst, write 967 \u00d7 921.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n1 (units place) \u00d7 967 = 967. Write down 967.\n\n2 (tens place) \u00d7 967 = 1934. Shift one position left: 19340.\n\n9 (hundreds place) \u00d7 967 = 8703. Shift two positions left: 870300.\n\nNow add them up:\n\n967\n+19340\n+870300\n--------\nLet's add 967 + 19340 first. 967 + 19340. Let's do 19340 + 900 = 20240, then 20240 + 67 = 20307.\n\nThen add 20307 + 870300. Let's break it down: 870300 + 20000 = 890300, then 890300 + 307 = 890607. \n\nSame result again. So, seems like 890,607 is the correct answer. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator here, I can cross-verify with another multiplication method. For example, using the difference of squares or something else. Wait, 967 and 921 are close to 990. Let me see:\n\nBut 967 = 990 - 23\n\n921 = 990 - 69\n\nSo, (990 - 23)(990 - 69) = 990\u00b2 - 990\u00d769 - 23\u00d7990 + 23\u00d769\n\nBut this might complicate. Let me compute each term:\n\n990\u00b2 = 980,100\n\n990\u00d769: 990\u00d770 = 69,300; subtract 990: 69,300 - 990 = 68,310\n\n23\u00d7990: 23\u00d71000 = 23,000; subtract 23\u00d710 = 230: 23,000 - 230 = 22,770\n\n23\u00d769: 20\u00d769 = 1,380; 3\u00d769 = 207; total 1,380 + 207 = 1,587\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\n980,100 - 68,310 - 22,770 + 1,587\n\nFirst, 980,100 - 68,310 = 911,790\n\nThen, 911,790 - 22,770 = 889,020\n\nThen, 889,020 + 1,587 = 890,607\n\nSame result! Wow, that's three different methods all leading to 890,607. So I must be correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 967 and 921 is 890,607.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 967 and 921 is \\boxed{890607}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 967 and 921, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 967 by the rightmost digit (1):\n   \\[\n   967 \\times 1 = 967\n   \\]\n   Shift one position to the left: 9670\n\n2. Multiply 967 by the middle digit (2):\n   \\[\n   967 \\times 2 = 1934\n   \\]\n   Shift one position to the left: 19340\n\n3. Multiply 967 by the leftmost digit (9):\n   \\[\n   967 \\times 9 = 8703\n   \\]\n   Shift two positions to the left: 870300\n\n4. Add the results together:\n   \\[\n   967 + 19340 + 870300\n   \\]\n\n   First, add 967 and 19340:\n   \\[\n   967 + 19340 = 20307\n   \\]\n\n   Then, add 20307 and 870300:\n   \\[\n   20307 + 870300 = 890607\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this result using another method by breaking down the multiplication:\n- \\(967 \\times 921 = 967 \\times (900 + 20 + 1)\\)\n- Calculate each part:\n  - \\(967 \\times 900 = 870300\\)\n  - \\(967 \\times 20 = 19340\\)\n  - \\(967 \\times 1 = 967\\)\n- Add the results:\n  \\[\n  870300 + 19340 + 967 = 890607\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 967 and 921 is \\(\\boxed{890607}\\).",
