ding this would involve more terms, but let's try:\n\nFirst, multiply 200 \u00d7 400 = 80,000\n\n200 \u00d7 30 = 6,000\n\n200 \u00d7 3 = 600\n\n60 \u00d7 400 = 24,000\n\n60 \u00d7 30 = 1,800\n\n60 \u00d7 3 = 180\n\n8 \u00d7 400 = 3,200\n\n8 \u00d7 30 = 240\n\n8 \u00d7 3 = 24\n\nNow, add all these together:\n\n80,000 + 6,000 + 600 + 24,000 + 1,800 + 180 + 3,200 + 240 + 24\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\nStart with 80,000 + 6,000 = 86,000\n\n86,000 + 600 = 86,600\n\n86,600 + 24,000 = 110,600\n\n110,600 + 1,800 = 112,400\n\n112,400 + 180 = 112,580\n\n112,580 + 3,200 = 115,780\n\n115,780 + 240 = 116,020\n\n116,020 + 24 = 116,044\n\nSame result! So, even when expanding all the terms, the total is 116,044. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 268 and 433 is indeed 116,044.\n\nJust to recap, the steps are:\n\n1. Multiply 268 by each digit of 433, starting from the rightmost digit (3), then moving to the next (30), then the next (400).\n\n2. Break down each multiplication into parts:\n\n   - 268 \u00d7 3 = 804\n\n   - 268 \u00d7 30 = 8,040\n\n   - 268 \u00d7 400 = 107,200\n\n3. Add the three results together:\n\n   - 804 + 8,040 = 8,844\n\n   - 8,844 + 107,200 = 116,044\n\nAll methods confirm that the product is 116,044. Therefore, the answer should be 116,044.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 268 and 433 is \\boxed{116044}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 268 and 433, we can break down the multiplication into parts and then add the results together. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Multiply 268 by the rightmost digit (3):\n   \\[\n   268 \\times 3 = 804\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 268 by the next digit (30):\n   \\[\n   268 \\times 30 = 8040\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 268 by the next digit (400):\n   \\[\n   268 \\times 400 = 107200\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   804 + 8040 + 107200\n   \\]\n\n5. First, add 804 and 8040:\n   \\[\n   804 + 8040 = 8844\n   \\]\n\n6. Then, add the result to 107200:\n   \\[\n   8844 + 10