      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 372 and 838. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two-digit numbers can be done step by step, breaking it down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm here. Let me recall how that works.\n\nFirst, I think I should write 372 multiplied by 838. Let me set it up like this:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0372\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0838\n--------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit of the second number, which is 8. I need to multiply 372 by 8 first. Let me do that:\n\n8 \u00d7 2 = 16. So I write down 6 and carry over 1.\n8 \u00d7 7 = 56, plus the carried 1 makes 57. Write down 7 and carry over 5.\n8 \u00d7 3 = 24, plus the carried 5 makes 29. Write down 9 and carry over 2.\n8 \u00d7 0 = 0, plus the carried 2 is 2. So the result is 2976.\n\nWait, no, hold on. Wait, 372 \u00d7 8. Let me check that again. 2\u00d78=16, yes. Then 7\u00d78=56, plus 1 is 57. Then 3\u00d78=24, plus 5 is 29. Then 0\u00d78=0, plus 2 is 2. So yes, 2976. Okay, that seems right.\n\nNow, the next step is to multiply 372 by the next digit in 838, which is 3. But since it's the tens place, I need to shift the result one position to the left. So 2976 becomes 29760.\n\nThen, the next digit is 8, which is the hundreds place. Again, shift the previous result two positions to the left. So 29760 becomes 2976000.\n\nWait, no. Wait, actually, when multiplying by each digit, starting from the right, each subsequent digit is multiplied and shifted left by one. So the first digit (rightmost) is 8, then 3 (tens place), then 8 (hundreds place). So after multiplying 372 by 8, we get 2976. Then multiply by 3 (tens place), which is 2976 \u00d7 3. Then shift left by one, so 29760. Then multiply by 8 (hundreds place), shift left by two, so 2976000. Then add all three results together: 2976 + 29760 + 2976000.\n\nWait, that seems like a lot. Let me verify. Alternatively, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can break down 838 into 800 + 30 + 8. Then multiply each part by 372 and add them up.\n\nLet me try that. So 372 \u00d7 800. Hmm, 372 \u00d7 8 is 2976, so 2976 \u00d7 100 = 297600.\n\nThen 372 \u00d7 30. 372 \u00d7 3 = 1116, so 1116 \u00d7 10 = 11160.\n\nThen 372 \u00d7 8. As before, that's 2976.\n\nNow add them all together: 297600 + 11160 + 2976.\n\nLet me compute that step by step.\n\nFirst, 297600 + 11160. Let's add 297600 + 10000 = 307600, then subtract 10000 - 11160? Wait, no. Wait, 297600 + 11160. Let's break it down:\n\n297600 + 10000 = 307600\n\n307600 + 1000 = 308600\n\n308600 + 116 = 308716\n\nWait, 11160 is 10000 + 1000 + 160. So adding 10000 to 297600 gives 307600, then add 1000 to get 308600, then add 160 to get 308716. So 297600 + 11160 = 308716.\n\nThen add 2976 to that. So 308716 + 2976.\n\nLet me compute that. 308716 + 2000 = 310716\n\n310716 + 976 = 311,692? Wait, 310716 + 900 = 310,616\n\n310,616 + 76 = 310,692\n\nWait, that can't be right. Wait, 308716 + 2976.\n\nLet me do it another way. 308716 + 2000 = 310716\n\n310716 + 900 = 310,616\n\n310,616 + 76 = 310,692\n\nYes, so total is 310,692.\n\nWait, so the product of 372 and 838 is 310,692?\n\nWait, let me check with another method to verify.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm properly.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u00a0372\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0838\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 372 by 8:\n\n8 \u00d7 2 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n8 \u00d7 7 = 56 + 1 = 57 \u2192 7, carry 5\n\n8 \u00d7 3 = 24 + 5 = 29 \u2192 9, carry 2\n\n8 \u00d7 0 = 0 + 2 = 2 \u2192 2\n\nSo result is 2976.\n\nNext, multiply 372 by 3 (tens place, shifted one position left):\n\n3 \u00d7 2 = 6 \u2192 6\n\n3 \u00d7 7 = 21 \u2192 1, carry 2\n\n3 \u00d7 3 = 9 + 2 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 \u00d7 0 = 0 + 1 = 1 \u2192 1\n\nSo result is 29760.\n\nNext, multiply 372 by 8 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):\n\n8 \u00d7 2 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n8 \u00d7 7 = 56 + 1 = 57 \u2192 7, carry 5\n\n8 \u00d7 3 = 24 + 5 = 29 \u2192 9, carry 2\n\n8 \u00d7 0 = 0 + 2 = 2 \u2192 2\n\nSo result is 297600.\n\nNow, add all three results:\n\n2976\n\n+29760\n\n+297600\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 2976 + 29760.\n\n2976 + 29760 = 32736\n\nThen, add 297600 to 32736.\n\n32736 + 297600 = 330,336\n\nWait, that's different from the previous total of 310,692. Hmm, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. There must be a mistake here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, when I did the breakdown into 800 + 30 + 8, then multiplied each part:\n\n372 \u00d7 800 = 297600\n\n372 \u00d7 30 = 11160\n\n372 \u00d7 8 = 2976\n\nAdding those gives 297600 + 11160 + 2976 = 310,692.\n\nBut when I did the standard multiplication, adding 2976 + 29760 + 297600 = 330,336.\n\nThese two results are different. So there's a mistake here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check the standard multiplication again.\n\nFirst step: 372 \u00d7 8 = 2976\n\nSecond step: 372 \u00d7 30. 372 \u00d7 3 = 1116, then \u00d710 is 11160\n\nThird step: 372 \u00d7 800. 372 \u00d7 8 = 2976, \u00d7100 is 297600\n\nSo adding 2976 + 11160 + 297600.\n\nWait, 2976 + 11160 = 14,136\n\n14,136 + 297,600 = 311,736\n\nWait, that's different from 310,692. Wait, so now I'm getting 311,736. Hmm, so which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check 372 \u00d7 800. 372 \u00d7 800 is 372 \u00d7 8 \u00d7 100 = 2976 \u00d7 100 = 297,600. That's correct.\n\n372 \u00d7 30 is 372 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 10 = 1,116 \u00d7 10 = 11,160. Correct.\n\n372 \u00d7 8 is 2,976. Correct.\n\nSo adding 297,600 + 11,160 + 2,976.\n\n297,600 + 11,160 = 308,760\n\n308,760 + 2,976 = 311,736\n\nSo the correct total is 311,736. But earlier, when I did the standard multiplication, I added 2976 + 29760 + 297600 as 330,336. That's wrong. So where did I go wrong in the standard multiplication?\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication, when you shift the digits, the second step (372 \u00d7 3) is shifted left by one, so 2976 becomes 29760. The third step (372 \u00d7 8) is shifted left by two, so 2976 becomes 297600. Then adding 2976 + 29760 + 297600.\n\nBut 2976 + 29760 is 32736, then 32736 + 297600 is 330,336. But that contradicts the other method. So which is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps the standard multiplication is wrong. Let me check the standard multiplication again.\n\nFirst, 372 \u00d7 8:\n\n8 \u00d7 2 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n8 \u00d7 7 = 56 + 1 = 57 \u2192 7, carry 5\n\n8 \u00d7 3 = 24 + 5 = 29 \u2192 9, carry 2\n\n8 \u00d7 0 = 0 + 2 = 2 \u2192 2\n\nSo 2976. Correct.\n\nThen, 372 \u00d7 3 (tens place):\n\n3 \u00d7 2 = 6 \u2192 6\n\n3 \u00d7 7 = 21 \u2192 1, carry 2\n\n3 \u00d7 3 = 9 + 2 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 \u00d7 0 = 0 + 1 = 1 \u2192 1\n\nSo 29760. Correct.\n\nThen, 372 \u00d7 8 (hundreds place):\n\n8 \u00d7 2 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n8 \u00d7 7 = 56 + 1 = 57 \u2192 7, carry 5\n\n8 \u00d7 3 = 24 + 5 = 29 \u2192 9, carry 2\n\n8 \u00d7 0 = 0 + 2 = 2 \u2192 2\n\nSo 297600. Correct.\n\nSo adding 2976 + 29760 + 297600.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 2976 + 29760.\n\n2976 + 29760:\n\n2976 + 29760 = 29760 + 2000 + 976 = 31760 + 976 = 32736\n\nThen, 32736 + 297600:\n\n32736 + 297600 = 330,336\n\nBut according to the breakdown, it should be 311,736. So there's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check 372 \u00d7 800 again. 372 \u00d7 800 is 372 \u00d7 8 \u00d7 100 = 2976 \u00d7 100 = 297,600. Correct.\n\n372 \u00d7 30 is 372 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 10 = 1,116 \u00d7 10 = 11,160. Correct.\n\n372 \u00d7 8 is 2,976. Correct.\n\nSo 297,600 + 11,160 + 2,976 = 297,600 + 11,160 = 308,760; 308,760 + 2,976 = 311,736.\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, it's 330,336. So which is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps the standard multiplication is wrong. Let me check the standard multiplication again.\n\nWait, when you do 372 \u00d7 838, the standard multiplication steps:\n\nFirst, multiply 372