rite 655\nMultiply by 305\nSo, 655\nx305\n--------\nFirst, multiply 655 by 5: 3275\nThen multiply 655 by 0: 0\nThen multiply 655 by 3: 1965\nAdd them up: 3275 + 0 + 1965 = 5240\n\nSame result. Okay, that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property. Let's see. 305 can be written as 300 + 5. So 655*(300 +5) = 655*300 + 655*5. Let's compute each part.\n\n655*300. Well, 655*3 is 1965, so 655*300 is 19650. Then 655*5 is 3275, as before. Then add 19650 + 3275. Let's do that. 19650 + 3000 = 22650, then 22650 + 275 = 22925. Wait, that's different. Wait, hold on. Wait, 655*300 is 655*3*100 = 1965*100 = 19650. Then 655*5 is 3275. So 19650 + 3275. Let's compute that. 19650 + 3000 = 22650, then 22650 + 275 = 22925. But earlier, when I did 3275 + 1965, I got 5240. Wait, that's conflicting. Wait, no, hold on. Wait, 655*300 is 19650, and 655*5 is 3275. So 19650 + 3275 = 22925. But earlier, when I did 3275 + 1965, I got 5240. Wait, that can't be. Wait, no, 3275 + 1965 is 5240, but 19650 + 3275 is 22925. Wait, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. Wait, so if I use the distributive property, 655*305 = 655*(300 +5) = 655*300 + 655*5 = 19650 + 3275 = 22925. But when I did the standard multiplication, I got 5240. That's a problem. There must be a mistake here. Wait, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check 655*305. Let's compute 655*305 using another method. Let's do 655*300 + 655*5. 655*300 is 19650, 655*5 is 3275. 19650 + 3275. Let's compute that again. 19650 + 3275. Let's break it down:\n\n19650 + 3000 = 22650\n\n22650 + 275 = 22925\n\nSo that's 22925. But when I did the standard multiplication, I got 5240. That's a discrepancy. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check again.\n\nStandard multiplication:\n\nMultiply 655 by 305.\n\nFirst, write 655\n\nMultiply by 305\n\nSo:\n\n655\n\nx305\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 655 by 5: 3275\n\nThen multiply 655 by 0: 0\n\nThen multiply 655 by 3: 1965\n\nAdd them up: 3275 + 0 + 1965 = 5240\n\nBut according to the distributive method, it's 22925. So which is correct?\n\nWait, this is a problem. There's a mistake here. Let me check 655*305.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 655*305 using another approach. Let's try using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 655 by 305:\n\nStart with the rightmost digit: 5\n\n655\n\nx305\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 655 by 5: 3275\n\nNext, multiply 655 by 0: 0\n\nNext, multiply 655 by 3: 1965\n\nNow, add them:\n\n3275\n\n+\u00a0\u00a00\n\n+1965\n\n= 3275 + 1965\n\nLet's compute 3275 + 1965:\n\n3275 + 1965:\n\nAdd thousands: 3000 + 1000 = 4000\n\nAdd hundreds: 200 + 900 = 1100\n\nAdd tens: 70 + 60 = 130\n\nAdd units: 5 +5 =10\n\nTotal: 4000 + 1100 = 5100; 5100 +130 = 5230; 5230 +10 = 5240\n\nSo that's 5240. But according to the distributive method, it's 22925. So clearly, there's a mistake here. Wait, but how?\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, 655*305. Let me compute 655*305 using another method. Let's use the fact that 305 is 300 +5, so 655*300 +655*5. 655*300 is 19650, 655*5 is 3275. 19650 +3275. Let's compute that again. 19650 + 3275.\n\n19650 + 3000 = 22650\n\n22650 + 275 = 22925\n\nBut 22925 vs 5240. These are different. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the distributive approach. Wait, 305 is 300 +5, so 655*300 +655*5. 655*300 is 655*3*100. 655*3 is 1965, so 1965*100=19650. Then 655*5=3275. So 19650 +3275=22925. But when I did the standard multiplication, I got 5240. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with another method. Let's compute 655*305 using the standard multiplication step by step.\n\nMultiplying 655 by 305:\n\nFirst, write 655\n\nMultiply by 305:\n\nStart with 5 (units place):\n\n655\n\nx\u00a0\u00a05\n\n------\n\n3275\n\nThen, multiply by 0 (tens place):\n\n655\n\nx\u00a0\u00a00\n\n------\n\n0\n\nThen, multiply by 3 (hundreds place):\n\n655\n\nx\u00a0\u00a03\n\n------\n\n1965\n\nNow, add them:\n\n3275\n\n+\