 100 = 617,400. That seems right.\n\nThen 686 x 24: 686 x 20 = 13,720 and 686 x 4 = 2,744. 13,720 + 2,744. Let's add those again:\n\n13,720 + 2,744. 13,720 + 2,000 = 15,720. Then 15,720 + 744 = 16,464. That's correct.\n\nSo 617,400 + 16,464. Let's add them properly:\n\n617,400\n+ 16,464\n= 617,400 + 16,464\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\n0 + 6 = 6\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\n7 + 1 = 8\n\n1 + 0 = 1\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\nWait, maybe I need to align them properly:\n\n  617,400\n+  16,464\n----------\nStart adding:\n\nUnits place: 0 + 4 = 4\n\nTens: 0 + 6 = 6\n\nHundreds: 4 + 4 = 8\n\nThousands: 7 + 1 = 8\n\nTen-thousands: 1 + 0 = 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 + 0 = 6\n\nSo that gives 633,864. But earlier, the standard multiplication gave 304,584. These two results are different. That means I must have made a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let's check the standard multiplication again. Maybe I messed up the partial products.\n\nOriginal problem: 686 x 924.\n\nFirst partial product: 686 x 4 = 2,744\n\nSecond partial product: 686 x 2 (tens place) = 1,372, shifted one position left: 13,720\n\nThird partial product: 686 x 9 (hundreds place) = 6,174, shifted two positions left: 617,400\n\nThen adding them: 2,744 + 13,720 + 617,400.\n\nWait, hold on. In the standard multiplication, when you multiply by the units digit (4), you get 2,744. Then multiplying by the tens digit (2) gives 1,372, but since it's the tens place, you shift it one position left, making it 13,720. Then multiplying by the hundreds digit (9) gives 6,174, shifted two positions left, making it 617,400. Then adding those three: 2,744 + 13,720 + 617,400.\n\nLet me compute that again:\n\n2,744 + 13,720 = 16,464\n\n16,464 + 617,400 = 633,864\n\nSo that's 633,864. But when I did the distributive method, I also got 633,864. So both methods give the same result. Wait, but earlier I thought the standard multiplication gave 304,584. Wait, no, that was a mistake. Wait, no, let me check again.\n\nWait, in the first metho